{"type":"message","id":"c975f897","parentId":"f29137ac","timestamp":"2026-10-15T23:10:53.167Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Evaluating GitHub API Queries**\n\nI need to clarify the differences between actual GitHub GraphQL fields like `baseRef.target.oid` and others. It looks like there's confusion regarding the `baseRefOid` semantics, especially with stale PR snapshots. I should query the official GitHub documentation to understand `baseRefOid` better. The introspection query to get field descriptions seems particularly valuable. I’m contemplating whether I need dynamic documentation or if the static page will suffice for my needs regarding API reconciliation.","thinkingSignature":"{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"rs_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad15d62d8688191887fc1669403cf4c\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Evaluating GitHub API Queries**\\n\\nI need to clarify the differences between actual GitHub GraphQL fields like `baseRef.target.oid` and others. It looks like there's confusion regarding the `baseRefOid` semantics, especially with stale PR snapshots. I should query the official GitHub documentation to understand `baseRefOid` better. The introspection query to get field descriptions seems particularly valuable. I’m contemplating whether I need dynamic documentation or if the static page will suffice for my needs regarding API reconciliation.\"}],\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABq0V1u2T7QzzVqxaCc1gxeUKclcBZQ-3qYQWjJ5g9yS6d57798JTWz5PEFkf7bAzwsOkAUO0CumFN7X6BgriKA41VtfiK3zcmaIyoKNGjXKAAHLi0qVUB4RPGWlf5wqcE65ioUtdX9DTvXk3f1rgscmkgVOMs4DUKr83ng2Hd9OLVYXlAr3hVhLnZSXba-ivMUjmi-qQNKTzusKz3TmnFQ9IkSNRkCsdFHSgfDM-HH3CgqvcG795bojbJgQx0AthZmS3c2Y88FtdyfDbh7OjReFieurfrSi50uYcbFagU4d2as1tv5Fjh394RGPx6VTgoD7-PalCsUgb37BVAnu4CarXxqjUogN_wiSM3qK9LxzCUkYK6iRvra4H3gWAUVhP8c4i6ZNhrPqencEKHLT1K89YxNqFLMwMGolbQe24BxafnycnlT7oPJI9dasDh3bpP0_AQOBwVn-9mppThhV5sXdBOMLOmZcVowiZph-OEtk6JdCt3tRyNuqIqZ3q3pESChBfW8hzIXB4