                     │\n                                                                                                                                                                                                          │\n Thinking...                                                                                                                                                                                              │\n                                                                                                                                                                                                          │\n✓ bash git status --short --branch; git rev-parse HEAD                                                                                                                                                    │\n                                                                                                                                                                                                          │\n Thinking...                                                                                                                                                                                              │\n                                                                                                                                                                                                          │\n Diagnosis: The failure was in fixture setup, not an observed application assertion. TestBrainBriefGitIntentLiveShapedOperationalRecall failed at brain_brief_git_intent_test.go:44 when a fixture’s git  │\n commit --allow-empty exited 128 with fatal: could not parse HEAD, before its subtests ran.\n\n Confidence is high in that immediate cause, but the underlying Git/ref/object condition is unknown. Go 1.27.2 setup, cache restore, build, and the cgo suite had proceeded; setup-go v7 causation is not\n established. A single focused macOS/arm64 race+CGO reproduction passed, but differences in Git build, filesystem, hardware, and cache mean this does not prove a flake.\n\n At the observed snapshot, 17 of 18 required checks passed, one failed, none were pending; Windows had completed successfully. No job rerun or code changes were made. The exact missing evidence is the\n fixture’s HEAD/ref/object state and sanitized Git environment at the failing exit. If a fix is needed, the bounded follow-up is diagnostic-only fixture reporting, on a new assigned issue/branch—not a\n speculative production change or weakened test.\n\n The checkout is clean at c11be1e; the investigation released the heavy slot. The current main failure still needs parent-owned resolution. Security remains a separate unresolved concern. Trail 271 is\n merged per the parent’s direct observation.\n\n\n POST-MERGE SUCCESS verified by parent on SAME8724085d27b91fd02353f3a4c275709bb21476b1/main. Parent performed exactly ONE job-only debug diagnostic repeat (correct jobdatabaseId116734834928, no\n codechange); new MacCGO check116742130239 passed, workflow38826422358 attempt2completedSUCCESS. Parent independently re-fetched both classicprotection/rules inventories, all18 required\n checkcontexts/AppIDs/actualcheckIDs/URLs/mainworkflowrun identities successful. Current defaulthead also872. Verified receipt\n /Users/alex/.local/state/herdr/orchestrations/dependency-followups-20261015/postmerge-356/success-receipt.json. Original failure/cause still unresolved: CI recovery is not a code fix. Preserved failure\n receipt, owner diagnosis and run/check observations in same directory. Followup COR-2144 created Backlog/Bug for sanitized fixture diagnostics; NO implementation authorized in this cleanup wave.\n You are now authorized final REPOSITORY CLEANUP ONLY in ownedwQ6. No worktree removal or Linear mutation. Reconcile only owned completed/paused worker/test resources, stop any actual owned residual\n execution, preserve original failure/diagnosti