2084000…\n\n Thinking...\n\n Evidence-backed outcome\n\n Both current-head benchmark logs show the same two fixture-coupling failures, not just the same job name:\n\n - Tar update — Trail 269, head cef529417a55efd4fd7e5cfce2c7279551224176, open. Its benchmark job reports:\n     1. test_preparation_artifacts_are_consistent: actual validation adds engine runtime pin package_lock hash is stale, absent from the exact expected list.\n     2. test_public_bundle_validates_and_is_protocol_checker_authoritative_v4: expected [], got that same stale-lock diagnostic.\n\n   Evidence: workflow run 38661768213, benchmark job 116184451316; the log’s merge checkout contains the stated head.\n\n - npm group update — Trail 272, head 4e8bdd8d50c5b36b37bf05a3cb3b98493fa150d6, open. Its benchmark job reports those same assertion failures and exact diagnostics.\n\n   Evidence: workflow run 38661788110, benchmark job 116184517856; its merge checkout also contains the stated head. This update changes scripts/bench/package-lock.json and web UI files; the failures\n   concern the benchmark lock, not the web UI delta.\n\n Both runs have no pending checks; parent reports formal findings zero and current Main review passed.\n\n Dependency map\n\n Current main c13e8d1c… does not contain an equivalent fixture fix. Immutable-object comparison shows the old expected assertion and production-root pin_repo remain on main; Nfix 38c5cf65… contains the\n two test changes. The production checker, pin file, and public-evidence implementation have identical Git blob IDs on main and Nfix. The earlier Nfix commit c7da4201… is an ancestor of 38c5cf65….\n\n Therefore, syncing either update to current main alone is insufficient. Both need the shared Nfix fixture-compatibility change in their base (or that same test-only change applied equivalently); no\n separate Tar-specific or npm-group-specific compatibility change is evidenced. The existing CI runs used merge base 2a05be9d…, so checks after syncing with current main still need verification.\n\n No refs, branches, source, or Git index were changed; no tests or dependency code were run. Brain CLI was unavailable (entire brain was unrecognized); Graph capability checks succeeded, and\n cross-commit conclusions above come from read-only Git objects and the exact CI logs.\n\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nTrails: entireio/entire-brain#268\n~/.herdr/worktrees/entire-brain/alex-nanoid-fixture-compat (dependabot/npm_and_yarn/scripts/bench/nanoid-5.1.16)\n↑957k ↓88k R30M CH98.5% $0.491 (sub) 32.9%/1.1M (auto)                                                                                                                   (openai-codex) gpt-6-luna • medium\ncompact @ 75% 🔌 MCP: 5 servers enabled\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":651,"timestamp":1792112590891}}
