{"type":"message","id":"e1e65b83","parentId":"3f7b22fe","timestamp":"2026-10-16T02:46:56.320Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_63693a1e7c1a4fc8950be47f0243e36b|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad1901fa21c8191ac2d93da945a0e99","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Executable agents (capabilities):\nUser agents\n- review-steward (user, context: fresh): Description: Owns one bounded review-feedback wave for exactly one open PR—fetching GitHub review threads, Trail findings, CI failures, and Trail monitor receipts; triaging, batch-fixing, verifying, pushing, resolving, and reporting direct-fetch coun...; Tools: read, write, edit, bash, grep, find, ls; Model: openai-codex/gpt-6.1-sol; Thinking: high; Acceptance: checked; Acceptance role: writer\n\nBuiltin agents\n- claude-code (builtin, external-cli:claude ✓): Description: Read-only Claude Code CLI analysis; requires local authentication and trusted user settings/hooks; Tools: default/ambient; Model: openai-codex/gpt-6-luna; Thinking: medium\n- claude-code-writer (builtin, external-cli:claude ✓): Description: Explicit file-writing Claude Code CLI mode; requires local authentication and trusted user settings/hooks; Tools: default/ambient; Model: openai-codex/gpt-6-luna; Thinking: medium; Acceptance role: writer\n- codex-exec (builtin, external-cli:codex ✓): Description: Read-only one-shot analysis through the installed Codex CLI; Tools: default/ambient; Model: openai-codex/gpt-6-luna; Thinking: medium\n- codex-exec-writer (builtin, external-cli:codex ✓): Description: Explicit workspace-writing one-shot execution through the installed Codex CLI; Tools: default/ambient; Model: openai-codex/gpt-6-luna; Thinking: medium; Acceptance role: writer\n- cursor-agent (builtin, external-cli:cursor-agent ✓): Description: Read-only one-shot analysis through the installed Cursor CLI; Tools: default/ambient; Model: openai-codex/gpt-6-luna; Thinking: medium\n- cursor-agent-writer (builtin, external-cli:cursor-agent ✓): Description: Explicit workspace-writing one-shot execution through the installed Cursor CLI; Tools: default/ambient; Model: openai-codex/gpt-6-luna; Thinking: medium; Acceptance role: writer\n- delegate (builtin): Description: Lightweight subagent that inherits the parent model with no default reads; Tools: read, grep, find, ls, bash, edit, write, contact_supervisor; Model: openai-codex/gpt-6-luna; Thinking: medium\n- evidence-auditor (builtin): Description: Independent evidence reviewer for checking whether important research claims are supported by their sources; Tools: read, web_search, fetch_content, get_search_content, source_check; Model: openai-codex/gpt-6-luna; Thinking: high\n- oracle (builtin, context: fork, aliases: advisor): Description: High-context decision-consistency oracle that protects inherited state and prevents drift; Tools: read, grep, find, ls, bash; Model: openai-codex/gpt-6.1-sol; Thinking: high\n- reviewer (builtin): Description: Versatile review specialist for code diffs, plans, proposed solutions, codebase health, and PR/issue validation; Tools: read, grep, find, ls, watchdog_diff, contact_supervisor; Model: openai-codex/gpt-6-luna; Thinking: high\n- scout (builtin): Description: Fast codebase recon that returns compressed context for handoff; Tools: read, grep, find, ls, bash, write, contact_supervisor; Model: openai-codex/gpt-6-luna; Thinking: low\n- worker (builtin, context: fresh, aliases: developer, coder, implementer, develop): Description: Implementation agent for normal tasks and approved oracle handoffs; Tools: read, grep, find, ls, bash, edit, write, contact_supervisor; Model: openai-codex/gpt-6.1-sol; Thinking: high; Acceptance role: writer\n\nProactive skill subagent suggestions:\n- entire-graph via reviewer (referenced by 4 configured agents/chains; agent:delegate, agent:reviewer, agent:scout, +1 more) - Use FIRST to locate code for any task in a git repo — \"where do I fix X\", \"who calls X\", \"what breaks if I change this\", blast radius, what a type/interface is and who implements it, entity-level review of a commit/branch/checkpoint. Runs the local `entire graph` code graph (deterministic, no network, no LLM) instead of broad grep-and-read. Not for lexical find of a known literal string (use peregrine/grep) or for reading patch text (use git).\nGuardrails: use these for broad tasks where a skill-specialist pass is useful; keep fanout small, use fresh context unless private/session context is explicitly needed, and skip when the user asks for a direct answer."}],"details":{"mode":"management","results":[],"agentCapabilities":{"agents":[{"name":"claude-code","description":"Read-only Claude Code CLI analysis; requires local authentication and trusted user settings/hooks","source":"builtin","executable":true,"runner":{"type":"external-cli","adapter":"claude-code","command":"claude","available":true,"capabilities":{"stop":true,"steer":false,"resume":false,"structuredOutput":false,"toolEvents":false,"supervisor":"unsupported","forkContext":false,"extensionBindings":false}},"tools":{"ambient":true,"names":[],"mcpDirectTools":[]},"model":{"value":"openai-codex/gpt-6-luna","thinking":"medium"},"execution":{"defaultAsync":true}},{"name":"claude-code-writer","description":"Explicit file-writing Claude Code CLI mode; requires local authentication and trusted user settings/hooks","source":"builtin","executable":true,"runner":{"type":"external-cli","adapter":"claude-code-writer","command":"claude","available":true,"capabilities":{"stop":true,"steer":false,"resume":false,"structuredOutput":false,"toolEvents":false,"supervisor":"unsupported","forkContext":false,"extensionBindings":false}},"tools":{"ambient":true,"names":[],"mcpDirectTools":[]},"model":{"value":"openai-codex/gpt-6-luna","thinking":"medium"},"execution":{"defaultAsync":true},"acceptance":{"role":"writer"}},{"name":"codex-exec","description":"Read-only one-shot analysis through the installed Codex CLI","source":"builtin","exec