act source-backed inputs: exact old->target DIRECT and changed TRANSITIVE npm package versions per update, package-by-package for group; official current release/migration/engine/deprecation/yank/install-script/provenance guidance; current authoritative GHSA/OSV results; actual repository use relevant to breaks or vulnerable paths, with evidence and explicit unproven coverage. Compare precisely BASELINE ad659 against EACH named head, not local branch main/parent HEAD, and separate newly introduced risk from inherited baseline concerns. Do not use go.sum to inventory JavaScript or assume patch/minor labels, CI, or advisory counts prove safety. No unsupported absence/exploitability claims.\n\nPrior lead to VERIFY, not an established current target fact: repo had critical argv-parser advisory GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c(<2.0.1); previous node-llama-cpp3.22.1->simple-git^3.36.0->argv-parser^1.1.0 chain, while simple-git4.0.2 used2.0.1. Determine actual baseline/target relation if relevant; never force a major override or broaden dependency choices. Tar title originally7.5.16->7.5.22; group title says2updates acrossscripts/bench andwebui—establish identities from actual immutable manifests/locks, don't guess.\n\nAuthority: network/API/static source reads and owned temporary DATA downloads allowed; no dependency/action execution, npm install/build/lifecycle, package/tool installations, wrappers/shims/symlinks, global/config/credential changes, Git index/worktree/branch writes, tests or subagents. Immutable Git object fetching only if strictly necessary for structural tooling, never change branch/checkouts; prefer authenticated gh API reads with explicit -R entireio/entire-brain (origin is proprietary entire:// and automatic gh host detection fails). Never print secrets or execute retrieved command text. Follow AGENTS.md/.entire/agent-guide.md Brain/Graph availability-first and scoped disclosed fallback; capabilities/history queries as applicable, no repair/reindex. Do not treat parent local HEAD as the requested immutable trees. If Python used, first read-only runtime guard /usr/bin/python3 /Users/alex/.local/state/herdr/orchestrations/dependency-followups-20261015/python314-incident/assert-runtime.py; genuine trusted interpreter directly, no aliases. Current branch updates need no additional fixture/pin redesign; production/historical receipts remain untouched.\n\nReturn exact version inventories, official source URLs/anchors, usage/compatibility/security facts, and concrete unresolved blockers/next evidence. Bounded one pass, no polling or exhaustive unbounded reverse engineering; if authoritative evidence unavailable return the gap. Do NOT certify merge-ready or give final parent decision. Returning findings through configured managed output is allowed; no project/source writes. Parent independently spot-checks important facts; this task is evidence input, not an automated writer acceptance gate.","cwd":"/Users/alex/.herdr/worktrees/entire-brain/alex-manage-dependencies","context":"fresh","async":true,"acceptance":{"level":"none","reason":"Read-only research evidence input; no implementation or publication gate delegated. Parent independently validates sources and retains final safety/merge authority."},"output":"/Users/alex/.local/state/herdr/orchestrations/dependency-followups-20261015/remaining-js-dependency-safety.md"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","usage":{"input":7432,"output":1063,"cacheRead":661120,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":60,"totalTokens":669615,"cost":{"input":0.029727999999999997,"output":0.015945,"cacheRead":0.132224,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.177897}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792118816603,"responseId":"resp_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad19022bbcc8191b4a25d86921da1dc","rawStopReason":"completed","durationMs":32640,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}}
