{"type":"custom_message","customType":"subagent-notify","content":"Background task completed: **delegate**\n\ndelegate:\n# Remaining JavaScript dependency updates — bounded evidence input\n\n## Result / critical evidence gap\n\nI could not establish the requested exact package inventories or security/compatibility findings. This runtime's Git object database has the baseline `ad65996bee631e3044773407df48edc1e85e0c17`, but not either supplied PR head (`git cat-file -e` failed for `bfbb527633840fbd1e76f395810adb1e36eeffb3` and `9a3f538b386ad22dca0f9d7f896f4f9e9c9234f5`). Authenticated GitHub REST access also failed: `gh api repos/entireio/entire-brain/contents/package.json?ref=ad65996...` returned 404. The local `main` resolves to `2a05be9d9a1662882be0ac3b2a070455734e2551`, which is explicitly not the requested baseline nor either target and was not used as a substitute. Therefore no exact old→new inventory, changed transitive inventory, package source/usage comparison, or current advisory verdict can be responsibly reported.\n\n## Verified local facts\n\n- Baseline commit exists locally and is the merge of PR #353, with commit message identifying a `scripts/bench/nanoid` update from 5.1.11 to 5.1.16. Its stat shows only `scripts/bench/package-lock.json` changed among dependency artifacts (three lockfile lines changed); this describes the baseline commit, not the remaining PRs.\n- Local package manifests/locks exist at `scripts/bench/package.json`, `scripts/bench/package-lock.json`, `webui/package.json`, and `webui/package-lock.json`, but inspecting local copies cannot prove their contents at the named target commits.\n- The requested heads are unavailable as local immutable Git objects. No checkout/fetch was attempted. No package manager, tests, install, build, or lifecycle scripts were run.\n- Brain preflight: the installed `entire` CLI reported `unknown command \"brain\"` for version/capabilities/brief; Brain unavailable. Graph preflight identified provider `entire-graph`, v`0.4.1-nightly.202609240616.f22e6c95`, with JavaScript/TypeScript semantic coverage and relationship features. Dependency manifests are inventory/text concerns; no graph query can substitute for reading the two immutable lockfile trees.\n\n## Advisory/release research not established\n\nNo authoritative current GHSA/OSV result or package-specific official release/migration/engine/deprecation/yank/install-script/provenance guidance was obtained. In particular, the supplied argv-parser lead (`GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c`, alleged affected range below 2.0.1) remains unverified against the baseline and targets. Do not treat it as either present or absent, and do not force a major override based on the lead.\n\nUseful authoritative lookup endpoints for a follow-up, once exact manifests/locks are available:\n\n- GitHub advisory record: https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c\n- OSV API/query interface: https://osv.dev/ (query each exact package and resolved version; preserve query timestamp/result)\n- npm package metadata and canonical package documentation: `https://registry.npmjs.org/<package>` and the package's upstream release/migration documentation; assess each exact resolved version rather than infer safety from semver labels.\n\nThese are lookup pointers, not evidence that any target includes or avoids the advisory.\n\n## Concrete blockers / next evidence\n\n1. Obtain read-only access to GitHub API/raw files for repository `entireio/entire-brain` (or provide the immutable trees/lockfiles as data) and compare only baseline `ad65996...` against each named head.\n2. For PR354, diff both manifests/locks at those trees and enumerate direct and lockfile-resolved transitive changes. For PR357, do this separately for `scripts/bench` and `webui`; determine package identities from the actual files, not PR title.\n3. For every changed resolved package, check current GHSA and OSV records and official upstream release notes/engine requirements/deprecation or yank state, install lifecycle scripts, and provenance/signature claims. Capture lookup time and exact version.\n4. Inspect repository call sites/configuration for relevant changed packages against each target tree; report what is observed and what static inspection cannot establish (including runtime paths and coverage). Distinguish inherited baseline findings from changes introduced by each PR.\n5. Parent-provided CI/benchmark observations are evidence about those checks only, not security clearance. The independent app-author Bugbot restriction remains a separate merge block; no retries/workarounds were attempted.\n\nThis is an evidence-gap report, not a merge-readiness recommendation.\n\nOutput saved to: /Users/alex/.local/state/herdr/orchestrations/dependency-followups-20261015/remaining-js-dependency-safety.md (4.4 KB, 34 lines). Read this file if needed.\n\nRetention-managed async directory: /var/folders/wl/8b8rnjvn6_jfl4wz9fw883qh0000gn/T/pi-subagents-uid-501/async-subagent-runs/b2f15f79-dfd7-4763-9206-5a9d048d892c\n\nSession file: /Users/alex/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-alex-.herdr-worktrees-entire-brain-alex-manage-dependencies--/2026-10-15T00-32-39-639Z_01a13cf9-b2d7-7659-85fa-866965c99692/8bdd46a7-b6b0-40db-b263-25eba5c33e15/run-0/session.jsonl","display":false,"id":"3254562c","parentId":"f1215800","timestamp":"2026-10-16T02:48:16.759Z"}
