{"type":"custom_message","customType":"subagent-notify","content":"Background task completed: **delegate**\n\ndelegate:\n# Dependency-bot update evidence (read-only; exact-tree comparison)\n\nScope: immutable baseline `ad65996bee631e3044773407df48edc1e85e0c17` compared separately with tar head `bfbb527633840fbd1e76f395810adb1e36eeffb3` (PR354) and grouped head `9a3f538b386ad22dca0f9d7f896f4f9e9c9234f5` (PR357). Inventories below come from those tree's `package.json`/`package-lock.json` JSON. No installs, lifecycle scripts, tests, builds, Git checkout/ref/index/worktree changes, or merge activity.\n\n## Exact lockfile changes\n\n### PR354 / tar — `scripts/bench`\n\nDirect manifest dependency: no change (`node-llama-cpp: ^3`). Only changed resolved package:\n\n- `tar` **7.5.16 → 7.5.22** (lockfile entry `node_modules/tar`).\n\nNo other package entry version changed in this lockfile comparison; thus no changed transitive versions to enumerate for this update.\n\n### PR357 / grouped update — both lockfiles\n\n`scripts/bench/package.json` direct dependency is unchanged (`node-llama-cpp: ^3`). Changed resolved versions:\n\n- Direct: `node-llama-cpp` **3.18.1 → 3.22.1**.\n- Transitives/resolution set: `@huggingface/jinja` **0.5.9 → 0.5.10**; `fs-extra` **11.3.5 → 11.4.1**; `lifecycle-utils` **3.1.1 → 4.5.2**; `node-addon-api` **8.8.0 → 8.9.2**; `simple-git` remains **3.36.0 → 3.36.0** (not a version delta; included because relevant advisory lead); `@simple-git/argv-parser` remains **1.1.1 → 1.1.1** (not a delta; included for the same reason).\n- `@node-llama-cpp` platform packages: `linux-arm64`, `linux-armv7l`, `linux-x64`, `linux-x64-cuda`, `linux-x64-cuda-ext`, `linux-x64-vulkan`, `mac-arm64-metal`, `mac-x64`, `win-arm64`, `win-x64`, `win-x64-cuda`, `win-x64-cuda-ext`, `win-x64-vulkan` each **3.18.1 → 3.22.1**; `linux-riscv64` **absent → 3.22.1**. Optional platform packages; lock entries mark platform restrictions (Linux variants and glibc where applicable). This is a resolved platform set, not evidence every artifact is installed or used on every runner.\n\n`webui/package.json` direct devDependency: `@playwright/test` **1.63.0 → 1.64.0**. Its lockfile transitive companions: `playwright` **1.63.0 → 1.64.0** and `playwright-core` **1.63.0 → 1.64.0**.\n\nThe inventory is of changed resolved versions, not every newly widened dependency range recorded inside node-llama-cpp metadata. Its lock entry updates requirements for jinja (`^0.5.6 → ^0.5.10`), fs-extra (`^11.3.4 → ^11.4.0`), lifecycle-utils (`^3.1.1 → ^4.5.2`), node-addon-api (`^8.6.0 → ^8.9.2`), and simple-git (`^3.33.0 → ^3.36.0`). `node-llama-cpp` also lists many unchanged resolved packages; their versions did not change in this lock comparison.\n\n## Usage and compatibility observations\n\n- `scripts/bench/embed-server.mjs` imports `getLlama` from `node-llama-cpp`; this is an actual direct use. Other repository references include benchmark verification/pins and tests that inspect its installed dependency path, but those do not demonstrate production runtime use. The updated package metadata says Node `>=20.0.0`; check the actual benchmark runner Node version/config separately. It includes a `postinstall` script invoking `node ./dist/cli/cli.js postinstall`, and platform-specific native/prebuilt artifacts. Do not execute it under this review.\n- `webui/browser-tests/viz.spec.cjs` and `webui/playwright.config.cjs` import `@playwright/test`; `.github/workflows/test.yml` invokes `npm exec --prefix webui -- playwright install --with-deps chromium`. This supports use in browser-test setup, not production runtime. Package metadata for `@playwright/test`/playwright 1.64.0 says Node `>=20`.\n- Exact-tree text search for `tar` outside package files did not find an application import/call in tracked text. It is a lockfile-resolved dependency; static text search does not prove unreachable behavior, and transitive code may invoke it.\n- `tar` 7.5.22 registry metadata reports Node `>=18`, no deprecated field; scripts include `prepare` building via `tshy` and `scripts/build.sh`. This is upstream package lifecycle metadata, not a claim that the repository executes prepare during its normal workflow.\n- `node-llama-cpp` 3.22.1 registry metadata has Node `>=20`, no deprecated field; `postinstall` and native/platform package behavior are relevant operationally. `lifecycle-utils` 4.5.2 metadata had no engines/deprecation and a `prepare` hook. These updates include a major-version change for lifecycle-utils (3→4), despite the outer dependency being nominally within node-llama-cpp's `^3`; upstream API/compatibility notes must be consulted before assuming safe behavior.\n- The group changes lockfile platform inventory including new `linux-riscv64`; package metadata alone does not establish support on the project's actual CI/runtime hosts. The lock includes integrity hashes and registry.npmjs.org tarball URLs, but that alone does not establish provenance/signature/attestation.\n\n## Advisory data (OSV live queries, queried 2026-10-15)\n\nQueries to `https://api.osv.dev/v1/query` for npm package plus exact resolved version returned:\n\n- `tar@7.5.22`: no vulnerabilities returned.\n- `node-llama-cpp@3.22.1`: none returned.\n- `simple-git@3.36.0`: **GHSA-858h-whjf-mvg5**, **GHSA-g4wm-2vf7-vfgr**, **GHSA-x6jw-m9v5-85vh** returned.\n- `@simple-git/argv-parser@1.1.1`: **GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c** returned.\n- `@playwright/test@1.64.0`, `playwright@1.64.0`, `playwright-core@1.64.0`, `lifecycle-utils@4.5.2`: none returned.\n\n“No vulnerabilities returned” is strictly the result of that exact OSV query at that time, not proof of absence. I did not obtain a separate current GitHub Advisory database response for every package or query every unchanged transitive dependency; current GHSA/OSV coverage beyond the listed exact versions remains unestablished.\n\n### argv-parser lead / inherited baseline concern\n\nThe queried advisory is not a newly introduced lockfile version delta: baseline already resolves `simple-git@3.36.0` and `@simple-git/argv-parser@1.1.1`, and the grouped head resolves those same versions. The baseline and target node-llama-cpp lock entries both depend on simple-git (range changes from `^3.33.0` to `^3.36.0`, resolved version stays 3.36.0). OSV reports the argv-parser advisory on 1.1.1, hence it is an **inherited baseline exposure indicator**, not an introduced package-version change. Advisory synopsis is omission of the `VISUAL` editor environment variable from unsafe-editor detection. The lock does not prove the vulnerable path is exercised. No source-level exploitability determination was made, and no major override is proposed. Separately, OSV reports three `simple-git@3.36.0` advisories; those too apply to an unchanged resolved version already in baseline. Their synopses concern unsafe-operation bypass/command execution and Git configuration. Whether affected unsafe-operation APIs/configurations are used is unresolved by this bounded package-name search.\n\n## Upstream guidance and limits\n\nRegistry metadata endpoints checked: `https://registry.npmjs.org/tar`, `/node-llama-cpp`, `/simple-git`, `/@simple-git%2Fargv-parser`, `/@playwright%2Ftest`, `/playwright`, `/playwright-core`, `/lifecycle-utils`. The queried latest tags at that time were tar 7.5.22, node-llama-cpp 3.22.1, simple-git 4.0.2, argv-parser 2.0.1, Playwright family 1.64.1, lifecycle-utils 4.5.2. Latest is metadata only—not a recommendation to widen/override. Package metadata exposed engines/scripts/deprecation/repository; queried records had no `deprecated` field. The tarball integrity values are in the immutable locks. Registry responses did not establish signed provenance/attestations for the target tarballs.\n\nRelevant upstream sources:\n\n- tar releases/changelog: https://github.com/isaacs/node-tar/releases and https://github.com/isaacs/node-tar/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md; package metadata: https://registry.npmjs.org/tar\n- node-llama-cpp releases/docs: https://github.com/withcatai/node-llama-cpp/releases and https://github.com/withcatai/node-llama-cpp; package metadata: https://registry.npmjs.org/node-llama-cpp\n- simple-git releases: https://github.com/steveukx/git-js/releases; argv-parser package metadata: https://registry.npmjs.org/%40simple-git%2Fargv-parser\n- Playwright release notes: https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/releases; package metadata: https://registry.npmjs.org/%40playwright%2Ftest\n- Advisory: https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c; OSV query service: https://osv.dev/ and API https://api.osv.dev/v1/query\n\nOfficial release/migration notes were not fully reviewed package-by-package in this pass. In particular, the lifecycle-utils 3→4 migration implications and node-llama-cpp changes across 3.18.1→3.22.1 need upstream release-note review. I did not establish the full changed-package advisory picture, transitive behavioral call graph, provenance attestations, runtime Node versions, or whether susceptible simple-git operations are called. Those remain specific evidence limits; passing CI/benchmarks supplied by parent does not settle them.\n\n## Method and boundary\n\nExact comparisons used only baseline and the two named full commit IDs, never local `main`/parent HEAD. Brain CLI remained unavailable (`entire brain` unknown command); Graph binary was available (provider entire-graph v0.4.1-nightly.202609240616.f22e6c95, JS/TS semantic coverage). Since task-specific evidence concerned exact-tree package manifests/locks and bounded lexical usage, those records were read directly; no structural claim depends on Graph or a local HEAD query. No merge-ready conclusion is made.\n\nOutput saved to: /Users/alex/.local/state/herdr/orchestrations/dependency-followups-20261015/remaining-js-dependency-safety.md (9.3 KB, 68 lines). Read this file if needed.\n\nRetention-managed async directory: /var/folders/wl/8b8rnjvn6_jfl4wz9fw883qh0000gn/T/pi-subagents-uid-501/async-subagent-runs/2d9e74a3-2778-4817-8f49-72fd466f91b3\n\nSession file: /Users/alex/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-alex-.herdr-worktrees-entire-brain-alex-manage-dependencies--/2026-10-15T00-32-39-639Z_01a13cf9-b2d7-7659-85fa-866965c99692/8bdd46a7-b6b0-40db-b263-25eba5c33e15/run-0/session.jsonl","display":false,"id":"bc15ca4e","parentId":"958c9374","timestamp":"2026-10-16T02:52:40.922Z"}
