{"type":"message","id":"0eef52e5","parentId":"b06417c8","timestamp":"2026-10-16T03:06:04.677Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_e95e4cc9250e4f8ea906d4ef0a53dd9b|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad19498a2d081918c6de5542de376f7","toolName":"mcp","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"COR-2136\",\"uuid\":\"d6007de0-031b-4ca0-be0b-a230f1a9793e\",\"title\":\"entire-brain: unblock nanoid security patch with isolated benchmark fixtures\",\"description\":\"## Outcome\\n\\nSafely complete the existing nanoid 5.1.11 → 5.1.16 dependency update associated with [https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/268](<https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/268>). Repair only the demonstrated benchmark test-fixture/expectation coupling, preserving production fail-closed behavior and immutable historical evidence. Work on the existing bot update, not a replacement PR.\\n\\n## Verified evidence\\n\\nCurrent main includes merged Go security baseline fb972e5d9d14ab6e2e935fb0a083ae565b316680. The bot branch was normally synchronized to head 9311e98eab636428192f52c23ee068b0f7b637b2. Its dependency delta is three package-lock fields for nanoid. GHSA-28wg-ghj8-5hjv identifies 5.1.16 as fixed; exact-version OSV returned no advisories and the official release documents the negative-size loop fix. Revalidate exact current head and authoritative target evidence before executing updated dependencies.\\n\\nOn that exact head, benchmark-corpus run 38707872366/job 116331683071 fails two assertions: ProtocolCheckTest.test_preparation_artifacts_are_consistent gains the exact legitimate `engine runtime pin package_lock hash is stale` diagnostic, while PublicEngineEvidenceTest.test_public_bundle_validates_and_is_protocol_checker_authoritative_v4 passes production CHECK.REPO as pin_repo despite synthetic temporary inputs and expects no errors. Other negative-control archive tests pass and are not the defect. Detailed triage is retained by parent; verify source directly.\\n\\n## Authorized bounded design\\n\\nSeparate test intentions: historical validation must continue rejecting the changed live lock, while synthetic public-bundle fixtures must have an isolated, internally consistent test-only runtime binding. Update only the precise expected historical diagnostic where warranted by this actual lockfile change; never introduce arbitrary error acceptance, suppress a diagnostic, reseal historical material or represent stale production proof as valid. Prior exploration mistakenly treated a production trust-root/checker redesign as necessary; no such migration is authorized or required by this test-only design. Exact implementation remains owner-validated.\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n\\n* Reproduce both exact failures before edits.\\n* Add focused regression/mutation coverage proving altered production lock bytes are still rejected, invalid synthetic bindings fail, and synthetic fixture authority never satisfies production authority.\\n* Both focused Python 3.14 tests and their full modules pass with unchanged real validators.\\n* Production validator code, pin/schema/checker/preregistration/storage commitments and historical receipt bytes remain unchanged.\\n* Full repository-native format/lint/test/build and exact-head CI evidence, scoped current upstream security/release/provenance evidence, independent review and findings/monitor disposition receipts are retained.\\n* Keep this one coherent update below normal size ceilings; existing bot branch normal synchronization/push only, never force. No new PR or initial preflight fanout for an already-open artifact.\\n* Parent owns merge, post-merge success inventory/check receipt, cleanup/removal and Linear lifecycle. Known Bugbot bot-author restriction must be reported honestly; no retry spam, author spoofing or admin/security-setting change.\\n\\n## Isolation\\n\\nThe parent checkout contains an intentionally preserved staged go-billy merge. Do not modify, reset, stash, abort or switch that checkout. Use an isolated owning workspace and inspect any existing session binding before writing. Process remaining bot candidates sequentially after this bounded outcome.\",\"projectMilestone\":{\"id\":\"b3b9c5e4-e502-4b63-9f45-382109d35556\",\"name\":\"Post launch\"},\"priority\":{\"value\":2,\"name\":\"High\"},\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2136/entire-brain-unblock-nanoid-security-patch-with-isolated-benchmark\",\"gitBranchName\":\"alex/cor-2136-entire-brain-unblock-nanoid-security-patch-with-isolated\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-15T08:54:32.075Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-16T03:06:03.463Z\",\"archivedAt\":null,\"completedAt\":\"2026-10-16T03:06:03.439Z\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-15T08:54:32.205Z\",\"canceledAt\":null,\"dueDate\":null,\"slaStartedAt\":null,\"slaMediumRiskAt\":null,\"slaHighRiskAt\":null,\"slaBreachesAt\":null,\"status\":\"Done\",\"statusType\":\"completed\",\"labels\":[\"Security\"],\"attachments\":[{\"id\":\"44042ef5-5d45-4db3-989f-525932475d49\",\"title\":\"N​​anoid security patch and fixture repair — Trail 268\",\"subtitle\":\"Entire is a fast, distributed, Git-compatible network for mirroring GitHub repositories so agents can clone fast without hitting origin rate limits.\",\"url\":\"https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/268\"}],\"documents\":[],\"createdBy\":\"Alex Ong\",\"createdById\":\"45a00cf6-3a37-45ab-a508-d9da7f9d514c\",\"assignee\":\"Alex Ong\",\"assigneeId\":\"45a00cf6-3a37-45ab-a508-d9da7f9d514c\",\"project\":\"P0 · GA the Local Brain\",\"projectId\":\"91954c69-3fab-4281-84e0-cf4b81d85d75\",\"team\":\"Core\",\"teamId\":\"894690b6-2173-4cbe-abd3-6e7ea5ff5bb9\"}"}],"details":{"mode":"call","mcpResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"COR-2136\",\"uuid\":\"d6007de0-031b-4ca0-be0b-a230f1a9793e\",\"title\":\"entire-brain: unblock nanoid security patch with isolated benchmark fixtures\",\"description\":\"## Outcome\\n\\nSafely complete the existing nanoid 5.1.11 → 5.1.16 dependency update associated with [https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/268](<https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/268>). Repair only the demonstrated benchmark test-fixture/expectation coupling, preserving production fail-closed behavior and immutable historical evidence. Work on the existing bot update, not a replacement PR.\\n\\n## Verified evidence\\n\\nCurrent main includes merged Go security baseline fb972e5d9d14ab6e2e935fb0a083ae565b316680. The bot branch was normally synchronized to head 9311e98eab636428192f52c23ee068b0f7b637b2. Its dependency delta is three package-lock fields for nanoid. GHSA-28wg-ghj8-5hjv identifies 5.1.16 as fixed; exact-version OSV returned no advisories and the official release documents the negative-size loop fix. Revalidate exact current head and authoritative target evidence before executing updated dependencies.\\n\\nOn that exact head, benchmark-corpus run 38707872366/job 116331683071 fails two assertions: ProtocolCheckTest.test_preparation_artifacts_are_consistent gains the exact legitimate `engine runtime pin package_lock hash is stale` diagnostic, while PublicEngineEvidenceTest.test_public_bundle_validates_and_is_protocol_checker_authoritative_v4 passes production CHECK.REPO as pin_repo despite synthetic temporary inputs and expects no errors. Other negative-control archive tests pass and are not the defect. Detailed triage is retained by parent; verify source directly.\\n\\n## Authorized bounded design\\n\\nSeparate test intentions: historical validation must continue rejecting the changed live lock, while synthetic public-bundle fixtures must have an isolated, internally consistent test-only runtime binding. Update only the precise expected historical diagnostic where warranted by this actual lockfile change; never introduce arbitrary error acceptance, suppress a diagnostic, reseal historical material or represent stale production proof as valid. Prior exploration mistakenly treated a production trust-root/checker redesign as necessary; no such migration is authorized or required by this test-only design. Exact implementation remains owner-validated.\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n\\n* Reproduce both exact failures before edits.\\n* Add focused regression/mutation coverage proving altered production lock bytes are still rejected, invalid synthetic bindings fail, and synthetic fixture authority never satisfies production authority.\\n* Both focused Python 3.14 tests and their full modules pass with unchanged real validators.\\n* Production validator code, pin/schema/checker/preregistration/storage commitments and historical receipt bytes remain unchanged.\\n* Full repository-native format/lint/test/build and exact-head CI evidence, scoped current upstream security/release/provenance evidence, independent review and findings/monitor disposition receipts are retained.\\n* Keep this one coherent update below normal size ceilings; existing bot branch normal synchronization/push only, never force. No new PR or initial preflight fanout for an already-open artifact.\\n* Parent owns merge, post-merge success inventory/check receipt, cleanup/removal and Linear lifecycle. Known Bugbot bot-author restriction must be reported honestly; no retry spam, author spoofing or admin/security-setting change.\\n\\n## Isolation\\n\\nThe parent checkout contains an intentionally preserved staged go-billy merge. Do not modify, reset, stash, abort or switch that checkout. Use an isolated owning workspace and inspect any existing session binding before writing. Process remaining bot candidates sequentially after this bounded outcome.\",\"projectMilestone\":{\"id\":\"b3b9c5e4-e502-4b63-9f45-382109d35556\",\"name\":\"Post launch\"},\"priority\":{\"value\":2,\"name\":\"High\"},\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2136/entire-brain-unblock-nanoid-security-patch-with-isolated-benchmark\",\"gitBranchName\":\"alex/cor-2136-entire-brain-unblock-nanoid-security-patch-with-isolated\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-15T08:54:32.075Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-16T03:06:03.463Z\",\"archivedAt\":null,\"completedAt\":\"2026-10-16T03:06:03.439Z\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-15T08:54:32.205Z\",\"canceledAt\":null,\"dueDate\":null,\"slaStartedAt\":null,\"slaMediumRiskAt\":null,\"slaHighRiskAt\":null,\"slaBreachesAt\":null,\"status\":\"Done\",\"statusType\":\"completed\",\"labels\":[\"Security\"],\"attachments\":[{\"id\":\"44042ef5-5d45-4db3-989f-525932475d49\",\"title\":\"N​​anoid security patch and fixture repair — Trail 268\",\"subtitle\":\"Entire is a fast, distributed, Git-compatible network for mirroring GitHub repositories so agents can clone fast without hitting origin rate limits.\",\"url\":\"https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/268\"}],\"documents\":[],\"createdBy\":\"Alex Ong\",\"createdById\":\"45a00cf6-3a37-45ab-a508-d9da7f9d514c\",\"assignee\":\"Alex Ong\",\"assigneeId\":\"45a00cf6-3a37-45ab-a508-d9da7f9d514c\",\"project\":\"P0 · GA the Local Brain\",\"projectId\":\"91954c69-3fab-4281-84e0-cf4b81d85d75\",\"team\":\"Core\",\"teamId\":\"894690b6-2173-4cbe-abd3-6e7ea5ff5bb9\"}"}]},"server":"linear","tool":"save_issue"},"isError":false,"durationMs":2783,"timestamp":1792119964677}}
{"type":"message","id":"e371724a","parentId":"0eef52e5","timestamp":"2026-10-16T03:06:04.677Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_1c0a84bf0ece405298cab24bf3318a2a|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad194998ed08191aa59b1c7f964246a","toolName":"mcp","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"COR-2139\",\"uuid\":\"a29fee86-bb57-45c0-bb53-5a3ddb8a828c\",\"title\":\"entire-brain: resolve go-git dependency-update merge conflicts\",\"description\":\"Resolve only the mechanical conflicts for the existing go-git beta update linked to [https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/277](<https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/277>). User explicitly authorized parallel conflict-repair workers in isolated checkouts; merges remain sequential and parent-owned.\\n\\nPreserve current main's merged security baseline and unrelated dependency selections. Retain the bot's intended update only if it does not undo an authoritative security fix; independently verify exact versions/fixed ancestry before running target code. Do not infer safety from beta version ordering. Resolve generated checksum/config conflicts normally; no force-push, authored-source conflict guesses, new privileges, test weakening, provenance migration, new PR, or admin changes. Stop for actual semantic/version-selection uncertainty.\\n\\nAcceptance: independently verified target/head/base and exact conflict scope; normal main merge, focused checks and full repository pre-push verification on resolved tree, independent diff review using a read-accessible artifact, non-force update to existing bot branch, current GitHub conflict status/head and CI next signal. Do not merge or claim full security readiness from conflict resolution. Existing bot-author Bugbot access restriction is reported, not retriggered repeatedly or bypassed. Parent owns review/merge/post-merge/cleanup/Linear lifecycle.\\n\\nUse one exclusive worker checkout. Do not touch nanoid's active fixture-repair workspace or the parent checkout. Coordinate overlapping go-billy manifest selections through parent metadata, not cross-worktree edits. Baseline <issue id=\\\"f657511b-fb0e-45ae-9a3c-c2712f68eecc\\\" href=\\\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2129/entire-brain-establish-a-verified-go-dependency-security-baseline\\\">COR-2129</issue> is complete; follow latest main rather than restoring older parent choices.\",\"projectMilestone\":{\"id\":\"b3b9c5e4-e502-4b63-9f45-382109d35556\",\"name\":\"Post launch\"},\"priority\":{\"value\":2,\"name\":\"High\"},\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2139/entire-brain-resolve-go-git-dependency-update-merge-conflicts\",\"gitBranchName\":\"alex/cor-2139-entire-brain-resolve-go-git-dependency-update-merge\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-15T10:02:24.857Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-16T03:06:03.340Z\",\"archivedAt\":null,\"completedAt\":\"2026-10-16T03:06:03.327Z\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-15T10:02:25.644Z\",\"canceledAt\":null,\"dueDate\":null,\"slaStartedAt\":null,\"slaMediumRiskAt\":null,\"slaHighRiskAt\":null,\"slaBreachesAt\":null,\"status\":\"Done\",\"statusType\":\"completed\",\"labels\":[\"Security\"],\"attachments\":[{\"id\":\"8b38d4af-2776-4a85-bcc1-ef094926c44d\",\"title\":\"Go-git conflict repair — Trail 277\",\"subtitle\":\"Entire is a fast, distributed, Git-compatible network for mirroring GitHub repositories so agents can clone fast without hitting origin rate limits.\",\"url\":\"https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/277\"}],\"documents\":[],\"createdBy\":\"Alex Ong\",\"createdById\":\"45a00cf6-3a37-45ab-a508-d9da7f9d514c\",\"assignee\":\"Alex Ong\",\"assigneeId\":\"45a00cf6-3a37-45ab-a508-d9da7f9d514c\",\"project\":\"P0 · GA the Local Brain\",\"projectId\":\"91954c69-3fab-4281-84e0-cf4b81d85d75\",\"team\":\"Core\",\"teamId\":\"894690b6-2173-4cbe-abd3-6e7ea5ff5bb9\"}"}],"details":{"mode":"call","mcpResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"COR-2139\",\"uuid\":\"a29fee86-bb57-45c0-bb53-5a3ddb8a828c\",\"title\":\"entire-brain: resolve go-git dependency-update merge conflicts\",\"description\":\"Resolve only the mechanical conflicts for the existing go-git beta update linked to [https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/277](<https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/277>). User explicitly authorized parallel conflict-repair workers in isolated checkouts; merges remain sequential and parent-owned.\\n\\nPreserve current main's merged security baseline and unrelated dependency selections. Retain the bot's intended update only if it does not undo an authoritative security fix; independently verify exact versions/fixed ancestry before running target code. Do not infer safety from beta version ordering. Resolve generated checksum/config conflicts normally; no force-push, authored-source conflict guesses, new privileges, test weakening, provenance migration, new PR, or admin changes. Stop for actual semantic/version-selection uncertainty.\\n\\nAcceptance: independently verified target/head/base and exact conflict scope; normal main merge, focused checks and full repository pre-push verification on resolved tree, independent diff review using a read-accessible artifact, non-force update to existing bot branch, current GitHub conflict status/head and CI next signal. Do not merge or claim full security readiness from conflict resolution. Existing bot-author Bugbot access restriction is reported, not retriggered repeatedly or bypassed. Parent owns review/merge/post-merge/cleanup/Linear lifecycle.\\n\\nUse one exclusive worker checkout. Do not touch nanoid's active fixture-repair workspace or the parent checkout. Coordinate overlapping go-billy manifest selections through parent metadata, not cross-worktree edits. Baseline <issue id=\\\"f657511b-fb0e-45ae-9a3c-c2712f68eecc\\\" href=\\\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2129/entire-brain-establish-a-verified-go-dependency-security-baseline\\\">COR-2129</issue> is complete; follow latest main rather than restoring older parent choices.\",\"projectMilestone\":{\"id\":\"b3b9c5e4-e502-4b63-9f45-382109d35556\",\"name\":\"Post launch\"},\"priority\":{\"value\":2,\"name\":\"High\"},\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2139/entire-brain-resolve-go-git-dependency-update-merge-conflicts\",\"gitBranchName\":\"alex/cor-2139-entire-brain-resolve-go-git-dependency-update-merge\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-15T10:02:24.857Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-16T03:06:03.340Z\",\"archivedAt\":null,\"completedAt\":\"2026-10-16T03:06:03.327Z\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-15T10:02:25.644Z\",\"canceledAt\":null,\"dueDate\":null,\"slaStartedAt\":null,\"slaMediumRiskAt\":null,\"slaHighRiskAt\":null,\"slaBreachesAt\":null,\"status\":\"Done\",\"statusType\":\"completed\",\"labels\":[\"Security\"],\"attachments\":[{\"id\":\"8b38d4af-2776-4a85-bcc1-ef094926c44d\",\"title\":\"Go-git conflict repair — Trail 277\",\"subtitle\":\"Entire is a fast, distributed, Git-compatible network for mirroring GitHub repositories so agents can clone fast without hitting origin rate limits.\",\"url\":\"https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/277\"}],\"documents\":[],\"createdBy\":\"Alex Ong\",\"createdById\":\"45a00cf6-3a37-45ab-a508-d9da7f9d514c\",\"assignee\":\"Alex Ong\",\"assigneeId\":\"45a00cf6-3a37-45ab-a508-d9da7f9d514c\",\"project\":\"P0 · GA the Local Brain\",\"projectId\":\"91954c69-3fab-4281-84e0-cf4b81d85d75\",\"team\":\"Core\",\"teamId\":\"894690b6-2173-4cbe-abd3-6e7ea5ff5bb9\"}"}]},"server":"linear","tool":"save_issue"},"isError":false,"durationMs":2136,"timestamp":1792119964677}}
