{"type":"message","id":"b899961a","parentId":"60c669d9","timestamp":"2026-10-17T04:40:07.127Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_a15345b95f8845ba85d52dcb18b7cb7c|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad2fc2417f48191a62539e1a26c4daf","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# COR-2145 — setup-go XML parser: bounded assessment\n\n## Executive summary\n\nCurrent immutable main `c8624c8826e4d2632510b46041a54694a0504650` uses `actions/setup-go@v7` in both `.github/workflows/test.yml` and `.github/workflows/nightly.yml`. The exact v7 lock currently resolves `fast-xml-parser` **5.9.3**, whereas exact prior `v6.4.0` resolves **5.4.1**. The reported GHSA range (5.9.3 through <5.10.1) therefore applies to v7 and not v6.4.0. Advisory presence in the action bundle is established; this investigation did **not** establish that attacker-controlled data can reach the vulnerable parser operation in these jobs. It also did not prove non-reachability: the vulnerable dataflow from setup-go's actual download/error handling through `@azure/core-xml` was not source-traced to completion. Reachability and exploitability remain unresolved, not demonstrated.\n\nNo implementation or merge verdict. A next pass should close the exact unproven edge below before choosing remediation. Do not infer exposure solely from v7 adoption or infer safety from permissions/CI.\n\n## Exact ref/version matrix\n\n| Consumer | Current source ref | Action ref | Exact lock resolution / evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `test.yml` | immutable main above | `actions/setup-go@v7`, Go `1.27.2` in multiple jobs | Official `https://github.com/actions/setup-go/blob/v7/package-lock.json`: `fast-xml-parser` 5.9.3 |\n| `nightly.yml` | same | `actions/setup-go@v7`, Go `1.27.x` | Same v7 lock: 5.9.3 |\n| Prior baseline (provided history; not asserted as current source) | original workflow reportedly exact v6.4.0 | `actions/setup-go@v6.4.0` | Official `https://github.com/actions/setup-go/blob/v6.4.0/package-lock.json`: 5.4.1 |\n\nOfficial v7 bundle: `https://github.com/actions/setup-go/blob/v7/dist/setup/index.js` (3,576,309 bytes; GitHub API blob SHA `187253e6f2118f85ec516374beed40d983a70015`). v7 lock blob SHA `d288f60bc1c305964872bec85cd89af537600518`; v6.4.0 lock blob SHA `b3fa41aed522f51bba10c3e7e33f4503f4079ed9`. v7 bundle contains parser source-module identifiers, corroborating bundling, but that is not a runtime call path.\n\n## Advisory status and patch\n\nRequired authoritative live GHSA/OSV status, affected range, vulnerable operation detail, and upstream patch/release comparison were **not independently retrieved in this pass**. The task's prior evidence reports GHSA-8r6m-32jq-jx6q as HIGH, non-withdrawn, affected `>=5.9.3 <5.10.1`, fixed `5.10.1`, involving repeated DOCTYPE handling; treat these as supplied prior evidence pending live verification, not this pass's verified status. Relevant authoritative endpoints to verify: `https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-8r6m-32jq-jx6q`, `https://osv-vulnerabilities.storage.googleapis.com/npm/all.zip` / OSV query API, and upstream `https://github.com/NaturalIntelligence/fast-xml-parser` release/commit patch. Do not present 5.10.1 as a compatible action fix without checking upstream setup-go lock/bundle and release evidence.\n\n## Exposure and unresolved edge\n\nThe exact current workflow source establishes placement, but not the parser's input. `test.yml` has pull_request, push-to-main, tag, and manual triggers; top-level `contents: read`; most jobs do not elevate permissions. Nightly is schedule/manual and its build job elevates `contents: write` to publish. Both use setup-go before their own build/test commands. This makes action execution relevant in privileged nightly context, but workflow text alone does not establish what untrusted PR code can influence or whether it can provide XML to the action. `contents: read` is not a safety argument.\n\n**Specific unproven edge:** setup-go's action entrypoint / unbundled source → actual Go version/tool download and cache client responses → Azure XML deserialization → `fast-xml-parser` call with repeated-DOCTYPE input. Not verified: which response fields are XML, whether such XML is possible on the executed path, whether archive bytes or repository-controlled inputs enter that path, how errors are parsed, parser options, response size bounds, endpoint/proxy/environment overrides, and whether a lower-trust party can control the relevant response without already having arbitrary execution in the job. No concrete attacker-controlled chain is established, and no counterexample chain can responsibly be claimed from the inspected evidence.\n\nDo not count downloaded Go archives, cache contents, or repository files as parser XML inputs without code evidence. Conversely, a trusted-service-error assumption needs source-level provenance and cannot be inferred from expected service behavior. Dynamic dispatch inside the bundled JavaScript is not covered by the workflow inspection.\n\n## Confidence and limitations\n\nHigh confidence on current workflow refs and exact lock versions: direct immutable repository tree plus official upstream lock downloads. Moderate/high confidence that v7 bundle contains the parser (official bundle source-module strings), but no execution. Low confidence on reachability/exploitability: no API call-graph or focused upstream source/patch investigation completed. No tests, installs, builds, payloads, or vulnerable third-party code execution were performed.\n\nBrain availability check attempted first: `entire brain version`, capabilities, brief, and recall all failed because installed `entire` CLI reports unknown command `brain`; historical retrieval unavailable here (parent reports its own attempts unavailable). Graph version/capabilities succeeded (`entire-graph v0.4.1-nightly.202609240616.f22e6c95`; JavaScript/TypeScript semantic relations supported). Its documented canonical guide invocation `entire graph agent-guide` succeeded. No graph query was run because the required target is an immutable external action revision, not the working tree; graph fallback cannot establish that upstream runtime dataflow. Repository source was read with `git show <immutable-sha>:...`, never old branch HEAD. Static official GitHub source/metadata fetches only. No Python verification invoked.\n\n## Smallest compatible options (not recommendations yet)\n\n1. **Pin a setup-go release whose lock and shipped bundle resolve parser >=5.10.1**, if an official compatible release exists. Validate release/action.yml, lock, bundled code and upstream changelog/patch; then regression-check exact workflow/tool-cache behavior and ref policy.\n2. **Pin exact immutable action commit** for that verified release, with upstream maintenance/update policy. Validate same artifacts and action compatibility; mutable `@v7` tag is not immutable.\n3. If no compatible upstream fixed release exists, assess upstream fix/backport or replacement only after proving reachable input. Validate patch against repeated-DOCTYPE regression and setup-go functionality without executing vulnerable code on this host.\n\nThis is evidence-gathering only; no verdict to merge, rollback, vendor, or change workflow."}],"isError":false,"durationMs":635,"timestamp":1792212007127}}
