{"type":"compaction","id":"7ead27a1","parentId":"7f0547da","timestamp":"2026-10-17T04:42:20.646Z","summary":"## Goal\nComplete seven dependency-bot updates in `entireio/entire-brain`, including compatibility fixes, conflict repair, actual-merge verification, and cleanup. **Processing is now complete:** all seven merged and passed all 18 required checks on their individual actual merge commits. Preserve separate unresolved diagnostic/security follow-ups.\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- User dislikes excessive orchestration, repeated verification/rebase loops, and setup-only handoffs. Prefer concrete existing-branch outcomes.\n- Never force-push, bypass protection, weaken tests/security, invent provenance, or change unrelated dependencies.\n- Preserve production benchmark validators, pins, historical receipts, checker/schema/preregistration commitments.\n- Parent exclusively owns Linear lifecycle, post-merge verification, and non-force workspace removal; workers exclusively write their owned checkout.\n- Reuse checks only with defensible unchanged-input evidence. Do not confuse CI success with security clearance.\n- Mandatory assistant merge gates included current-head Bugbot, CI/main review, zero findings/threads, adjudicated monitor claims. Bugbot was absent due to bot-author restriction; **user performed merges**, assistant did not waive or bypass this.\n- Human-facing reports are Trail-primary.\n- **Python incident restriction:** no executable wrappers/shims/symlinks or global tool/config writes. Run the read-only runtime guard before Python verification; use the genuine repaired interpreter directly.\n- Use explicit `-R entireio/entire-brain` for `gh`: proprietary `entire://` origin can defeat automatic host detection. A nonexistent-file 404 is not authentication failure.\n- Entire Brain availability must be checked before relevant history/source tasks; installed CLI lacked `brain`, permitting scoped disclosed fallback, not installation/reindexing.\n- Controll