ed reverified. This is recovery, **not a root-cause fix or proven flake**.\n- [x] Four owned workspaces cleanly removed without force after preserved receipts and graceful Ctrl+D / idle Fish verification:\n  - wQ5 go-billy: COR-2137 Done2026-10-15T23:15:09Z.\n  - wQ6 setup-go: COR-2138 Done2026-10-16T00:32:21Z.\n  - wQ3 nanoid / wQ4 go-git: path/Git registry/Herdr absence verified2026-10-16T03:04:04Z; COR-2136/COR-2139 Done03:06:03Z.\n  - Ignored `.entire`/cache state privately archived for353/362 before removal; local publication branch refs intentionally retained.\n  - No owned worktrees created for354/357/358; parent workspace intentionally retained.\n- [x] Final verification summary saved2026-10-16T03:23:37Z; all seven actual merges verified, four workspaces removed. Last observed main `358e74a0384e543a30930a726ca5c5818741caec`.\n- [x] User asked “we’re all done now yes?”; assistant confirmed dependency work complete, then explained three remaining separate tickets.\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] None for the dependency-update run. No active worker/test/review/cleanup or pending build is required by this completed task.\n\n### Blocked\nNo remaining merge/build/cleanup blockers. **Separate follow-ups remain Backlog, no implementation authorized:**\n- **COR-2144 — Capture diagnostic context for intermittent Git fixture HEAD parse failures.**\n  - Unknown cause of MacCGO fixture failure above; add minimal sanitized failure-only HEAD/ref/object/environment diagnostics if pursued.\n  - Preserve failure semantics/redaction; no secrets/full config dumps, retry loops, test weakening.\n- **COR-2145 — Assess setup-go v7 bundled XML-parser advisory and workflow exposure.**\n  - Exact upstream v7/v7.0.0 commit `b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e`, fast-xml-parser5.9.3 confirmed runtime lock/bundle.\n  - Active HIGH `GHSA-8r6m-32jq-jx6q`, affected `>=5.9.3,<5.10.1`, fixed5.10.1.\n  - Shipped inclusion established; attacker-controlled XML reachability/exploitability not established. Successful CI does not clear it.\n- **COR-2164 — Assess inherited critical argv-parser advisory in benchmark Git tooling.**\n  - Baselinead659 and both tar/npm updated trees resolve `simple-git3.36.0` / `@simple-git/argv-parser1.1.1`.\n  - Parent verified authoritative active CRITICAL `GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c`, affected `<2.0.1`, fixed2.0.1; synopsis `VISUAL` editor omission from unsafe-editor detection.\n  - **Inherited**, not introduced version regression; vulnerable-path reachability unknown. No forced simple-git4 major override.\n  - OSV also reported `GHSA-858h-whjf-mvg5`, `GHSA-g4wm-2vf7-vfgr`, `GHSA-x6jw-m9v5-85vh` on unchanged simple-git3.36.0; exact applicability needs confirmation.\n- Additional bounded safety assessment gaps retained for tar/npm/upload-artifact: official release/migration/provenance/usage completeness, lifecycle-utils3→4/native-install implications, broader action bundled-runtime review. Not demonstrated exploits or build blockers.\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **Completed processing ≠ universal security certification**: final run dispositions `UPDATED_AND_MERGED:[353,361,362]`, `NEEDS_ATTENTION:[354,356,357,358]`; **all seven actually merged and build-verified**. Attention preserves incomplete safety review, not unfinished merge/cleanup.\n- **Parallel isolated repairs, sequential human merges**: no cross-checkout writing or unmerged lane borrowing; later actual merged fixes integrated normally.\n- **Fixture correction, not provenance redesign**: isolate synthetic test runtime and precise historical diagnostics, preserve real stale rejection and production commitments.\n- **Required gate inventory, not overgating**: Python coverage exporter missing package was optional for local gate contract; no installation or waiver of actual gates.\n- **Root cause before fixes**: exact job logs/focused reproduction first; no speculative rollback or setup-go blame. One same-SHA CI experiment recovered checks; unknown cause separately ticketed.\n- **Actual live branch refs govern ancestry**: scalar PR base snapshot mismatch did not warrant endless checks/rebases once live refs and ancestry agreed.\n- **Evidence before formal finding closure**: green CI/no confirmed regression alone insufficient; same steward supplied proof-backed disposition. Missing Bugbot never substituted for technical finding adjudication.\n- **No repeated broad suites/indefinite polling**: serialize heavy Go slots, leave active bounded commands undisturbed, reuse valid receipts, stop first failure. Native async notifications instead of sleep/poll loops.\n- **Post-merge receipts before cleanup**: full inventories/check IDs/URLs on each actual SHA, then owner release, graceful session exit, ignored-state preservation, non-force removal, then Linear Done.\n- **Monitor errors/disappearance not success**: `unknown monitor` / `monitor not found` and delayed premerge timeout notifications reconciled using actual immutable API evidence; later native success corroborated receipts.\n- **Research correction bounded once**: initial safety helper falsely generalized nonexistent root `package.json`404/missing heads. Parent supplied actual paths/immutable objects with `git fetch --no-write-fetch-head --no-tags`, resumed same child once; no credentials/tool repair or alternate harness.\n\n## Next Steps\n1. No further work necessary for this dependency run; answer user questions concisely.\n2. Only if separately requested, start a bounded new task for COR-2144, COR-2145, or COR-2164. Refresh authoritative versions/advisories/context first; no ongoing implementation authority.\n3. Preserve final verification/cleanup receipts, local publication refs, private ignored-state archives, original diagnostic failure evidence. Do not remove user’s parent workspace or reopen completed agents.\n4. Do not claim the Git failure was fixed or all dependencies security-cleared; describe verified build recovery and separate unresolved assessment work.\n\n## Critical Context\n- P