":0.009612800000000001,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0553328}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792212462085,"responseId":"resp_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad2fdeea2c08191ae362245bff67298","rawStopReason":"completed","durationMs":57150,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}}
{"type":"message","id":"8d68cb90","parentId":"0948ea18","timestamp":"2026-10-17T04:48:41.146Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_0bcb25b3e62a4469a5f5b83a3fff3ff3|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad2fe244c208191b97cee72cb30bd19","toolName":"mcp","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found 9 tools matching \"comment\":\n\nlinear_get_attachment\n  Retrieve an issue attachment by ID. Use format=url to get its title and download URL without fetching the file content. Linear upload URLs are signed for five minutes; call again to refresh. External URLs are returned unchanged. Files embedded in comments have no issue attachment ID; use the URLs in list_comments attachments instead. Download and process documents with your own file tools.\n\n  Parameters:\n    id (string) *required* - Issue attachment ID from get_issue's attachments array (attachments[].id)\n    format (enum: \"content\", \"url\") - Omit or use content to fetch a Linear-hosted file. Use url for attachment metadata without fetching the file; also supports external links\n\nlinear_list_comments\n  List comments on a Linear issue, project, initiative, document, project milestone, or project/initiative status update. Provide exactly one of `issueId`, `projectId`, `initiativeId`, `documentId`, `milestoneId`, or `statusUpdateId`. For issues, projects, and initiatives this returns both top-level discussion threads and inline description comments. Inline (anchored) comments carry a non-null `quotedText` set to the snippet of description text they reference. Returned comments include `author` and nullable `onBehalfOf`; when set, `onBehalfOf` identifies the user the agent author acted for. Files uploaded in comment bodies are returned in `attachments` with titles and download URLs, not issue attachment IDs. Signed upload URLs expire after five minutes; call list_comments again to refresh them. Download documents using these URLs and process them with your own file tools.\n\n  Parameters:\n    limit (number) - Maximum number of results to return per page [maximum: 250] [default: 50]\n    cursor (string) - Omit for the first page. To continue, pass the previous response's cursor when hasNextPage is true\n    orderBy (enum: \"createdAt\", \"updatedAt\") - Timestamp to sort results by: creation time or last update time [default: \"updatedAt\"]\n    issueId (string) - Issue ID or identifier (e.g., LIN-123). P-prefixed identifiers (e.g., P-ENG-123) are projects, not issues (provide exactly one parent)\n    projectId (string) - Project name, ID, identifier (e.g., P-ENG-123), or slug (provide exactly one parent)\n    initiativeId (string) - Initiative name, ID, identifier (e.g., I-123), or slug (provide exactly one parent)\n    documentId (string) - Document ID or slug (provide exactly one parent)\n    milestoneId (string) - Milestone UUID (provide exactly one parent). Resolve milestone names via `list_milestones` first.\n    statusUpdateId (string) - Status update UUID (provide exactly one parent). Resolve status updates via `get_status_updates` first.\n    statusUpdateType (enum: \"project\", \"initiative\") - Type of status update named by `statusUpdateId`, as returned by `get_status_updates`. Only valid together with `statusUpdateId`; omit to check both project and initiative status updates.\n\nlinear_save_comment\n  Create or update a comment on a Linear issue, project, initiative, document, project milestone, or project/initiative status update. If `id` is provided, updates the existing comment; otherwise creates a new one. To start a new thread, pass `body` and exactly one of `issueId`, `projectId`, `initiativeId`, `documentId`, `milestoneId`, or `statusUpdateId` — comments on issues/projects/initiatives become top-level discussion threads; comments on documents/milestones become description comments. A status update holds a single thread, so a comment on an update that already has one is added to it as a reply. To reply to an existing thread, pass `parentId` and `body`; the reply inherits the parent's thread type, so no entity reference is needed. Parent reference fields are ignored when `id` or `parentId` is provided (`statusUpdateType` is rejected instead).\n\n  Parameters:\n    id (string) - Comment ID. If provided, updates the existing comment\n    issueId (string) - Issue ID or identifier (e.g., LIN-123). P-prefixed identifiers (e.g., P-ENG-123) are projects, not issues (provide exactly one parent)\n    projectId (string) - Project name, ID, identifier (e.g., P-ENG-123), or slug (provide exactly one parent)\n    initiativeId (string) - Initiative name, ID, identifier (e.g., I-123), or slug (provide exactly one parent)\n    documentId (string) - Document ID or slug (provide exactly one parent)\n    milestoneId (string) - Milestone UUID (provide exactly one parent). Resolve milestone names via `list_milestones` first.\n    statusUpdateId (string) - Status update UUID (provide exactly one parent). Resolve status updates via `get_status_updates` first.\n    statusUpdateType (enum: \"project\", \"initiative\") - Type of status update named by `statusUpdateId`, as returned by `get_status_updates`. Only valid together with `statusUpdateId`; omit to check both project and initiative status updates.\n    parentId (string) - Parent comment ID (for replies, only when creating)\n    body (string) *required* - Content as Markdown. Do not escape the string — use literal newlines and special characters, not escape sequences. To mention a user, use @displayName (e.g., @johndoe)\n\nlinear_delete_comment\n  Delete a Linear comment. Inline description comments (those with non-null `quotedText`) anchor a mark in the editor, so their root cannot be deleted — delete the replies individually or resolve the thread instead.\n\n  Parameters:\n    id (string) *required* - Comment ID\n\nlinear_extract_images\n  Extract and fetch images from markdown content. Use this to view screenshots, diagrams, or other images embedded in Linear issues, comments, or documents. Pass the markdown content (e.g., issue description) and receive the images as viewable data.\n\n  Parameters:\n    markdown (string) *required* - Markdown content containing image references (e.g., issue description, comment body)\n\nlinear_save_diff_comment\n  Create, reply to, or edit a comment or persisted draft on a Linear diff. Set draft to true to save without submitting. Provide draftId to edit or submit a persisted draft, and commentId only to edit a submitted comment. Submitting an inline draft reuses its saved anchor; submitting a reply draft requires parentId again.\n\n  Parameters:\n    urlOrId (string) - Linear review URL, diff slug, pull request ID, Linear full identifier, or GitHub PR URL [minLength: 1]\n    commentId (string) - Existing comment ID to edit\n    draftId (string) - Existing persisted draft ID to edit or submit\n    draft (boolean) - Save as a private persisted draft without submitting [default: false]\n    parentId (string) - Top-level comment ID to reply to; also required when submitting a persisted reply draft\n    body (string) *required* - Content as Markdown. Do not escape the string — use literal newlines and special characters, not escape sequences [minLength: 1]\n    anchor (object) - Optional comment anchor copied from a diff thread or built for a file or diff hunk\n    anchorContent (string) - Exact source text of the anchor's end line; stored with an inline draft so it can be re-anchored after the diff receives new revisions\n\nlinear_resolve_diff_thread\n  Resolve or reopen a top-level comment thread on a Linear diff\n\n  Parameters:\n    threadId (string) *required* - Top-level diff thread/comment ID [minLength: 1]\n    resolved (boolean) - True to resolve the thread; false to reopen it [default: true]\n\nlinear_delete_diff_comment\n  Delete a comment or persisted draft from a Linear diff\n\n  Parameters:\n    commentId (string) - Submitted diff comment ID to delete [minLength: 1]\n    draftId (string) - Persisted diff comment draft ID to delete [minLength: 1]\n\nlinear_submit_diff_review\n  Approve a Linear diff, request changes, or submit a review comment\n\n  Parameters:\n    urlOrId (string) *required* - Linear review URL, diff slug, pull request ID, Linear full identifier, or GitHub PR URL [minLength: 1]\n    decision (enum: \"approved\", \"changesRequested\", \"commented\") *required* - Review decision: approved, changesRequested, or commented\n    body (string) - Content as Markdown. Do not escape the string — use literal newlines and special characters, not escape sequences. Required when requesting changes or commenting [minLength: 1]"}],"details":{"mode":"search","matches":[{"server":"linear","tool":"linear_get_attachment"},{"server":"linear","tool":"linear_list_comments"},{"server":"linear","tool":"linear_save_comment"},{"server":"linear","tool":"linear_delete_comment"},{"server":"linear","tool":"linear_extract_images"},{"server":"linear","tool":"linear_save_diff_comment"},{"server":"linear","tool":"linear_resolve_diff_thread"},{"server":"linear","tool":"linear_delete_diff_comment"},{"server":"linear","tool":"linear_submit_diff_review"}],"count":9,"query":"comment"},"isError":false,"durationMs":1,"timestamp":1792212521146}}
{"type":"message","id":"bb7f7d71","parentId":"8d68cb90","timestamp":"2026-10-17T04:48:41.146Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_a7fb52f4e272489a802415f7f4c7485a|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad2fe2722a88191b6d3fc84c601120a","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"files\":[{\"filename\":\"spec/entities_security_spec.js\",\"patch\":\"@@ -536,6 +536,17 @@ describe(\\\"XMLParser entity expansion security\\\", function () {\\n \\n       expect(result.root).toEqual('A'.repeat(500));\\n     });\\n+\\n+    it(\\\"should throw error when DOCTYPE is repeated\\\", function () {\\n+      const xmlData = `\\u003c!DOCTYPE root [\\u003c!ENTITY e \\\"a\\\"\\u003e]\\u003e\\u003c!DOCTYPE root2 [\\u003c!ENTITY e2 \\\"b\\\"\\u003e]\\u003e\\u003croot\\u003ea\\u003c/root\\u003e`;\\n+\\n+      const options = {\\n+      };\\n+      const parser = new XMLParser(options);\\n+      expect(() =\\u003e {\\n+        parser.parse(xmlData);\\n+      }).toThrowError(\\\"Multiple DOCTYPE declarations found.\\\");\\n+    });\\n   });\\n \\n   // =================================================================\"},{\"filename\":\"src/xmlparser/OrderedObjParser.js\",\"patch\":\"@@ -87,6 +87,7 @@ export default class OrderedObjParser {\\n     this.ignoreAttributesFn = getIgnoreAttributesFn(this.options.ignoreAttributes)\\n     this.entityExpansionCount = 0;\\n     this.currentExpandedLength = 0;\\n+    this.doctypefound = false;\\n     let namedEntities = { ...XML };\\n     if (this.options.entityDecoder) {\\n       this.entityDecoder = this.options.entityDecoder\\n@@ -294,6 +295,7 @@ const parseXml = function (xmlData) {\\n   // Reset entity expansion counters for this document\\n   this.entityExpansionCount = 0;\\n   this.currentExpandedLength = 0;\\n+  this.doctypefound = false;\\n   const options = this.options;\\n   const docTypeReader = new DocTypeReader(options.processEntities);\\n   const xmlLen = xmlData.length;\\n@@ -378,6 +380,8 @@ const parseXml = function (xmlData) {\\n         i = endIndex;\\n       } else if (c1 === 33\\n         \\u0026\\u0026 xmlData.charCodeAt(i + 2) === 68) { //'!D'\\n+        if (this.doctypefound) throw new Error(\\\"Multiple DOCTYPE declarations found.\\\");\\n+        this.doctypefound = true;\\n         const result = docTypeReader.readDocType(xmlData, i);\\n         this.entityDecoder.addInputEntities(result.entities);\\n         i = result.i;\"}],\"sha\":\"4e546e03987662de5495d050b5fba26bea65383f\"}\n{\"files\":[{\"filename\":\"packages/argv-parser/src/env/parse-env.ts\",\"patch\":\"@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@ const GitEnvKeys = {\\n    'pager': 'allowUnsafePager',\\n    'prefix': 'allowUnsafeConfigPaths',\\n    'ssh_askpass': 'allowUnsafeAskPass',\\n+   'visual': 'allowUnsafeEditor',\\n } as const satisfies Record\\u003cstring, VulnerabilityCategory\\u003e;\\n \\n type GitEnv = Record\\u003cstring, string\\u003e \\u0026 {\"}],\"sha\":\"68874c239f0c7a87f4a68c3d2c4a0d7c75bb27f4\"}\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":1908,"timestamp":1792212521146}}
