GU1-jn_Cgfa7AgvMtBS1Rw1G0nQG-1FQMnu8gwkxKpFFAwwd-3H9-dDzMRTKl90Gz031VSzTpwBfMsOZA1pp8mFZgDPflvrpS1RuHpifrUAdSeCm7rUEUB9aD0RWkiYU5qwgxXd0NUFsnoM0iKSX24v0Yy9Iv5fSeipd7OubVG6uxfNr6E_UlB0SB6ku3pbM2ndNQSBE_AMLUEMmQi54JKcrnAU4UwmWW9teolpJAeOs5DJEfAra1gO5mGlDUqvfUs2r9nswMjg8W8N5WapQUSrgruYIKNaivrLCzcOsSOTjf1EwvY8H27N28MS1qZ6TUtuBhdmaY0MDh8nUVqBlR_1yeoXWaqfkjU0Rdubf0mHIJ730Bp5jHJdTPCSi6cerAQ-5KNBfUAySHxdjrrxAJFgvkTbSpfiZ4gEFOAFTrReUfAyFCqvlCKsMM6HnHPi_4yemYd1qhwCeLKlk7mv25oeH1G6bly-URFjft7MQEvw-o_qvl8xDOwCnLwb5gBHUW4mMIRmXFsAiauz06TXy16hxSrEMy78E421mpChFu2sljwusJgQzknpuqqIwVhcWFFFXMByyBQtniRRT9upjHF3ircbJt78Yde3CkS3DbRrnL20JbYmgISnHWZoXWuinq0N8G3R3ZrIeyutS14x_4_7LiIoFiO0S-OoLULgNQitJb7j9EPwtnqDMqJ2KwzEfZCgcdwNqrXc00IRri9-HYLFYOPU4TQTxgvtr8W7HPX65blydI7eup3g7QZinRWFKHGzZYxGM8cnVeSzZveHfe9aHLtEyrU-cacg6BJ0AytFM9PObYXmBqLtf2f80JLubxnHsB2oJOvCCHElVZa8WezeUvZMhZVmGjsUmOasGPSFy4WHGHnAAIIassXtbCunPHu7AOQ==\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_1e1f175789174d67aefc454737554b48|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad2fef0eda48191af9622ed71394eb5","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/Users/alex/.local/state/herdr/orchestrations/security-followups-20261017/assessment.md","content":"# COR-2145 and COR-2164 — parent assessment\n\nResearch snapshot: entireio/entire-brain immutable main `c8624c8826e4d2632510b46041a54694a0504650`, still the directly observed main head on final source review, 2026-10-17. Investigation only: no project source changes, installs, builds, third-party code execution, payloads, CI reruns, upstream posts, or global tool/config/auth changes. Both vulnerabilities remain open; this is not security clearance.\n\n## COR-2145: CI XML denial of service, not demonstrated code execution\n\nCurrent setup-go `@v7` resolves to official commit `b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e`. Its shipped entrypoint has Git blob SHA `187253e6f2118f85ec516374beed40d983a70015`, independently reproduced from the downloaded bytes. Runtime lock includes fast-xml-parser5.9.3. GitHub GHSA-8r6m-32jq-jx6q is active HIGH, affected>=5.9.3,<5.10.1, fixed5.10.1. Impact described by upstream is excessive CPU/memory, event-loop blocking and process termination, not a demonstrated secret-extraction/code-execution vulnerability.\n\nActual relevant dataflow, now narrowed beyond the child reports:\n\n1. setup-go action.yml defaults `cache:true`; both current workflow files omit an override at inspected setup steps, including the publishing nightly job (contents:write). Low default test permissions are not proof of parser safety.\n2. setup-go src/main.ts invokes cache restore only when its cache Boolean is true; src/cache-save.ts similarly guards the post-step save. Installer manifests are JSON and Go payloads are archives, not parser XML.\n3. @actions/cache6.2.0 has an Azure SDK download path (`lib/internal/downloadUtils.js`, `downloadCacheStorageSDK`: BlockBlobClient.getProperties/downloadToBuffer) and upload path (`uploadUtils.js`, `uploadCacheArchiveSDK`: BlobClient.getBlockBlobClient().uploadFile). These are service-operation paths, not XML parsing of the cache archive itself. Backend/download selection still conditions which route executes in a particular job; no live CI traffic capture was performed.\n4. Exact @azure/storage-blob12.32.0 `StorageClient.js` builds StorageContextClient with `getCoreClientOptions`. Its `Pipeline.js` imports core-xml.parseXML and explicitly wires it into createClientPipeline's deserializationOptions. Generated BlobImpl uses sendOperationRequest; download success 200/206 has a Stream mapper, default errors have StorageError; getProperties is HEAD.\n5. Exact @azure/core-client1.10.2 `deserializationPolicy.js` parses a nonempty non-stream response body only according to Content-Type. application/xml / application/atom+xml invoke the injected parseXML callback, before error mapping. Thus an XML *service/error response*, unlike a streamed success archive, can reach the wrapper.\n6. @azure/core-xml1.5.1 `dist/esm/xml.js` calls XMLValidator.validate, then XMLParser with processEntities:true. Validation alone is not a demonstrated mitigation: inspected fast-xml-parser v5.9.3 src/validator.js skips each DOCTYPE with readCommentAndCDATA and has no document-wide duplicate-DOCTYPE rejection. No vulnerable parser was executed.\n\nThe storage-blob and core-client archives were fetched from official npm registry as static data; SHA512 integrity matches the exact setup-go lock. Archive members were read to stdout into owned evidence files, never installed or executed. This closes the child report's missing pipeline-to-XML callback edge. It does NOT establish that an untrusted PR author can supply arbitrary XML service replies. No route was found from repository content/cache archive bytes to the XML body. Changing a service endpoint/proxy/runner environment or controlling a relevant service response could change that threat model; no such capability was demonstrated for contributors here. Service-side reflection and all runner/network configurations were not exhaustively proved safe.\n\nPatch proof: advisory-linked commit [4e546e03987662de5495d050b5fba26bea65383f](https://github.com/NaturalIntelligence/fast-xml-parser/commit/4e546e03987662de5495d050b5fba26bea65383f) adds a per-document doctypefound flag, throws on the second declaration and adds a regression test. This is the authoritative patch, superseding the child's unrelated/uncorrelated historical 57ad... reference.\n\nRelease/fix disposition: current newest official setup-go release is still v7.0.0, whose v7 bundle remains affected. No fixed official v7 release was verified. Exact old v6.4.0 lock has parser5.4.1; official v6.5.0 has5.8.0/cache5.1.0, outside THIS GHSA's range. They are not parser5.10.1 fixes or universally security-cleared replacements, and rollback compatibility/full bundle assessment was not established. Do not rewrite upstream bundles.\n\nRecommendation: keep upstream bundle remediation open. If immediate containment is desired, a separately reviewed `cache:false` change bypasses the observed restore and post-save branches without changing Go1.27.2; it leaves the vulnerable code bundled and costs caching performance, so is a mitigation rather than a package fix or a blanket elimination proof. Prefer an official action release whose shipped bundle actually contains the fix when available.\n\nSources: [GHSA](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-8r6m-32jq-jx6q), [action metadata](https://github.com/actions/setup-go/blob/b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e/action.yml), [main](https://github.com/actions/setup-go/blob/b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e/src/main.ts), [post-save](https://github.com/actions/setup-go/blob/b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e/src/cache-save.ts), [validator](https://github.com/NaturalIntelligence/fast-xml-parser/blob/v5.9.3/src/validator.js), [v7 release](https://github.com/actions/setup-go/releases/tag/v7.0.0), [v6.5 release](https://github.com/actions/setup-go/releases/tag/v6.5.0). Exact SDK members and integrity verifier are retained beside this report.\n\n## COR-2164: inherited Git tooling guard bypasses; no embedding-request path found\n\nCurrent locked chain is node-llama-cpp3.22.1 -> simple-git3.36.0 -> scoped @simple-git/argv-parser1.1.1. Parent independently checked all three downloaded npm tarballs against the project's lock SHA512 integrity: all match. This concern was inherited, not introduced by the dependency update.\n\nGitHub global advisory API confirms all four are active, not withdrawn:\n\n| Advisory | Component/range | Fix | Required operation/input |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [v5rq-49vh-5v5c](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c), CRITICAL | scoped parser<2.0.1 | parser2.0.1 | Attacker-influenced VISUAL environment plus an editor-opening Git command and applicable editor/TERM precedence |\n| [858h-whjf-mvg5](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-858h-whjf-mvg5), HIGH | simple-git<=3.36.0 |4.0.0| Unsafe abbreviated push receive-pack/exec options |\n| [g4wm-2vf7-vfgr](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-g4wm-2vf7-vfgr), HIGH | simple-git<=3.36.0 |4.0.0| Untrusted clone config include/includeIf (plus readable attacker config), or config-resolution environment |\n| [x6jw-m9v5-85vh](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-x6jw-m9v5-85vh), CRITICAL | simple-git>=3.15.0,<4.0.1 |4.0.1| Untrusted trailer command config with interpret-trailers operation |\n\nThe earlier child used guessed repository-specific advisory endpoints and got404. These were corrected with `/advisories/<id>`; network/auth was functional. Current structured affected ranges/fixed versions win over stale descriptive text saying no remediation existed.\n\nObserved callers: node-llama-cpp clone utilities use fixed clone options (depth, branch, optional recursive, quiet), fixed HTTPS GitHub URL construction or package bundle paths, and removeRemote; release-bundle utilities use repository/history operations with explicit messages, not an observed editor-opening command. No observed push with arbitrary receive-pack/exec options or interpret-trailers/untrusted config inclusion was established. Source inspection is not an exhaustive all-operations proof.\n\nImportant correction to the child's summary: Git is NOT confined to explicit developer CLI commands, and prebuilt use is not guaranteed. Published getLlama.js defaults build to auto outside Electron; when no usable binary exists, it can build from source. OnPostInstallCommand.js also invokes getLlamaForOptions with default build behavior unless skip configuration is selected. Thus installation AND server-startup fallback can reach source-download/build tooling. Request text enters embedding only after initialization; no observed path carries HTTP embedding text/model contents into Git arguments/environment. Repository/ref configuration is installer/operator/environment input in the inspected path, not an embedding request field.\n\nThis narrows the supported exposure claim: vulnerable guard code is present and Git tooling can run, but no attacker-controlled application input satisfying these four advisory conditions was demonstrated. Do not call the package globally safe, or assume all CI/config input is trusted. The exact postinstall/startup behavior and fixed clone options were independently read by the parent after the child reports.\n\nPatch proof: [68874c239f0c7a87f4a68c3d2c4a0d7c75bb27f4](https://github.com/steveukx/git-js/commit/68874c239f0c7a87f4a68c3d2c4a0d7c75bb27f4) adds `visual:allowUnsafeEditor` to the parser environment classification. No payload or updated package was executed.\n\nCurrent official remediation state, verified against npm complete version metadata: latest stable simple-git3.x is still3.36.0. Latest simple-git is4.0.2 with parser2.0.1. Latest node-llama-cpp3.22.2 still declares simple-git^3.36.0, excluding4.x. Therefore a normal node-llama-cpp patch update does NOT fix these advisories, and no published compatible simple-git3.x patch route was found. The child's statement that a compatible route already exists is withdrawn; it was only an unverified option.\n\nRecommendation: pursue a maintained official node-llama-cpp release adopting the corrected Git stack, or a maintainer-backed simple-git3.x security backport. Do not blindly force4.x or override parser2.x without API/contract evidence and focused verification. Prebuilt-only/fail-closed installation/startup is a possible separately reviewed mitigation, not a proven universally compatible change; it must cover postinstall AND runtime fallback and preserve benchmark provenance/pins. No benchmark engine or historical evidence was changed.\n\n## Final disposition\n\nResearch complete with explicit limits; vulnerabilities not remediated and issues not closed. No exploit demonstrated in these workflows/benchmark inputs. Available immediate options are bounded mitigations or upstream coordination, not a verified one-command compatible fix. No new background watch or workspace is required. First child reports are partial historical inputs, not accepted standalone conclusions. Parent synthesis above supersedes unsupported summaries. Source-tree changes remain zero; unrelated .pi/subagents runtime is preserved.\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","usage":{"input":2364,"output":3672,"cacheRead":140416,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1034,"totalTokens":146452,"cost":{"input":0.0047279999999999996,"output":0.03672,"cacheRead":0.014041600000000001,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0554896}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792212698750,"responseId":"resp_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad2fedb76a88191b71dd1956639ee0a","rawStopReason":"completed","durationMs":57376,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}}
