nf6HPvb8lwXIVCW_akzcQIXMoWvEuOINlhRbmJ9JLqaic_qeAw-lOLGksjXq239dkoojavEH7nqwDRin3JSIh5oIuj3pznugfYlf-t8RycD3t0AOD0aEX6lMRcHoCO_0niHAPpCn87eqA_K2no0TmaUeNE-CdavWIbc8bU_13Or4BkyJRJv4USMIfY-UwmdExcA7KoY_v5xamLv-1i5wp8svFk-enJxmopWCUL-tORzn4QheiAx-zIYUvxhNfEg35NUqHhzaXJ7aeS5zgTxUoWBET7sNvcHiBSL2ZUN24HWDYGJD4TTYfqoU_8Mlo340LqP9kdgtxCK5qpzZrX8XS3yAqYQ99d91VTWtNfg2_bRbzsp1BfCGnY25GHbyg0oTsWRbSjl3PcZ5ShMNGPLvNIkwy4kWhJJ2PBi0qpb_AumEtPqWe4g-ublB7vfJ5N1zRb7r1VaUc3YBNdpa55RuHO_u97AG2jJX87GTRGZDzbl9XmnektrSxcGmPovyBo6TxpHSvlZtVGBGN8aH1gfjfWxENV7CEA52AJ4T5nxhwSIjs1vnIZsZxMFmUzKmSsRECtpD4gR4I-dD1k2LW-fHrwX_ZjinDQ7QgGsUn62SMx9ydQDYqOZ_JyihKUWUvlplVws5_fmS4-3tqPZR2TzdQ9K_F84HK18JekGQLFepY2gEqnYOlTAu3UtDrdiwtANmOqJscWyX6aqjEWQ2WO1ARzMZ__CKTJfRihk_xc-uuGrUhI6Y-vpDWNoa7uGSB_Up3wAH45EtYp4jD1O2We0h_x8-2Sfq51x77jO98lFsJISBA_R6YDuy1cy96lpAmM9ax9dr-fckEuuRYceXDchZ8DHFuitjrpaEZWFEQDzHclH0pjCnfVDR6GfCgMtOO3ahgg-qPpc1TRHqW3t2f4HK0nbVXMVLWox0tPPirmfcae-E1RfAeqM44EhNgQ9E_gMN-jUgIMNSCVh52A8sGj0VgzDfw9JIpqpKWs56O-rX2TRIevIAtpz1VDOAOG-KUdjI_0W0gcmJvh4OoXTGLGYYp60sbHsQuHDmeO7pm6nglavr0k1vLFbDBoaAFevRXyZ-gjLkKDF2Ab_Oy428cIsVncFVbFRbLXHnTKFyHNNDTzibaKj\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_250f630defb842fb9de67ce89317fc06|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad2ff3202fc81919069271d95d79433","name":"mcp","arguments":{"tool":"linear_save_comment","args":{"issueId":"COR-2145","body":"## Deeper assessment — 2026-10-17 (investigation only)\n\nReviewed immutable current main `c8624c8826e4d2632510b46041a54694a0504650`. Vulnerable code remains present; this issue is not resolved.\n\n* `setup-go@v7` still resolves to `b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e`, with parser5.9.3. Official latest action release is still v7.0.0; no fixed v7 bundle was verified. Shipped bundle Git blob hash independently matches the official API object.\n* The advisory is a **CPU/memory denial-of-service** flaw, not demonstrated secret extraction/RCE. Authoritative fix [4e546e0](https://github.com/NaturalIntelligence/fast-xml-parser/commit/4e546e03987662de5495d050b5fba26bea65383f) rejects a second DOCTYPE and adds regression coverage.\n* The relevant XML is an SDK **service/error response**, not repository files or cache archive bytes. Static source trace: cache SDK download/upload clients → storage-blob Pipeline deserializationOptions.parseXML → core-client non-stream XML Content-Type response parsing → core-xml XMLValidator then entity-enabled XMLParser. Exact storage-blob12.32.0/core-client1.10.2 archive SHA512s match the action lock. Successful blob downloads are streamed; HEAD has no normal body. Backend/download selection conditions the executed route.\n* XML prevalidation is not established as mitigation: parser5.9.3 validator skips each DOCTYPE without a document-wide duplicate guard. No payload was executed.\n* Cache defaults true, including inspected setup steps in the publishing nightly job. No route was found by which a PR contributor supplies arbitrary XML service replies. That attacker-control edge remains unproven; do not call it unreachable or security-cleared. Runner/proxy/endpoint/service trust is material.\n\n**Recommendation:** retain upstream bundled-dependency remediation. If immediate containment is wanted, separately review `cache:false`: source guards both restore and post-save, while preserving Go1.27.2. This bypasses the observed cache branch, costs cache performance and does not remove the vulnerable bundle. Prefer an official patched bundle when available; do not vendor-edit it. v6.5.0 uses parser5.8.0 (outside this GHSA), but rollback compatibility and overall safety were not established, so no automatic downgrade recommendation.\n\nNo code/dependency/CI/admin changes, installs, builds or exploit execution. Research handoff only; remediation awaits a decision/upstream release.\n\nSources: [advisory](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-8r6m-32jq-jx6q), [action metadata](https://github.com/actions/setup-go/blob/b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e/action.yml), [cache guards](https://github.com/actions/setup-go/blob/b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e/src/cache-save.ts), [v7 release](https://github.com/actions/setup-go/releases/tag/v7.0.0)."}}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_b5ad4f14015b4cf0b95a3257e6afdda3|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad2ff4475e48191b9425e8d3f7face6","name":"mcp","arguments":{"tool":"linear_save_comment","args":{"issueId":"COR-2164","body":"## Deeper assessment — 2026-10-17 (investigation only)\n\nCurrent immutable main `c8624c8826e4d2632510b46041a54694a0504650` still locks node-llama-cpp3.22.1 → simple-git3.36.0 → scoped @simple-git/argv-parser1.1.1. All three inspected npm archive SHA512s independently match the project lock. This remains inherited, not an introduced update regression; issue is not resolved.\n\n**Exposure:** Git can run during npm postinstall AND automatic server-startup source-build fallback. The initial suggestion that ordinary runtime necessarily uses prebuilts was too strong: published getLlama defaults build:auto; postinstall invokes the same default build selection. Embedding request text reaches inference after initialization, not observed Git flags/environment. Inspected cloning/history callers use fixed clone options and explicit messages; no editor-opening call with attacker-controlled VISUAL was established. Installer/operator/CI environment and repo configuration remain trust boundaries; this is not proof of universal non-reachability.\n\nCorrect global GitHub advisory endpoints confirm four active findings:\n\n* [GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c): CRITICAL parser<2.0.1, fixed2.0.1; untrusted VISUAL plus editor-opening operation and applicable editor/TERM settings. [Actual patch](https://github.com/steveukx/git-js/commit/68874c239f0c7a87f4a68c3d2c4a0d7c75bb27f4) adds VISUAL classification.\n* [GHSA-858h-whjf-mvg5](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-858h-whjf-mvg5): HIGH simple-git<=3.36.0, fixed4.0.0; unsafe abbreviated push options.\n* [GHSA-g4wm-2vf7-vfgr](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-g4wm-2vf7-vfgr): HIGH same range/fix; untrusted clone configuration includes/config-resolution environment.\n* [GHSA-x6jw-m9v5-85vh](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-x6jw-m9v5-85vh): CRITICAL >=3.15.0,<4.0.1; untrusted trailer-command config plus interpret-trailers.\n\nNo current benchmark-input path satisfying these conditions was demonstrated. Not an exhaustive all-callers/CI-config audit or exploit proof.\n\n**Fix status:** full npm version metadata confirms newest stable simple-git3.x remains3.36.0. Current simple-git4.0.2 includes parser2.0.1. Latest node-llama-cpp3.22.2 STILL requires simple-git^3.36.0, excluding4.x. Therefore merely updating node-llama-cpp to its latest patch does NOT fix this; a compatible published3.x fix route was not found.\n\n**Recommendation:** maintained official parent update adopting the corrected Git stack, or maintainer-backed3.x security backport. No blind4.x/parser override. A prebuilt-only mitigation would need to cover BOTH installation and runtime fallback, supported-platform failure behavior, and benchmark provenance/pins; none was implemented or declared compatible.\n\nNo project source/pin changes, installs, builds, third-party execution or payloads. Research complete with explicit limits; remediation awaits decision/upstream support."}}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_24cb9f4b7ca744e8ad5b2143a2b79780|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad2ff4475e48191bde890e5cfb8dac3","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/Users/alex/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-plugins-official/superpowers/6.4.1/skills/verification-before-completion/SKILL.md","offset":null,"limit":null}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","usage":{"input":3895,"output":2931,"cacheRead":142592,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1341,"totalTokens":149418,"cost":{"input":0.00779,"output":0.029310000000000003,"cacheRead":0.014259200000000001,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0513592}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792212756437,"responseId":"resp_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad2ff1533e481919ae249df3b2da28b","rawStopReason":"completed","durationMs":48586,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}}
{"type":"message","id":"80117a3f","parentId":"638e04cd","timestamp":"2026-10-17T04:53:28.668Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_250f630defb842fb9de67ce89317fc06|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad2ff3202fc81919069271d95d79433","toolName":"mcp","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"ee015d94-8872-4627-87ab-83298e09e527\",\"body\":\"## Deeper assessment — 2026-10-17 (investigation only)\\n\\nReviewed immutable current main `c8624c8826e4d2632510b46041a54694a0504650`. Vulnerable code remains present; this issue is not resolved.\\n\\n* `setup-go@v7` still resolves to `b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e`, with parser5.9.3. Official latest action release is still v7.0.0; no fixed v7 bundle was verified. Shipped bundle Git blob hash independently matches the official API object.\\n* The advisory is a **CPU/memory denial-of-service** flaw, not demonstrated secret extraction/RCE. Authoritative fix [4e546e0](https://github.com/NaturalIntelligence/fast-xml-parser/commit/4e546e03987662de5495d050b5fba26bea65383f) rejects a second DOCTYPE and adds regression coverage.\\n* The relevant XML is an SDK **service/error response**, not repository files or cache archive bytes. Static source trace: cache SDK download/upload clients → storage-blob Pipeline deserializationOptions.parseXML → core-client non-stream XML Content-Type response parsing → core-xml XMLValidator then entity-enabled XMLParser. Exact storage-blob12.32.0/core-client1.10.2 archive SHA512s match the action lock. Successful blob downloads are streamed; HEAD has no normal body. Backend/download selection conditions the executed route.\\n* XML prevalidation is not established as mitigation: parser5.9.3 validator skips each DOCTYPE without a document-wide duplicate guard. No payload was executed.\\n* Cache defaults true, including inspected setup steps in the publishing nightly job. No route was found by which a PR contributor supplies arbitrary XML service replies. That attacker-control edge remains unproven; do not call it unreachable or security-cleared. Runner/proxy/endpoint/service trust is material.\\n\\n**Recommendation:** retain upstream bundled-dependency remediation. If immediate containment is wanted, separately review `cache:false`: source guards both restore and post-save, while preserving Go1.27.2. This bypasses the observed cache branch, costs cache performance and does not remove the vulnerable bundle. Prefer an official patched bundle when available; do not vendor-edit it. v6.5.0 uses parser5.8.0 (outside this GHSA), but rollback compatibility and overall safety were not established, so no automatic downgrade recommendation.\\n\\nNo code/dependency/CI/admin changes, installs, builds or exploit execution. Research handoff only; remediation awaits a decision/upstream release.\\n\\nSources: [advisory](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-8r6m-32jq-jx6q), [action metadata](https://github.com/actions/setup-go/blob/b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e/action.yml), [cache guards](https://github.com/actions/setup-go/blob/b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e/src/cache-save.ts), [v7 release](https://github.com/actions/setup-go/releases/tag/v7.0.0).\",\"attachments\":[],\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-17T04:53:26.567Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-17T04:53:26.542Z\",\"parentId\":null,\"resolvedAt\":null,\"quotedText\":null,\"author\":{\"id\":\"45a00cf6-3a37-45ab-a508-d9da7f9d514c\",\"name\":\"Alex Ong\"},\"onBehalfOf\":null}"}],"details":{"mode":"call","mcpResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"ee015d94-8872-4627-87ab-83298e09e527\",\"body\":\"## Deeper assessment — 2026-10-17 (investigation only)\\n\\nReviewed immutable current main `c8624c8826e4d2632510b46041a54694a0504650`. Vulnerable code remains present; this issue is not resolved.\\n\\n* `setup-go@v7` still resolves to `b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e`, with parser5.9.3. Official latest action release is still v7.0.0; no fixed v7 bundle was verified. Shipped bundle Git blob hash independently matches the official API object.\\n* The advisory is a **CPU/memory denial-of-service** flaw, not demonstrated secret extraction/RCE. Authoritative fix [4e546e0](https://github.com/NaturalIntelligence/fast-xml-parser/commit/4e546e03987662de5495d050b5fba26bea65383f) rejects a second DOCTYPE and adds regression coverage.\\n* The relevant XML is an SDK **service/error response**, not repository files or cache archive bytes. Static source trace: cache SDK download/upload clients → storage-blob Pipeline deserializationOptions.parseXML → core-client non-stream XML Content-Type response parsing → core-xml XMLValidator then entity-enabled XMLParser. Exact storage-blob12.32.0/core-client1.10.2 archive SHA512s match the action lock. Successful blob downloads are streamed; HEAD has no normal body. Backend/download selection conditions the executed route.\\n* XML prevalidation is not established as mitigation: parser5.9.3 validator skips each DOCTYPE without a document-wide duplicate guard. No payload was executed.\\n* Cache defaults true, including inspected setup steps in the publishing nightly job. No route was found by which a PR contributor supplies arbitrary XML service replies. That attacker-control edge remains unproven; do not call it unreachable or security-cleared. Runner/proxy/endpoint/service trust is material.\\n\\n**Recommendation:** retain upstream bundled-dependency remediation. If immediate containment is wanted, separately review `cache:false`: source guards both restore and post-save, while preserving Go1.27.2. This bypasses the observed cache branch, costs cache performance and does not remove the vulnerable bundle. Prefer an official patched bundle when available; do not vendor-edit it. v6.5.0 uses parser5.8.0 (outside this GHSA), but rollback compatibility and overall safety were not established, so no automatic downgrade recommendation.\\n\\nNo code/dependency/CI/admin changes, installs, builds or exploit execution. Research handoff only; remediation awaits a decision/upstream release.\\n\\nSources: [advisory](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-8r6m-32jq-jx6q), [action metadata](https://github.com/actions/setup-go/blob/b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e/action.yml), [cache guards](https://github.com/actions/setup-go/blob/b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e/src/cache-save.ts), [v7 release](https://github.com/actions/setup-go/releases/tag/v7.0.0).\",\"attachments\":[],\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-17T04:53:26.567Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-17T04:53:26.542Z\",\"parentId\":null,\"resolvedAt\":null,\"quotedText\":null,\"author\":{\"id\":\"45a00cf6-3a37-45ab-a508-d9da7f9d514c\",\"name\":\"Alex Ong\"},\"onBehalfOf\":null}"}]},"server":"linear","tool":"save_comment"},"isError":false,"durationMs":1987,"timestamp":1792212808668}}
{"type":"message","id":"2b7cb399","parentId":"80117a3f","timestamp":"2026-10-17T04:53:28.669Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_b5ad4f14015b4cf0b95a3257e6afdda3|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad2ff4475e48191b9425e8d3f7face6","toolName":"mcp","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"0c5301ec-b969-4393-b4b6-65376f49ccf4\",\"body\":\"## Deeper assessment — 2026-10-17 (investigation only)\\n\\nCurrent immutable main `c8624c8826e4d2632510b46041a54694a0504650` still locks node-llama-cpp3.22.1 → simple-git3.36.0 → scoped @simple-git/argv-parser1.1.1. All three inspected npm archive SHA512s independently match the project lock. This remains inherited, not an introduced update regression; issue is not resolved.\\n\\n**Exposure:** Git can run during npm postinstall AND automatic server-startup source-build fallback. The initial suggestion that ordinary runtime necessarily uses prebuilts was too strong: published getLlama defaults build:auto; postinstall invokes the same default build selection. Embedding request text reaches inference after initialization, not observed Git flags/environment. Inspected cloning/history callers use fixed clone options and explicit messages; no editor-opening call with attacker-controlled VISUAL was established. Installer/operator/CI environment and repo configuration remain trust boundaries; this is not proof of universal non-reachability.\\n\\nCorrect global GitHub advisory endpoints confirm four active findings:\\n\\n* [GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c): CRITICAL parser<2.0.1, fixed2.0.1; untrusted VISUAL plus editor-opening operation and applicable editor/TERM settings. [Actual patch](https://github.com/steveukx/git-js/commit/68874c239f0c7a87f4a68c3d2c4a0d7c75bb27f4) adds VISUAL classification.\\n* [GHSA-858h-whjf-mvg5](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-858h-whjf-mvg5): HIGH simple-git<=3.36.0, fixed4.0.0; unsafe abbreviated push options.\\n* [GHSA-g4wm-2vf7-vfgr](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-g4wm-2vf7-vfgr): HIGH same range/fix; untrusted clone configuration includes/config-resolution environment.\\n* [GHSA-x6jw-m9v5-85vh](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-x6jw-m9v5-85vh): CRITICAL >=3.15.0,<4.0.1; untrusted trailer-command config plus interpret-trailers.\\n\\nNo current benchmark-input path satisfying these conditions was demonstrated. Not an exhaustive all-callers/CI-config audit or exploit proof.\\n\\n**Fix status:** full npm version metadata confirms newest stable simple-git3.x remains3.36.0. Current simple-git4.0.2 includes parser2.0.1. Latest node-llama-cpp3.22.2 STILL requires simple-git^3.36.0, excluding4.x. Therefore merely updating node-llama-cpp to its latest patch does NOT fix this; a compatible published3.x fix route was not found.\\n\\n**Recommendation:** maintained official parent update adopting the corrected Git stack, or maintainer-backed3.x security backport. No blind4.x/parser override. A prebuilt-only mitigation would need to cover BOTH installation and runtime fallback, supported-platform failure behavior, and benchmark provenance/pins; none was implemented or declared compatible.\\n\\nNo project source/pin changes, installs, builds, third-party execution or payloads. Research complete with explicit limits; remediation awaits decision/upstream support.\",\"attachments\":[],\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-17T04:53:28.020Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-17T04:53:27.568Z\",\"parentId\":null,\"resolvedAt\":null,\"quotedText\":null,\"author\":{\"id\":\"45a00cf6-3a37-45ab-a508-d9da7f9d514c\",\"name\":\"Alex Ong\"},\"onBehalfOf\":null}"}],"details":{"mode":"call","mcpResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"0c5301ec-b969-4393-b4b6-65376f49ccf4\",\"body\":\"## Deeper assessment — 2026-10-17 (investigation only)\\n\\nCurrent immutable main `c8624c8826e4d2632510b46041a54694a0504650` still locks node-llama-cpp3.22.1 → simple-git3.36.0 → scoped @simple-git/argv-parser1.1.1. All three inspected npm archive SHA512s independently match the project lock. This remains inherited, not an introduced update regression; issue is not resolved.\\n\\n**Exposure:** Git can run during npm postinstall AND automatic server-startup source-build fallback. The initial suggestion that ordinary runtime necessarily uses prebuilts was too strong: published getLlama defaults build:auto; postinstall invokes the same default build selection. Embedding request text reaches inference after initialization, not observed Git flags/environment. Inspected cloning/history callers use fixed clone options and explicit messages; no editor-opening call with attacker-controlled VISUAL was established. Installer/operator/CI environment and repo configuration remain trust boundaries; this is not proof of universal non-reachability.\\n\\nCorrect global GitHub advisory endpoints confirm four active findings:\\n\\n* [GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c): CRITICAL parser<2.0.1, fixed2.0.1; untrusted VISUAL plus editor-opening operation and applicable editor/TERM settings. [Actual patch](https://github.com/steveukx/git-js/commit/68874c239f0c7a87f4a68c3d2c4a0d7c75bb27f4) adds VISUAL classification.\\n* [GHSA-858h-whjf-mvg5](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-858h-whjf-mvg5): HIGH simple-git<=3.36.0, fixed4.0.0; unsafe abbreviated push options.\\n* [GHSA-g4wm-2vf7-vfgr](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-g4wm-2vf7-vfgr): HIGH same range/fix; untrusted clone configuration includes/config-resolution environment.\\n* [GHSA-x6jw-m9v5-85vh](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-x6jw-m9v5-85vh): CRITICAL >=3.15.0,<4.0.1; untrusted trailer-command config plus interpret-trailers.\\n\\nNo current benchmark-input path satisfying these conditions was demonstrated. Not an exhaustive all-callers/CI-config audit or exploit proof.\\n\\n**Fix status:** full npm version metadata confirms newest stable simple-git3.x remains3.36.0. Current simple-git4.0.2 includes parser2.0.1. Latest node-llama-cpp3.22.2 STILL requires simple-git^3.36.0, excluding4.x. Therefore merely updating node-llama-cpp to its latest patch does NOT fix this; a compatible published3.x fix route was not found.\\n\\n**Recommendation:** maintained official parent update adopting the corrected Git stack, or maintainer-backed3.x security backport. No blind4.x/parser override. A prebuilt-only mitigation would need to cover BOTH installation and runtime fallback, supported-platform failure behavior, and benchmark provenance/pins; none was implemented or declared compatible.\\n\\nNo project source/pin changes, installs, builds, third-party execution or payloads. Research complete with explicit limits; remediation awaits decision/upstream support.\",\"attachments\":[],\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-17T04:53:28.020Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-17T04:53:27.568Z\",\"parentId\":null,\"resolvedAt\":null,\"quotedText\":null,\"author\":{\"id\":\"45a00cf6-3a37-45ab-a508-d9da7f9d514c\",\"name\":\"Alex Ong\"},\"onBehalfOf\":null}"}]},"server":"linear","tool":"save_comment"},"isError":false,"durationMs":3640,"timestamp":1792212808669}}
{"type":"message","id":"ad3a0eca","parentId":"2b7cb399","timestamp":"2026-10-17T04:53:28.669Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_24cb9f4b7ca744e8ad5b2143a2b79780|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad2ff4475e48191bde890e5cfb8dac3","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: verification-before-completion\ndescription: Use when about to claim work is complete, fixed, or passing, before committing or creating PRs - requires running verification commands and confirming output before making any success claims; evidence before assertions always\n---\n\n# Verification Before Completion\n\n## Overview\n\n**Core principle:** Evidence before claims, always.\n\n**Violating the letter of this rule is violating the spirit of this rule.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO COMPLETION CLAIMS WITHOUT FRESH VERIFICATION EVIDENCE\n```\n\nIf you haven't run the verification command in this message, you cannot claim it passes.\n\n## The Gate Function\n\n```\nBEFORE claiming any status or expressing satisfaction:\n\n1. IDENTIFY: What command proves this claim?\n2. RUN: Execute the FULL command (fresh, complete)\n3. READ: Full output, check exit code, count failures\n4. VERIFY: Does output confirm the claim?\n   - If NO: State actual status with evidence\n   - If YES: State claim WITH evidence\n5. ONLY THEN: Make the claim\n\nSkip any step = lying, not verifying\n```\n\n## Common Failures\n\n| Claim | Requires | Not Sufficient |\n|-------|----------|----------------|\n| Tests pass | Test command output: 0 failures | Previous run, \"should pass\" |\n| Linter clean | Linter output: 0 errors | Partial check, extrapolation |\n| Build succeeds | Build command: exit 0 | Linter passing, logs look good |\n| Bug fixed | Test original symptom: passes | Code changed, assumed fixed |\n| Regression test works | Red-green cycle verified | Test passes once |\n| Agent completed | VCS diff shows changes | Agent reports \"success\" |\n| Requirements met | Line-by-line checklist | Tests passing |\n\n## Red Flags - STOP\n\n- Using \"should\", \"probably\", \"seems to\"\n- Expressing satisfaction before verification (\"Great!\", \"Perfect!\", \"Done!\", etc.)\n- About to commit/push/PR without verification\n- Trusting agent success reports\n- Relying on partial verification\n- Thinking \"just this once\"\n- Tired and wanting work over\n- **ANY wording implying success without having run verification**\n\n## Rationalization Prevention\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Should work now\" | RUN the verification |\n| \"I'm confident\" | Confidence ≠ evidence |\n| \"Just this once\" | No exceptions |\n| \"Linter passed\" | Linter ≠ compiler |\n| \"Agent said success\" | Verify independently |\n| \"I'm tired\" | Exhaustion ≠ excuse |\n| \"Partial check is enough\" | Partial proves nothing |\n| \"Different words so rule doesn't apply\" | Spirit over letter |\n\n## Key Patterns\n\n**Tests:**\n```\n✅ [Run test command] [See: 34/34 pass] \"All tests pass\"\n❌ \"Should pass now\" / \"Looks correct\"\n```\n\n**Regression tests (TDD Red-Green):**\n```\n✅ Write → Run (pass) → Revert fix → Run (MUST FAIL) → Restore → Run (pass)\n❌ \"I've written a regression test\" (without red-green verification)\n```\n\n**Build:**\n```\n✅ [Run build] [See: exit 0] \"Build passes\"\n❌ \"Linter passed\" (linter doesn't check compilation)\n```\n\n**Requirements:**\n```\n✅ Re-read plan → Create checklist → Verify each → Report gaps or completion\n❌ \"Tests pass, phase complete\"\n```\n\n**Agent delegation:**\n```\n✅ Agent reports success → Check VCS diff → Verify changes → Report actual state\n❌ Trust agent report\n```\n\n## When To Apply\n\n**ALWAYS before:**\n- ANY variation of success/completion claims\n- ANY expression of satisfaction\n- ANY positive statement about work state\n- Committing, PR creation, task completion\n- Moving to next task\n- Delegating to agents\n\n**Rule applies to:**\n- Exact phrases\n- Paraphrases and synonyms\n- Implications of success\n- ANY communication suggesting completion/correctness\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":43,"timestamp":1792212808669}}
