{"type":"message","id":"38518291","parentId":"8f62a44f","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:49:43.913Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_e73d03712f8a47e5ba7d8ad0b2b9f8b5|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad53ef3caf48191985dbd331d441761","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"set -e; /usr/bin/python3 /Users/alex/.local/state/herdr/orchestrations/dependency-followups-20261015/python314-incident/assert-runtime.py; /opt/homebrew/bin/python3.14 /Users/alex/.claude/skills/routing-workspace-agents/scripts/route.py --complexity normal --fallback-index 0 < /Users/alex/.local/state/herdr/orchestrations/security-remediation-wPB-20261018/quota.json > /Users/alex/.local/state/herdr/orchestrations/security-remediation-wPB-20261018/cor2145.route.json; /opt/homebrew/bin/python3.14 /Users/alex/.claude/skills/routing-workspace-agents/scripts/route.py --complexity high --fallback-index 1 < /Users/alex/.local/state/herdr/orchestrations/security-remediation-wPB-20261018/quota.json > /Users/alex/.local/state/herdr/orchestrations/security-remediation-wPB-20261018/cor2164.route.json; git fetch origin main; gh api repos/entireio/entire-brain/git/ref/heads/main --jq .object.sha; git rev-parse origin/main; realpath /Users/alex/workspace/entire-brain; git -C /Users/alex/workspace/entire-brain rev-parse --show-toplevel","timeout":30}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_495fcf3d61fa4bdba5330f77779993ab|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad53ef7c14c8191ba2bad726b5da714","name":"mcp","arguments":{"tool":"linear_list_comments","args":{"issueId":"COR-2145","limit":5,"orderBy":"updatedAt"}}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_6471a13707174980a83d3a4a2454ac75|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad53ef7c14c8191b348ac069cacc16d","name":"mcp","arguments":{"tool":"linear_list_comments","args":{"issueId":"COR-2164","limit":5,"orderBy":"updatedAt"}}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","usage":{"input":3701,"output":399,"cacheRead":196224,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":200324,"cost":{"input":0.007402,"output":0.0039900000000000005,"cacheRead":0.0196224,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0310144}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792360177750,"responseId":"resp_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad53ef26cf88191aa5aba685c48c0f0","rawStopReason":"completed","durationMs":6162,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}}
{"type":"message","id":"47ca7d74","parentId":"38518291","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:49:45.387Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_e73d03712f8a47e5ba7d8ad0b2b9f8b5|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad53ef3caf48191985dbd331d441761","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"runtime_guard\": \"PASS\", \"python\": \"3.14.8\", \"executable\": \"/opt/homebrew/bin/python3.14\", \"sha256\": \"1b5cb11d163e5ba34e2a05fc533c0ed89574d4425f9749a9d89405f651980e0d\", \"global_writes\": false}\nFrom entire://aws-ap-southeast-2.entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain\n * branch              main       -> FETCH_HEAD\n0f23cbc2cf12ec7d51229c3f1a82072e773989e3\n0f23cbc2cf12ec7d51229c3f1a82072e773989e3\n/Users/alex/workspace/entire-brain\n/Users/alex/workspace/entire-brain\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":1344,"timestamp":1792360185387}}
{"type":"message","id":"d821e90c","parentId":"47ca7d74","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:49:45.387Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_495fcf3d61fa4bdba5330f77779993ab|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad53ef7c14c8191ba2bad726b5da714","toolName":"mcp","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"fbdc6686-fef5-4b1c-89a0-e4c1a57f8e79\",\"body\":\"## Assessment: not exploitable as configured. Recommend closing — but it surfaced a bigger gap.\\n\\n**The advisory.** fast-xml-parser 5.9.3 is affected by [CVE-2026-73569](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/cve-2026-73569) (GHSA-8r6m-32jq-jx6q), fixed in **5.10.1**. Repeated DOCTYPE declarations reset entity-expansion limits, so a crafted document can exhaust CPU/memory and kill the process. CWE-776. GitHub scores it 8.7 High (CVSS 4.0); SUSE 7.5.\\n\\n**Where it sits.** Not a direct dependency. The chain is:\\n\\n```\\nactions/setup-go → @actions/cache → @azure/storage-blob → @azure/core-xml → fast-xml-parser\\n```\\n\\n**Is it reachable?** Yes. `setup-go`'s `cache` input defaults to `true`, and none of our 16 invocations disables it, so `@actions/cache` runs on every job.\\n\\n**Is it exploitable?** No. `@azure/core-xml` parses **Azure Blob Storage REST responses from GitHub's own Actions cache service**. That XML is not repository content, not PR-author controlled, and not reachable by a contributor. Exploiting it requires either compromising GitHub's cache backend or MITM-ing TLS from the runner — both strictly worse than the DoS they would buy. Impact if it happened: an ephemeral runner hangs or dies. No secret disclosure, no artifact tampering, no write path into a release.\\n\\n**Version drift.** `@azure/core-xml` requires `^5.5.9`, so a fresh resolution already lands on 5.10.1+. The 5.9.3 observation was a point-in-time snapshot of setup-go's committed bundle, not a floor we are held to.\\n\\n### The finding worth keeping: we pin nothing\\n\\nChecking this turned up something larger than the CVE. **No GitHub Action in this repo is SHA-pinned** — every one floats on a mutable tag:\\n\\n| Action | Uses | Pin |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `actions/setup-go` | 16 | `@v7` |\\n| `actions/checkout` | 16 + 4 | `@v6.0.2`, `@v6` |\\n| `actions/upload-artifact` | 10 | `@v7` |\\n| `actions/setup-python` | 7 | `@v7` |\\n| `actions/download-artifact` | 5 + 1 | `@v6`, `@v4` |\\n| `actions/setup-node` | 1 | `@v4` |\\n\\nThree consequences: we cannot state which bundle we actually ran; any dependency assessment (including this one) is true only until the tag moves; and a compromised tag push executes arbitrary code in a job holding our secrets. That is the real supply-chain exposure here, and unlike the CVE it is actionable.\\n\\n**Recommended disposition:** close this as assessed — no action needed for CVE-2026-73569 — and open a separate issue to SHA-pin all actions with Dependabot keeping them current. Happy to do that pinning change on request.\\n\",\"attachments\":[],\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T13:45:15.052Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-18T13:45:14.880Z\",\"parentId\":null,\"resolvedAt\":null,\"quotedText\":null,\"author\":{\"id\":\"383d093a-5c76-4a6c-9c2b-660b61ca3f3d\",\"name\":\"Suhaan Thayyil\"},\"onBehalfOf\":null},{\"id\":\"ee015d94-8872-4627-87ab-83298e09e527\",\"body\":\"## Deeper assessment — 2026-10-17 (investigation only)\\n\\nReviewed immutable current main `c8624c8826e4d2632510b46041a54694a0504650`. Vulnerable code remains present; this issue is not resolved.\\n\\n* `setup-go@v7` still resolves to `b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e`, with parser5.9.3. Official latest action release is still v7.0.0; no fixed v7 bundle was verified. Shipped bundle Git blob hash independently matches the official API object.\\n* The advisory is a **CPU/memory denial-of-service** flaw, not demonstrated secret extraction/RCE. Authoritative fix [4e546e0](https://github.com/NaturalIntelligence/fast-xml-parser/commit/4e546e03987662de5495d050b5fba26bea65383f) rejects a second DOCTYPE and adds regression coverage.\\n* The relevant XML is an SDK **service/error response**, not repository files or cache archive bytes. Static source trace: cache SDK download/upload clients → storage-blob Pipeline deserializationOptions.parseXML → core-client non-stream XML Content-Type response parsing → core-xml XMLValidator then entity-enabled XMLParser. Exact storage-blob12.32.0/core-client1.10.2 archive SHA512s match the action lock. Successful blob downloads are streamed; HEAD has no normal body. Backend/download selection conditions the executed route.\\n* XML prevalidation is not established as mitigation: parser5.9.3 validator skips each DOCTYPE without a document-wide duplicate guard. No payload was executed.\\n* Cache defaults true, including inspected setup steps in the publishing nightly job. No route was found by which a PR contributor supplies arbitrary XML service replies. That attacker-control edge remains unproven; do not call it unreachable or security-cleared. Runner/proxy/endpoint/service trust is material.\\n\\n**Recommendation:** retain upstream bundled-dependency remediation. If immediate containment is wanted, separately review `cache:false`: source guards both restore and post-save, while preserving Go1.27.2. This bypasses the observed cache branch, costs cache performance and does not remove the vulnerable bundle. Prefer an official patched bundle when available; do not vendor-edit it. v6.5.0 uses parser5.8.0 (outside this GHSA), but rollback compatibility and overall safety were not established, so no automatic downgrade recommendation.\\n\\nNo code/dependency/CI/admin changes, installs, builds or exploit execution. Research handoff only; remediation awaits a decision/upstream release.\\n\\nSources: [advisory](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-8r6m-32jq-jx6q), [action metadata](https://github.com/actions/setup-go/blob/b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e/action.yml), [cache guards](https://github.com/actions/setup-go/blob/b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e/src/cache-save.ts), [v7 release](https://github.com/actions/setup-go/releases/tag/v7.0.0).\",\"attachments\":[],\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-17T04:53:26.567Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-17T04:53:26.542Z\",\"parentId\":null,\"resolvedAt\":null,\"quotedText\":null,\"author\":{\"id\":\"45a00cf6-3a37-45ab-a508-d9da7f9d514c\",\"name\":\"Alex Ong\"},\"onBehalfOf\":null}],\"hasNextPage\":false}"}],"details":{"mode":"call","mcpResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"fbdc6686-fef5-4b1c-89a0-e4c1a57f8e79\",\"body\":\"## Assessment: not exploitable as configured. Recommend closing — but it surfaced a bigger gap.\\n\\n**The advisory.** fast-xml-parser 5.9.3 is affected by [CVE-2026-73569](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/cve-2026-73569) (GHSA-8r6m-32jq-jx6q), fixed in **5.10.1**. Repeated DOCTYPE declarations reset entity-expansion limits, so a crafted document can exhaust CPU/memory and kill the process. CWE-776. GitHub scores it 8.7 High (CVSS 4.0); SUSE 7.5.\\n\\n**Where it sits.** Not a direct dependency. The chain is:\\n\\n```\\nactions/setup-go → @actions/cache → @azure/storage-blob → @azure/core-xml → fast-xml-parser\\n```\\n\\n**Is it reachable?** Yes. `setup-go`'s `cache` input defaults to `true`, and none of our 16 invocations disables it, so `@actions/cache` runs on every job.\\n\\n**Is it exploitable?** No. `@azure/core-xml` parses **Azure Blob Storage REST responses from GitHub's own Actions cache service**. That XML is not repository content, not PR-author controlled, and not reachable by a contributor. Exploiting it requires either compromising GitHub's cache backend or MITM-ing TLS from the runner — both strictly worse than the DoS they would buy. Impact if it happened: an ephemeral runner hangs or dies. No secret disclosure, no artifact tampering, no write path into a release.\\n\\n**Version drift.** `@azure/core-xml` requires `^5.5.9`, so a fresh resolution already lands on 5.10.1+. The 5.9.3 observation was a point-in-time snapshot of setup-go's committed bundle, not a floor we are held to.\\n\\n### The finding worth keeping: we pin nothing\\n\\nChecking this turned up something larger than the CVE. **No GitHub Action in this repo is SHA-pinned** — every one floats on a mutable tag:\\n\\n| Action | Uses | Pin |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `actions/setup-go` | 16 | `@v7` |\\n| `actions/checkout` | 16 + 4 | `@v6.0.2`, `@v6` |\\n| `actions/upload-artifact` | 10 | `@v7` |\\n| `actions/setup-python` | 7 | `@v7` |\\n| `actions/download-artifact` | 5 + 1 | `@v6`, `@v4` |\\n| `actions/setup-node` | 1 | `@v4` |\\n\\nThree consequences: we cannot state which bundle we actually ran; any dependency assessment (including this one) is true only until the tag moves; and a compromised tag push executes arbitrary code in a job holding our secrets. That is the real supply-chain exposure here, and unlike the CVE it is actionable.\\n\\n**Recommended disposition:** close this as assessed — no action needed for CVE-2026-73569 — and open a separate issue to SHA-pin all actions with Dependabot keeping them current. Happy to do that pinning change on request.\\n\",\"attachments\":[],\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T13:45:15.052Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-18T13:45:14.880Z\",\"parentId\":null,\"resolvedAt\":null,\"quotedText\":null,\"author\":{\"id\":\"383d093a-5c76-4a6c-9c2b-660b61ca3f3d\",\"name\":\"Suhaan Thayyil\"},\"onBehalfOf\":null},{\"id\":\"ee015d94-8872-4627-87ab-83298e09e527\",\"body\":\"## Deeper assessment — 2026-10-17 (investigation only)\\n\\nReviewed immutable current main `c8624c8826e4d2632510b46041a54694a0504650`. Vulnerable code remains present; this issue is not resolved.\\n\\n* `setup-go@v7` still resolves to `b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e`, with parser5.9.3. Official latest action release is still v7.0.0; no fixed v7 bundle was verified. Shipped bundle Git blob hash independently matches the official API object.\\n* The advisory is a **CPU/memory denial-of-service** flaw, not demonstrated secret extraction/RCE. Authoritative fix [4e546e0](https://github.com/NaturalIntelligence/fast-xml-parser/commit/4e546e03987662de5495d050b5fba26bea65383f) rejects a second DOCTYPE and adds regression coverage.\\n* The relevant XML is an SDK **service/error response**, not repository files or cache archive bytes. Static source trace: cache SDK download/upload clients → storage-blob Pipeline deserializationOptions.parseXML → core-client non-stream XML Content-Type response parsing → core-xml XMLValidator then entity-enabled XMLParser. Exact storage-blob12.32.0/core-client1.10.2 archive SHA512s match the action lock. Successful blob downloads are streamed; HEAD has no normal body. Backend/download selection conditions the executed route.\\n* XML prevalidation is not established as mitigation: parser5.9.3 validator skips each DOCTYPE without a document-wide duplicate guard. No payload was executed.\\n* Cache defaults true, including inspected setup steps in the publishing nightly job. No route was found by which a PR contributor supplies arbitrary XML service replies. That attacker-control edge remains unproven; do not call it unreachable or security-cleared. Runner/proxy/endpoint/service trust is material.\\n\\n**Recommendation:** retain upstream bundled-dependency remediation. If immediate containment is wanted, separately review `cache:false`: source guards both restore and post-save, while preserving Go1.27.2. This bypasses the observed cache branch, costs cache performance and does not remove the vulnerable bundle. Prefer an official patched bundle when available; do not vendor-edit it. v6.5.0 uses parser5.8.0 (outside this GHSA), but rollback compatibility and overall safety were not established, so no automatic downgrade recommendation.\\n\\nNo code/dependency/CI/admin changes, installs, builds or exploit execution. Research handoff only; remediation awaits a decision/upstream release.\\n\\nSources: [advisory](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-8r6m-32jq-jx6q), [action metadata](https://github.com/actions/setup-go/blob/b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e/action.yml), [cache guards](https://github.com/actions/setup-go/blob/b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e/src/cache-save.ts), [v7 release](https://github.com/actions/setup-go/releases/tag/v7.0.0).\",\"attachments\":[],\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-17T04:53:26.567Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-17T04:53:26.542Z\",\"parentId\":null,\"resolvedAt\":null,\"quotedText\":null,\"author\":{\"id\":\"45a00cf6-3a37-45ab-a508-d9da7f9d514c\",\"name\":\"Alex Ong\"},\"onBehalfOf\":null}],\"hasNextPage\":false}"}]},"server":"linear","tool":"list_comments"},"isError":false,"durationMs":1473,"timestamp":1792360185387}}
{"type":"message","id":"04516cb7","parentId":"d821e90c","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:49:45.387Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_6471a13707174980a83d3a4a2454ac75|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad53ef7c14c8191b348ac069cacc16d","toolName":"mcp","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"cbc63fb9-9078-4fea-b61c-fd516507a960\",\"body\":\"## Assessment: real criticals, zero exposure. Recommend sequencing behind COR-2154 rather than patching.\\n\\n**What it actually is.** \\\"Benchmark Git tooling\\\" resolves to **`simple-git`**, reached from the Stage 1b embed server. `npm audit --package-lock-only` on `scripts/bench`:\\n\\n| Package | Severity | Advisory |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `@simple-git/argv-parser` | **critical** | `VISUAL` editor env var omitted from unsafe-editor detection |\\n| `simple-git` | **critical** | unsafe-operation guard does not block trailer command configuration |\\n| `node-llama-cpp` | high | — |\\n\\nTotals: 2 critical, 1 high, 0 moderate/low.\\n\\n**The chain.** `node-llama-cpp` → `simple-git` → `@simple-git/argv-parser`. `node-llama-cpp` is the *only* reason any of this is present; `scripts/bench/package.json` declares it as the sole dependency, for `embed-server.mjs`.\\n\\n**Exposure: none that I can find.**\\n\\n- **Never in CI.** No workflow references `scripts/bench`, `embed-server`, or `node-llama-cpp`. Nothing installs this lockfile on a runner.\\n- **Never shipped.** It is Node tooling under `scripts/`; it is not in any release build. The product's embedder is a separate Go `staticEmbedder` in `internal/cli/embed.go`, unrelated to this tree.\\n- **Local-only, operator-run.** The embed server is Stage 1b benchmark tooling we start by hand. Both advisories need attacker-controlled git config or environment in the repository simple-git operates on — i.e. an attacker already on the machine running the benchmark.\\n\\nSo the severity is real upstream and the blast radius here is a developer laptop already under the operator's control.\\n\\n### Why patching is the wrong move\\n\\n**COR-2154 deletes this entire dependency tree.** It replaces the bundled embedder and RRF with in-process BM25 plus taxonomy filters — and `node-llama-cpp` exists solely to serve that embedder. When COR-2154 lands, `scripts/bench`'s only dependency goes, taking `simple-git` and `@simple-git/argv-parser` with it.\\n\\nBumping a transitive dep of a package we are about to remove buys nothing and costs a lockfile churn plus a re-verification of the benchmark harness.\\n\\n**Recommended disposition:** mark this blocked on **COR-2154** (which already has a PR) and re-run `npm audit` afterwards to confirm the tree is gone. If COR-2154 slips or is dropped, revisit — at that point the right fix is upgrading `node-llama-cpp` to a release carrying patched `simple-git`, not pinning the transitive.\\n\",\"attachments\":[],\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T13:45:34.203Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-18T13:45:34.108Z\",\"parentId\":null,\"resolvedAt\":null,\"quotedText\":null,\"author\":{\"id\":\"383d093a-5c76-4a6c-9c2b-660b61ca3f3d\",\"name\":\"Suhaan Thayyil\"},\"onBehalfOf\":null},{\"id\":\"0c5301ec-b969-4393-b4b6-65376f49ccf4\",\"body\":\"## Deeper assessment — 2026-10-17 (investigation only)\\n\\nCurrent immutable main `c8624c8826e4d2632510b46041a54694a0504650` still locks node-llama-cpp3.22.1 → simple-git3.36.0 → scoped @simple-git/argv-parser1.1.1. All three inspected npm archive SHA512s independently match the project lock. This remains inherited, not an introduced update regression; issue is not resolved.\\n\\n**Exposure:** Git can run during npm postinstall AND automatic server-startup source-build fallback. The initial suggestion that ordinary runtime necessarily uses prebuilts was too strong: published getLlama defaults build:auto; postinstall invokes the same default build selection. Embedding request text reaches inference after initialization, not observed Git flags/environment. Inspected cloning/history callers use fixed clone options and explicit messages; no editor-opening call with attacker-controlled VISUAL was established. Installer/operator/CI environment and repo configuration remain trust boundaries; this is not proof of universal non-reachability.\\n\\nCorrect global GitHub advisory endpoints confirm four active findings:\\n\\n* [GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c): CRITICAL parser<2.0.1, fixed2.0.1; untrusted VISUAL plus editor-opening operation and applicable editor/TERM settings. [Actual patch](https://github.com/steveukx/git-js/commit/68874c239f0c7a87f4a68c3d2c4a0d7c75bb27f4) adds VISUAL classification.\\n* [GHSA-858h-whjf-mvg5](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-858h-whjf-mvg5): HIGH simple-git<=3.36.0, fixed4.0.0; unsafe abbreviated push options.\\n* [GHSA-g4wm-2vf7-vfgr](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-g4wm-2vf7-vfgr): HIGH same range/fix; untrusted clone configuration includes/config-resolution environment.\\n* [GHSA-x6jw-m9v5-85vh](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-x6jw-m9v5-85vh): CRITICAL >=3.15.0,<4.0.1; untrusted trailer-command config plus interpret-trailers.\\n\\nNo current benchmark-input path satisfying these conditions was demonstrated. Not an exhaustive all-callers/CI-config audit or exploit proof.\\n\\n**Fix status:** full npm version metadata confirms newest stable simple-git3.x remains3.36.0. Current simple-git4.0.2 includes parser2.0.1. Latest node-llama-cpp3.22.2 STILL requires simple-git^3.36.0, excluding4.x. Therefore merely updating node-llama-cpp to its latest patch does NOT fix this; a compatible published3.x fix route was not found.\\n\\n**Recommendation:** maintained official parent update adopting the corrected Git stack, or maintainer-backed3.x security backport. No blind4.x/parser override. A prebuilt-only mitigation would need to cover BOTH installation and runtime fallback, supported-platform failure behavior, and benchmark provenance/pins; none was implemented or declared compatible.\\n\\nNo project source/pin changes, installs, builds, third-party execution or payloads. Research complete with explicit limits; remediation awaits decision/upstream support.\",\"attachments\":[],\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-17T04:53:28.020Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-17T04:53:27.568Z\",\"parentId\":null,\"resolvedAt\":null,\"quotedText\":null,\"author\":{\"id\":\"45a00cf6-3a37-45ab-a508-d9da7f9d514c\",\"name\":\"Alex Ong\"},\"onBehalfOf\":null}],\"hasNextPage\":false}"}],"details":{"mode":"call","mcpResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"cbc63fb9-9078-4fea-b61c-fd516507a960\",\"body\":\"## Assessment: real criticals, zero exposure. Recommend sequencing behind COR-2154 rather than patching.\\n\\n**What it actually is.** \\\"Benchmark Git tooling\\\" resolves to **`simple-git`**, reached from the Stage 1b embed server. `npm audit --package-lock-only` on `scripts/bench`:\\n\\n| Package | Severity | Advisory |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `@simple-git/argv-parser` | **critical** | `VISUAL` editor env var omitted from unsafe-editor detection |\\n| `simple-git` | **critical** | unsafe-operation guard does not block trailer command configuration |\\n| `node-llama-cpp` | high | — |\\n\\nTotals: 2 critical, 1 high, 0 moderate/low.\\n\\n**The chain.** `node-llama-cpp` → `simple-git` → `@simple-git/argv-parser`. `node-llama-cpp` is the *only* reason any of this is present; `scripts/bench/package.json` declares it as the sole dependency, for `embed-server.mjs`.\\n\\n**Exposure: none that I can find.**\\n\\n- **Never in CI.** No workflow references `scripts/bench`, `embed-server`, or `node-llama-cpp`. Nothing installs this lockfile on a runner.\\n- **Never shipped.** It is Node tooling under `scripts/`; it is not in any release build. The product's embedder is a separate Go `staticEmbedder` in `internal/cli/embed.go`, unrelated to this tree.\\n- **Local-only, operator-run.** The embed server is Stage 1b benchmark tooling we start by hand. Both advisories need attacker-controlled git config or environment in the repository simple-git operates on — i.e. an attacker already on the machine running the benchmark.\\n\\nSo the severity is real upstream and the blast radius here is a developer laptop already under the operator's control.\\n\\n### Why patching is the wrong move\\n\\n**COR-2154 deletes this entire dependency tree.** It replaces the bundled embedder and RRF with in-process BM25 plus taxonomy filters — and `node-llama-cpp` exists solely to serve that embedder. When COR-2154 lands, `scripts/bench`'s only dependency goes, taking `simple-git` and `@simple-git/argv-parser` with it.\\n\\nBumping a transitive dep of a package we are about to remove buys nothing and costs a lockfile churn plus a re-verification of the benchmark harness.\\n\\n**Recommended disposition:** mark this blocked on **COR-2154** (which already has a PR) and re-run `npm audit` afterwards to confirm the tree is gone. If COR-2154 slips or is dropped, revisit — at that point the right fix is upgrading `node-llama-cpp` to a release carrying patched `simple-git`, not pinning the transitive.\\n\",\"attachments\":[],\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T13:45:34.203Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-18T13:45:34.108Z\",\"parentId\":null,\"resolvedAt\":null,\"quotedText\":null,\"author\":{\"id\":\"383d093a-5c76-4a6c-9c2b-660b61ca3f3d\",\"name\":\"Suhaan Thayyil\"},\"onBehalfOf\":null},{\"id\":\"0c5301ec-b969-4393-b4b6-65376f49ccf4\",\"body\":\"## Deeper assessment — 2026-10-17 (investigation only)\\n\\nCurrent immutable main `c8624c8826e4d2632510b46041a54694a0504650` still locks node-llama-cpp3.22.1 → simple-git3.36.0 → scoped @simple-git/argv-parser1.1.1. All three inspected npm archive SHA512s independently match the project lock. This remains inherited, not an introduced update regression; issue is not resolved.\\n\\n**Exposure:** Git can run during npm postinstall AND automatic server-startup source-build fallback. The initial suggestion that ordinary runtime necessarily uses prebuilts was too strong: published getLlama defaults build:auto; postinstall invokes the same default build selection. Embedding request text reaches inference after initialization, not observed Git flags/environment. Inspected cloning/history callers use fixed clone options and explicit messages; no editor-opening call with attacker-controlled VISUAL was established. Installer/operator/CI environment and repo configuration remain trust boundaries; this is not proof of universal non-reachability.\\n\\nCorrect global GitHub advisory endpoints confirm four active findings:\\n\\n* [GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c): CRITICAL parser<2.0.1, fixed2.0.1; untrusted VISUAL plus editor-opening operation and applicable editor/TERM settings. [Actual patch](https://github.com/steveukx/git-js/commit/68874c239f0c7a87f4a68c3d2c4a0d7c75bb27f4) adds VISUAL classification.\\n* [GHSA-858h-whjf-mvg5](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-858h-whjf-mvg5): HIGH simple-git<=3.36.0, fixed4.0.0; unsafe abbreviated push options.\\n* [GHSA-g4wm-2vf7-vfgr](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-g4wm-2vf7-vfgr): HIGH same range/fix; untrusted clone configuration includes/config-resolution environment.\\n* [GHSA-x6jw-m9v5-85vh](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-x6jw-m9v5-85vh): CRITICAL >=3.15.0,<4.0.1; untrusted trailer-command config plus interpret-trailers.\\n\\nNo current benchmark-input path satisfying these conditions was demonstrated. Not an exhaustive all-callers/CI-config audit or exploit proof.\\n\\n**Fix status:** full npm version metadata confirms newest stable simple-git3.x remains3.36.0. Current simple-git4.0.2 includes parser2.0.1. Latest node-llama-cpp3.22.2 STILL requires simple-git^3.36.0, excluding4.x. Therefore merely updating node-llama-cpp to its latest patch does NOT fix this; a compatible published3.x fix route was not found.\\n\\n**Recommendation:** maintained official parent update adopting the corrected Git stack, or maintainer-backed3.x security backport. No blind4.x/parser override. A prebuilt-only mitigation would need to cover BOTH installation and runtime fallback, supported-platform failure behavior, and benchmark provenance/pins; none was implemented or declared compatible.\\n\\nNo project source/pin changes, installs, builds, third-party execution or payloads. Research complete with explicit limits; remediation awaits decision/upstream support.\",\"attachments\":[],\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-17T04:53:28.020Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-17T04:53:27.568Z\",\"parentId\":null,\"resolvedAt\":null,\"quotedText\":null,\"author\":{\"id\":\"45a00cf6-3a37-45ab-a508-d9da7f9d514c\",\"name\":\"Alex Ong\"},\"onBehalfOf\":null}],\"hasNextPage\":false}"}]},"server":"linear","tool":"list_comments"},"isError":false,"durationMs":1329,"timestamp":1792360185387}}
