{"type":"message","id":"0d9c1446","parentId":"39fb16bc","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:50:14.374Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_6066420c42c94763a6e6c36f9f9e4b10|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad53f15b2fc81918598e07aab7a6f8c","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"complexity\": \"high\", \"harness\": \"pi\", \"model\": \"openai-codex/gpt-6-sol\", \"quota\": {\"claude\": {\"healthy\": true, \"sessionRemaining\": 100.0, \"stale\": false, \"weeklyRemaining\": 99.0, \"weeklyResetsAt\": \"2026-10-25T00:59:59.000Z\"}, \"codex\": {\"healthy\": true, \"stale\": false, \"weeklyRemaining\": 99.0, \"weeklyResetsAt\": \"2026-10-24T23:41:50.000Z\"}, \"generatedAt\": \"2026-10-18T21:47:32.396Z\"}, \"reason\": \"Weekly remaining / days until reset from generatedAt (one-hour floor): Claude: 99% / 6.13364 days = 16.1405; Codex: 99% / 6.07937 days = 16.2846. Selected Codex with the higher score.\", \"schema\": \"workspace-agent-route.v1\", \"status\": \"selected\"}\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":110,"timestamp":1792360214374}}
{"type":"message","id":"1be893d5","parentId":"0d9c1446","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:50:14.374Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_e3b62de6dc6e4b6487e50a39dadece5f|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad53f15b2fc81919bbad4fbd06476ec","toolName":"mcp","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"COR-2154\",\"uuid\":\"3541dbcc-98f9-47a1-83cf-2be25a897434\",\"title\":\"Replace facts semantic retrieval (bundled embedder + RRF) with in-process BM25 + taxonomy filters\",\"description\":\"Drops the bundled embedder and RRF fusion for facts retrieval in favour of in-process BM25 plus taxonomy filters.\\n\\n**PR:** <pull-request id=\\\"141565d2-e97c-4b5f-9475-402f0b3009c7\\\" href=\\\"https://linear.app/entirehq/review/replace-facts-semantic-retrieval-bundled-embedder-rrf-with-in-process-b100a0100f20\\\">entireio/entire-brain#365</pull-request> — mergeable, Entire Gates red\\n\\n## This one does not ride the fix stack\\n\\nEvery other M2 PR is a truth-in-output fix with no behavioural risk. This changes **what facts come back**, so it needs its own review and its own measurement, and must not be folded into the integration branch.\\n\\nRequired before landing:\\n\\n* A retrieval quality comparison against the current ranker on a fixed query set, reported with the median beside the mean.\\n* Confirmation that dropping the bundled embedder does not change the install footprint in a way the release notes miss.\\n\\nPrior art on why a ranker change needs its own measurement: `semantic-fts5-trigram-refuted` (trigram looked right, measured 2.2× slower on real queries and 18× build).\",\"projectMilestone\":{\"id\":\"bc05f7ea-a603-4d11-bcdc-d9ef4afb9d74\",\"name\":\"M2 Close the brain blockers\"},\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"},\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2154/replace-facts-semantic-retrieval-bundled-embedder-rrf-with-in-process\",\"gitBranchName\":\"alex/cor-2154-replace-facts-semantic-retrieval-bundled-embedder-rrf-with\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-16T01:09:28.061Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-18T13:45:34.491Z\",\"archivedAt\":null,\"completedAt\":null,\"startedAt\":null,\"canceledAt\":null,\"dueDate\":null,\"slaStartedAt\":null,\"slaMediumRiskAt\":null,\"slaHighRiskAt\":null,\"slaBreachesAt\":null,\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"labels\":[],\"attachments\":[],\"documents\":[],\"stateHistory\":[{\"state\":{\"id\":\"6170bf77-16d7-4d42-9fe6-e0090e8536a0\",\"name\":\"Backlog\",\"type\":\"backlog\"},\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-16T01:09:28.061Z\",\"endedAt\":null}],\"createdBy\":\"Suhaan Thayyil\",\"createdById\":\"383d093a-5c76-4a6c-9c2b-660b61ca3f3d\",\"project\":\"P0 · GA the Local Brain\",\"projectId\":\"91954c69-3fab-4281-84e0-cf4b81d85d75\",\"team\":\"Core\",\"teamId\":\"894690b6-2173-4cbe-abd3-6e7ea5ff5bb9\",\"relations\":{\"blocks\":[],\"blockedBy\":[],\"relatedTo\":[{\"id\":\"COR-2164\",\"title\":\"Assess inherited critical argv-parser advisory in benchmark Git tooling\"},{\"id\":\"COR-2157\",\"title\":\"Cut a stable entire-brain release and re-run the outsider install against it\"}],\"duplicateOf\":null}}"}],"details":{"mode":"call","mcpResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"COR-2154\",\"uuid\":\"3541dbcc-98f9-47a1-83cf-2be25a897434\",\"title\":\"Replace facts semantic retrieval (bundled embedder + RRF) with in-process BM25 + taxonomy filters\",\"description\":\"Drops the bundled embedder and RRF fusion for facts retrieval in favour of in-process BM25 plus taxonomy filters.\\n\\n**PR:** <pull-request id=\\\"141565d2-e97c-4b5f-9475-402f0b3009c7\\\" href=\\\"https://linear.app/entirehq/review/replace-facts-semantic-retrieval-bundled-embedder-rrf-with-in-process-b100a0100f20\\\">entireio/entire-brain#365</pull-request> — mergeable, Entire Gates red\\n\\n## This one does not ride the fix stack\\n\\nEvery other M2 PR is a truth-in-output fix with no behavioural risk. This changes **what facts come back**, so it needs its own review and its own measurement, and must not be folded into the integration branch.\\n\\nRequired before landing:\\n\\n* A retrieval quality comparison against the current ranker on a fixed query set, reported with the median beside the mean.\\n* Confirmation that dropping the bundled embedder does not change the install footprint in a way the release notes miss.\\n\\nPrior art on why a ranker change needs its own measurement: `semantic-fts5-trigram-refuted` (trigram looked right, measured 2.2× slower on real queries and 18× build).\",\"projectMilestone\":{\"id\":\"bc05f7ea-a603-4d11-bcdc-d9ef4afb9d74\",\"name\":\"M2 Close the brain blockers\"},\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"},\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2154/replace-facts-semantic-retrieval-bundled-embedder-rrf-with-in-process\",\"gitBranchName\":\"alex/cor-2154-replace-facts-semantic-retrieval-bundled-embedder-rrf-with\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-16T01:09:28.061Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-18T13:45:34.491Z\",\"archivedAt\":null,\"completedAt\":null,\"startedAt\":null,\"canceledAt\":null,\"dueDate\":null,\"slaStartedAt\":null,\"slaMediumRiskAt\":null,\"slaHighRiskAt\":null,\"slaBreachesAt\":null,\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"labels\":[],\"attachments\":[],\"documents\":[],\"stateHistory\":[{\"state\":{\"id\":\"6170bf77-16d7-4d42-9fe6-e0090e8536a0\",\"name\":\"Backlog\",\"type\":\"backlog\"},\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-16T01:09:28.061Z\",\"endedAt\":null}],\"createdBy\":\"Suhaan Thayyil\",\"createdById\":\"383d093a-5c76-4a6c-9c2b-660b61ca3f3d\",\"project\":\"P0 · GA the Local Brain\",\"projectId\":\"91954c69-3fab-4281-84e0-cf4b81d85d75\",\"team\":\"Core\",\"teamId\":\"894690b6-2173-4cbe-abd3-6e7ea5ff5bb9\",\"relations\":{\"blocks\":[],\"blockedBy\":[],\"relatedTo\":[{\"id\":\"COR-2164\",\"title\":\"Assess inherited critical argv-parser advisory in benchmark Git tooling\"},{\"id\":\"COR-2157\",\"title\":\"Cut a stable entire-brain release and re-run the outsider install against it\"}],\"duplicateOf\":null}}"}]},"server