nt exact shipped bundle, actual workflow trust boundaries and newest human feedback must drive the decision, not green CI or severity labels alone. Any proposed broader action-hardening project is separate scope and requires parent decision.\n\n2. ISSUE / REQUIREMENTS\nRead authoritative COR-2145 and ALL current comments: https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2145 . Team Core; project P0 · GA the Local Brain; milestone Post launch; label Security; assignee Alex. Requirements: resolve current official action refs; verify release/provenance, advisory and actual runtime bundle (not dev-only inventory); assess workflow input/credentials/dataflow; prefer an official compatible patched bundle or evidence-supported mitigation; explicit disposition, not inferred safety from successful CI. Do not mutate Linear.\nNEW relevant comment by Suhaan Thayyil, 2026-10-18T13:45:15Z, id fbdc6686-fef5-4b1c-89a0-e4c1a57f8e79: recommends closing as non-exploitable under trusted Azure cache-service responses and opening separate SHA-pinning work. It also says a fresh dependency resolution picks fixed parser. Treat this as input to verify, not authority to close or broaden scope. Crucial distinction: a checked-in GitHub Action dist bundle does NOT freshly npm-resolve dependencies at job runtime; determine what actually ships and runs. No-action under an explicit threat model is distinct from package fixed or a universal impossibility claim. If the evidence supports closing as assessed, obtain fresh independent evidence review and return the disposition to parent, with no bogus code change.\n\n3. SETTLED CONSTRAINTS / AUTHORITY\nYou may explore, design, implement via the prescribed Pi workflow, run actual repository verification, commit/push normally, create the human-authored PR and confirm automatic Trail linking, and own its sole-writer review steward through readiness. No force push, protection bypass, auto-approval, manual replacement Trail, broad action/version churn, upstream bundle rewriting, Go security-baseline downgrade, global tool/config/auth changes, or benchmark production pin/history/validator changes. Optional-cache disabling is an acceptable CONTAINMENT candidate if independently justified; report its performance tradeoff and bundled-code residue, not a full dependency fix. Do not disable caching solely to satisfy a report when a supported no-action conclusion or official fix is appropriate. Do not unilaterally SHA-pin every action or create a new issue. Surface a genuinely unsettled scope/product choice; otherwise carry the smallest coherent slice to review, not setup-only handoff. Soft PR ceiling400 net/10files; hard800 non-generated. No unsafe exploit/DoS payload execution on this host. Normal trusted repository dependency/test/build operations are authorized for this implementation phase; the prior report's research-only no-install/no-execution scope does not prohibit ordinary verification now.\nPython incident guard remains mandatory: before Python verification run /usr/bin/python3 /Users/alex/.local/state/herdr/orchestrations/dependency-followups-20261015/python314-incident/assert-runtime.py; then genuine /opt/homebrew/bin/python3.14 directly. Never wrappers/shims/symlinks, interpreter replacement or global configuration writes. Don't install optional CI-only exporters unless truly required by the local gate contract.\n\n4. INTERFACES / DEPENDENCIES\nYour checkout is the only one you may write. Separate COR-2164 owner handles benchmark/npm Git risk, not these action workflows. No implementation dependency between the two. Start from verified fresh origin/main (dispatch observed 0f23cbc2cf12ec7d51229c3f1a82072e773989e3), not parent's old manage-dependencies branch. Never borrow unmerged other-lane changes. Preserve benchmark validation/provenance and user edits. Brain is unavailable in parent's recorded preflight; do your normal capability preflight, disclose any scoped fallback and use Graph first for structural questions/impact per AGENTS. Installed-tool failures are blockers, not permission to repair global tools or switch harness.\n\n5. ACCEPTANCE / LIVE OWNERSHIP\nReturn actual implementation/disposition and fresh independent review evidence; complete repo CI-equivalent formatting/static/test/build gates for any code/config PR, current-head personal review gates, canonical Trail URL/state once linked and aggregate receipt. Ignore exact Partial Gates unconditionally. Owner/controller must not implement application code after planning; delegate to configured Pi writer, fresh independent review; when steward starts it is sole writer. Parent's native Herdr watch owns liveness; report an exact next signal/blocker instead of indefinite polling. On PR creation record it on the owning mission via pull_request receipt. Publish verified Trail state with the footer helper; send canonical URL to parent promptly. No cleanup, release/exit, workspace removal or Done until parent supplies successful actual merge-commit required-check receipt and authorizes cleanup. Keep resource/cleanup receipts. Don't mistake controller idle for active child's completion.\n\n6. EVIDENCE VS HYPOTHESES\nRead /Users/alex/.local/state/herdr/orchestrations/security-followups-20261017/assessment.md and this issue's research comment ee015d94-8872-4627-87ab-83298e09e527. Evidence is dated Oct17 and MUST be refreshed, not treated as current requirements. At that snapshot v7=b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e, runtime parser5.9.3; active HIGH GHSA-8r6m-32jq-jx6q affected>=5.9.3,<5.10.1/fixed5.10.1. Parent closed static Azure pipeline XML callback edge and independently checked bundle/hash + SDK lock integrity. XML response body, not streamed archive bytes, was relevant; no contributor-controlled service-XML source was established. No patched v7 then existed. Correct parser fix commit4e546e03987662de5495d050b5fba26bea65383f. Old v6.4/v6.5 versions outside THIS advisory are not blanket safety/rollback compatibility proof. Do not attribute unrelated historical Git fixture CI failure to this flaw. Explicit -R entireio/entire-brain for gh; entire:// origin breaks implicit host inference. Missing-file404 is not auth failure; global advisory API is /advisories/GHSA-..., not guessed repository advisory routes.\n\nStart now: revalidate latest feedback and facts, choose/verify the smallest justified outcome, then execute your complete ownership workflow without awaiting routine parent approval.\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","usage":{"input":3469,"output":6143,"cacheRead":203776,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":4455,"totalTokens":213388,"cost":{"input":0.006938,"output":0.061430000000000005,"cacheRead":0.020377600000000003,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.08874560000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792360215182,"responseId":"resp_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad53f17d6048191b6b156b186e2beb5","rawStopReason":"completed","durationMs":117636,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}}
