{"type":"message","id":"e6a9d829","parentId":"9d8fbd92","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:52:45.358Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_f6b270bfb6f9488589c6e73b34514c66|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad53f90761881918d2f0df6b09e2f27","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/Users/alex/.local/state/herdr/orchestrations/security-remediation-wPB-20261018/cor2164.packet.txt","content":"/skill:owning-workspace-slice\n\nOwn COR-2164 in this isolated entireio/entire-brain worktree through a conclusive verified disposition and, where appropriate, a tested compatible remediation PR reviewed to readiness. Alex explicitly requested workers to handle COR-2145 and COR-2164. This is implementation ownership, not another version/advisory inventory report. Apply owning-workspace-slice plus normal global/project instructions, brainstorming, Pi-native planning/delegated TDD, fresh review and verification. Parent alone mutates Linear lifecycle/dependencies and owns merge/post-merge/cleanup/removal.\n\n1. OUTCOME / WHY\nResolve the inherited benchmark Git dependency exposure without unsafe major overrides, needless churn or damage to benchmark evidence. First verify the new proposed dependency on COR-2154. A substantiated removal/dependency/no-code disposition may be better than patching, but it must be proved from current source and the actual pending change, not asserted from somebody else's summary. Return a concrete outcome/next dependency, not a setup-only handoff.\n\n2. ISSUE / AUTHORITATIVE REQUIREMENTS\nRead COR-2164 and all current comments: https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2164 . Core / P0 · GA the Local Brain / Post launch / Security / Alex. Original acceptance: exact current advisory/package status, actual benchmark/native-install Git operations and trusted/untrusted environment/config flow, compatible official remediation, inherited-vs-introduced distinction. No forced simple-git4 override or unrelated updates.\nNEW Suhaan comment2026-10-18T13:45:34Z id cbc63fb9-9078-4fea-b61c-fd516507a960 says scripts/bench not installed in CI/not shipped/local operator only, and COR-2154 will delete the entire dependency tree; recommends sequencing behind it and auditing after. Treat all these as claims to verify, not code facts or closure authorization. COR-2154 metadata currently says Backlog, relatedTo2164 (not formally blocked), own separate retrieval-ranker change requiring quality measurement (mean AND median on fixed queries) and install-footprint review. Its linked existing change is PR365; actual status/head/removal contents must be verified. Read current issue/branch/diff read-only, do NOT write/own that separate retrieval change or assume changing the product embedder automatically makes historical external embedding baselines obsolete. Do not delete benchmark tooling, archives or pins on that inference. Parent will set any justified formal Linear dependency after your evidence.\n\n3. DECISIONS / AUTHORITY / HARD CONSTRAINTS\nYou own exploration/spec/ephemeral plan, normal scoped dependency installs and actual repo test/build checks, implementation via configured Pi writer, normal commits/pushes, human-authored PR and automatic Trail association, then sole-writer review steward to readiness. Prefer maintained official compatible parent update/backport. If only a cross-major route exists, establish actual API/contract compatibility and focused tests; no blind forced4.x/parser override, unrelated dependency churn, preregistration/schema/checker weakening, production benchmark engine/pin/history/receipt repin or deletion. No force push, policy bypass/auto-approval, manual replacement Trail, unsafe host PoC/code-injection payloads, global tool/config/credential changes or upstream posting. No broader retrieval-ranker work or copying unmerged2154 changes. If removal is genuinely pending and makes a standalone patch wasteful, give parent exact verified dependency/removal acceptance/merge signal and retain workspace; do not quietly park or poll forever. If it does NOT remove this tree, say so and continue to a compatible scoped fix or the concrete compatibility decision needed. No PR merely for research prose if the accepted outcome is no-code; fresh independent evidence review is still required.\nPR soft ceiling400net/10files, hard800non-generated; split before exceeding. Python runtime incident restriction persists: /usr/bin/python3 /Users/alex/.local/state/herdr/orchestrations/dependency-followups-20261015/python314-incident/assert-runtime.py BEFORE verification, then genuine /opt/homebrew/bin/python3.14; no executable wrappers/shims/symlinks or global tool/config writes. Prior report's research-only no-install/no-execution restriction was scoped to that old task, not normal authorized implementation verification; no hostile payloads on this host.\n\n4. INTERFACES / DEPENDENCIES\nOnly write your new checkout. Separate2145 worker owns action/XML disposition; no dependency on that worker. Source is fresh origin/main, observed0f23cbc2cf12ec7d51229c3f1a82072e773989e3, not parent's old branch. The claimed COR-2154 dependency is UNVERIFIED pending your examination; don't invent a block or stack before proof. Do not alter another checkout or borrow unmerged fixes. Brain parent preflight unavailable (unknown command); normal own availability/capability checks and scoped disclosure/Graph structural discovery/impact remain required by AGENTS. Tool/harness infrastructure failure is a blocker, never fallback to another agent CLI/direct implementation.\n\n5. ACCEPTANCE / OWNERSHIP / LIVENESS\nConclusive current code/advisory/compatibility/removal findings, independent evidence review, and for any PR all actual CI-equivalent format/static/test/build gates, inspected complete diff and current-head personal review receipts. Ignore exact Partial Gates. Controller must delegate application implementation after planning using Pi workflow; no direct implementation shortcut. Once a review steward starts, it is the only writer. Human PR first, confirm linked Trail automatically; no manual fill-in. Send canonical Trail URL/state to parent immediately, publish verified local footer state, record PR receipt on owning mission. Parent-native Herdr watch handles liveness. Return aggregate review state and exact next external/decision signal; do not indefinitely poll. Do not clean/remove/exit/markDone until parent actual merge-commit success receipt and cleanup authorization. Keep resource/cleanup receipts. Controller idle may hide an active child: report actual evidence.\n\n6. VERIFIED PRIOR INPUTS / REPLACEABLE HYPOTHESES\nRead parent /Users/alex/.local/state/herdr/orchestrations/security-followups-20261017/assessment.md plus issue research comment0c5301ec-b969-4393-b4b6-65376f49ccf4. These are Oct17 snapshots, not current requirements: scripts/bench lock had node-llama-cpp3.22.1 -> simple-git3.36.0 -> scoped @simple-git/argv-parser1.1.1, inherited, official npm archive SHA512s matched lock. At that time latest node-llama-cpp3.22.2 stillrequiredsimple-git^3.36.0; latest3.xgit3.36.0(nofixed3.x); latestgit4.0.2withparser2.0.1. Active GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c CRITICAL parser<2.0.1 fixed2.0.1 (VISUAL + editor operation), GHSA-858h-whjf-mvg5 HIGHgit<=3.36.0fixed4.0.0(push-abbreviation guard), GHSA-g4wm-2vf7-vfgr HIGHsame range/fix(config include), GHSA-x6jw-m9v5-85vh CRITICALgit>=3.15.0,<4.0.1(trailer command config). Parent independently verified actual advisory metadata, VISUAL patch68874c239f0c7a87f4a68c3d2c4a0d7c75bb27f4, registry complete versions and archive integrity.\nImportant correction: Git can run during postinstall AND runtime getLlama automatic source-build fallback, not just an explicit source-download CLI. No observed HTTP embedding input path to Git env/options or unsafe operation was demonstrated; this is not a universal zero-exposure proof. Check present source, genuine all relevant callers and the newer human claims. Explicit gh -R entireio/entire-brain (entire:// origin); global advisory endpoint /advisories/GHSA-... avoids earlier guessed repo404s. No connection to old macOS Git fixture failure is established.\n\nStart now with current COR-2154/removal verification and issue feedback, settle the smallest justified path, and proceed through your full ownership workflow or return the exact real dependency/decision. No more inventory-only research reports.\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","usage":{"input":6324,"output":1810,"cacheRead":207104,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":215238,"cost":{"input":0.012648,"output":0.0181,"cacheRead":0.0207104,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0514584}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792360333778,"responseId":"resp_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad53f8e894c8191b8809e4314cf2c09","rawStopReason":"completed","durationMs":31579,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}}
