{"type":"message","id":"8365bbeb","parentId":"0440b4e3","timestamp":"2026-10-18T23:38:37.571Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_5b9e4fdd924b43359a2b403caf87963d|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad5587bb2b08191a6136b2d304daaf7","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# COR-2145 progress receipt\n\n## Decision / scope\n- Rejected the unsupported blanket \"trusted service response, no action\" disposition; the independent evidence audit did not establish that boundary.\n- Verified and selected the smallest justified fix: pin all 16 setup-go invocations to official immutable upstream commit `90ad2b35f69faf97585ad74d28fa006d2739b7af`, whose exact checked-in runtime bundles contain the repeated-DOCTYPE rejection and whose package-lock resolves fast-xml-parser 5.10.1. Current official v7 tag remains v7.0.0/vulnerable; no fixed v7 release verified. Keep Go versions and cache enabled; no all-action pinning or bundle rewrite.\n- Commit `0a7266858c6b08e6384d94111395f26baf5dce6b`, five files, 109 insertions/16 deletions (93 net); only setup-go workflows and guard/test. Worktree clean after commit/push.\n\n## Verification\n- Test-first guard showed red on old @v7 and on mutable .yaml while .yml was pinned; six fixtures now pass. Bash syntax, ShellCheck, real workflow guard, diff checks pass.\n- Go suite, vet, cgo/default coverage, phase1 semantic tests, native/cross builds (darwin amd64/arm64, linux amd64/arm64, windows amd64), Node tests, browser tests, Python release/SDK/mutation/benchmark suites pass.\n- One host macOS Python 3.14.8 coverage unit test fails (`test_failed_suite_retains_failure_and_subprocess_coverage`: child.py coverage absent); its test/runner files are unchanged from origin/main. Full same 11-test suite (2 expected skips) passed in Ubuntu 24.04.5 x86_64, Python 3.14.8 from official actions/python-versions release asset SHA256 `fa74abc70a55c10f6631967784878704eef81bbde9b8ec27469534f6ba997cb3`, coverage 7.16.1, Git 2.43.0. Docker image `ubuntu@sha256:68ee22004a9109b44973313b02ff7b1de250f1de0f5ecb628d73f579aaff33ac`; container ran amd64 emulation on local ARM Docker host.\n- Unfiltered actionlint diagnostics are not reported as clean: exact origin/main baseline and current branch both emit 21 custom Depot runner-label warnings and 2 inline ShellCheck SC2035 warnings. Filtered check passed. Exact logs retained at `cor2145-actionlint-default-branch.log` and `cor2145-actionlint-current-branch.log` in this session's subagent artifacts.\n- Four-agent one-shot preflight completed. Two guard findings (.yaml coverage; durable negative test) were fixed in one worker batch; no second review round.\n\n## PR / review aggregate\n- Human-authored PR exists; its automatic Trail association is verified. No manual Trail or Linear mutation.\n- Canonical Trail: https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/317, state open; footer observations published at 2026-10-18T23:12:19.481837Z and 2026-10-18T23:32:50Z. After the aggregate receipt, corrected the existing Trail description to distinguish immutable current-main commit `90ad2b35f69faf97585ad74d28fa006d2739b7af` from still-vulnerable `v7` release tag `b7ad1dad31e06c5925ef5d2fc7ad053ef454303e`, and to state the exact 16 uses. Re-read Trail: status open; head unchanged; Checks, Findings, Up-to-date pass; approvals-only failure. No repository changes or review reruns.\n- Current head `0a7266858c6b08e6384d94111395f26baf5dce6b`: GitHub mergeable MERGEABLE; zero unresolved threads; Bugbot current terminal success; authenticated `trail-review` current_passed; zero open findings. Parent's fresh native review-monitor receipt confirms all checks terminal on this same SHA and healthy GitHub/Entire sources; its earlier summary `source_unavailable` is superseded.\n- Monitors: confidence 80, drift 30, risk 24, security 12, all evaluated on current PR/Trail head; Slop not configured. Aggregate claims: 10 non_actionable_opinion and 1 already_fixed_or_stale, 11 documented no-action dispositions, evidence recorded; 0 actionable and 0 insufficient_evidence. Private rationale retained steward-side only.\n- Latest parent authenticated same-head aggregate: 17/17 required checks succeeded (exact `Partial Gates` ignored); all observed ordinary checks terminal-success, including Windows phase1-semantic, shards 0–7, coverage and the final Windows aggregate. The branch check set recorded 34 entries: 32 successes (including Bugbot) and 2 expected skips (publish and release-evidence). GitHub `MERGEABLE`; 0 unresolved threads, 0 open Trail findings. Entire Checks/Findings/Up-to-date passed; only approval gate remains failed for lack of human approval. The personal conjunction holds; automated work is complete and human handoff. Do not poll approval. Parent owns merge/post-merge monitoring.\n- Review steward completed one wave with no checkout changes. Its bounded tool failures included stale temp-path/guessed endpoint attempts; subsequent authenticated detail and direct checks succeeded. No code edits/commit/push by steward. One non-verification host `python3` wrapper invocation in its JSON-inspection command violated the custom exact-interpreter rule; no code changed. Preserve this process deviation in the parent receipt.\n\n## Resources / cleanup\n- Docker container `cor2145-python-coverage-ci-20261019` (ID `d09820e31fbac11c073af9e561218071e35735f9fd5cb28cb98709bc97f3007c`) and pulled Ubuntu image were removed; no volumes, privileged mode, credential/home/socket mounts, or persistent processes. Idempotent cleanup: `if docker container inspect cor2145-python-coverage-ci-20261019 >/dev/null 2>&1; then docker rm -f cor2145-python-coverage-ci-20261019; fi; if docker image inspect ubuntu:24.04 >/dev/null 2>&1; then docker image rm ubuntu:24.04; fi`.\n- Temporary Python dependency target, Playwright browser download, `webui/node_modules`, test-results, Go test outputs, and preflight diff artifact were removed. No persistent app/service/tunnel.\n- Intentional retained steward-side temporary evidence (no services/processes) in `/tmp/trail317-steward-detail.json`, `/tmp/trail317-steward-gates.json`, `/tmp/trail317-steward-refreshed.json`, `/tmp/trail317-steward-wave1-private-receipt.md`, `/tmp/trail317-upstream-commit.json`, `/tmp/trail317-upstream-setup.js`, and `/tmp/trail317-upstream-cache.js`; rationale remains steward-held and is not relayed. After the owner no longer needs these artifacts, exact idempotent cleanup is `rm -f -- /tmp/trail317-steward-detail.json /tmp/trail317-steward-gates.json /tmp/trail317-steward-refreshed.json /tmp/trail317-steward-wave1-private-receipt.md /tmp/trail317-upstream-commit.json /tmp/trail317-upstream-setup.js /tmp/trail317-upstream-cache.js`. No final workspace cleanup/removal before parent-authorized post-merge success gate.\n- Entire global mission listing during PR receipt routing removed numerous stale global mission pointer files (it reported missing backing records); underlying mission records/workspaces were not touched. No attempt was made to restore stale pointers or repeat global listing. A pull_request receipt was added to the current steward mission.\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":61,"timestamp":1792366717571}}
