{"type":"custom","customType":"web-search-results","data":{"id":"mvehfxdwapvbly","type":"search","timestamp":1792367685572,"queries":[{"query":"site.docs.github.com security hardening GitHub Actions pin actions full length commit SHA Dependabot","answer":"GitHub’s current guidance is:\n\n- **Best protection:** use a **workflow dependency lockfile**. It locks every direct and transitive action/reusable-workflow dependency to a verified commit and source-repository identity; GitHub says this supersedes SHA pinning for repositories that adopt it. ([docs.github.com](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/concepts/security/workflow-dependency-lockfiles?utm_source=openai))\n- **Otherwise:** pin every third-party action to a **full-length commit SHA**—not a mutable tag or branch—and verify the SHA belongs to the intended upstream repository rather than a fork. ([docs.github.com](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/security/secure-use?utm_medium=referral&utm_source=openai))\n- **Enforce it:** repository, organization, and enterprise Actions policies can require full-length SHA pins. Dependencies recorded in a lockfile satisfy that requirement; anything outside the lockfile still needs a full SHA. ([docs.github.com](https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/enabling-features-for-your-repository/managing-github-actions-settings-for-a-repository?trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block&utm_source=openai))\n- **Keep pins current:** configure Dependabot version updates with the `github-actions` ecosystem in `.github/dependabot.yml`; it updates action references in workflows and reusable workflows. ([docs.github.com](https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/how-tos/secure-your-supply-chain/secure-your-dependencies/auto-update-actions?learn=dependency_version_updates&learnProduct=code-security&utm_source=openai))\n\nExample:\n\n```yaml\n- uses: actions/checkout@<40-character-commit-sha> # v4.x.x\n```\n\nKeeping the version comment on the same line helps Dependabot recognize and update the reference. ([docs.github.com](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/security/secure-use?utm_medium=referral&utm_source=openai))","results":[{"title":"Workflow dependency lockfiles - GitHub Docs","url":"https://docs.github.com/en/actions/concepts/security/workflow-dependency-lockfiles","snippet":"source-repository identity; GitHub says this supersedes SHA pinning for repositories that adopt it. (docs.github.com)\n- **Otherwise:** pin every third-party action to a **full-length commit SHA**—not a mutable tag or"},{"title":"Secure use reference - GitHub Docs","url":"https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/security/secure-use?utm_medium=referral","snippet":"le tag or branch—and verify the SHA belongs to the intended upstream repository rather than a fork. (docs.github.com)\n- **Enforce it:** repository, organization, and enterprise Actions policies can require full-length"},{"title":"Managing GitHub Actions settings for a repository - GitHub Docs","url":"https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/enabling-features-for-your-repository/managing-github-actions-settings-for-a-repository?trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block","snippet":"orded in a lockfile satisfy that requirement; anything outside the lockfile still needs a full SHA. (docs.github.com)\n- **Keep pins current:** configure Dependabot version updates with the `github-actions` ecosystem i"}],"error":null,"provider":"openai","providers":["openai"]},{"query":"site:docs.github.com secure use reference pin actions full length commit SHA","answer":"GitHub recommends pinning third-party GitHub Actions to a **full-length commit SHA** rather than a tag or branch. A SHA is immutable, while tags can be moved or deleted; verify that the SHA belongs to the intended action repository rather than a fork. ([docs.github.com](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/security/secure-use?utm_source=openai))\n\n```yaml\n- uses: actions/javascript-action@a824008085750b8e136effc585c3cd6082bd575f\n```\n\nGitHub also supports repository- and organization-level policies that **require actions to be pinned to full-length SHAs**. ([docs.github.com](https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/enabling-features-for-your-repository/managing-github-actions-settings-for-a-repository?trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block&utm_source=openai))\n\nFor stronger dependency protection, GitHub now recommends workflow dependency lockfiles where available: they lock direct and transitive action dependencies and verify repository identity at runtime. ([docs.github.com](https://docs.github.com/en/enterprise-cloud%40latest/actions/concepts/security/workflow-dependency-lockfiles?utm_source=openai))","results":[{"title":"Secure use reference - GitHub Docs","url":"https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/security/secure-use","snippet":"moved or deleted; verify that the SHA belongs to the intended action repository rather than a fork. (docs.github.com)\n\n```yaml\n- uses: actions/javascript-action@a824008085750b8e136effc585c3cd6082bd575f\n```\n\nGitHub als"},{"title":"Managing GitHub Actions settings for a repository - GitHub Docs","url":"https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/enabling-features-for-your-repository/managing-github-actions-settings-for-a-repository?trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block","snippet":"ository- and organization-level policies that **require actions to be pinned to full-length SHAs**. (docs.github.com)\n\nFor stronger dependency protection, GitHub now recommends workflow dependency lockfiles where avai"},{"title":"Workflow dependency lockfiles - GitHub Enterprise Cloud Docs","url":"https://docs.github.com/en/enterprise-cloud%40latest/actions/concepts/security/workflow-dependency-lockfiles","snippet":"ble: they lock direct and transitive action dependencies and verify repository identity at runtime. (docs.github.com)"}],"error":null,"provider":"openai","providers":["openai"]}]},"id":"8a59d62e","parentId":"69f444f4","timestamp":"2026-10-18T23:54:45.572Z"}
{"type":"message","id":"5a1fee40","parentId":"8a59d62e","timestamp":"2026-10-18T23:54:45.573Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_3754470774bc45d7a5e114b0899a4e62|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad55c3a040881918617ec379c55b883","toolName":"web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Providers used:** Query 1: openai; Query 2: openai\n\n## Query: \"site.docs.github.com security hardening GitHub Actions pin actions full length commit SHA Dependabot\"\n\nGitHub’s current guidance is:\n\n- **Best protection:** use a **workflow dependency lockfile**. It locks every direct and transitive action/reusable-workflow dependency to a verified commit and source-repository identity; GitHub says this supersedes SHA pinning for repositories that adopt it. ([docs.github.com](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/concepts/security/workflow-dependency-lockfiles?utm_source=openai))\n- **Otherwise:** pin every third-party action to a **full-length commit SHA**—not a mutable tag or branch—and verify the SHA belongs to the intended upstream repository rather than a fork. ([docs.github.com](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/security/secure-use?utm_medium=referral&utm_source=openai))\n- **Enforce it:** repository, organization, and enterprise Actions policies can require full-length SHA pins. Dependencies recorded in a lockfile satisfy that requirement; anything outside the lockfile still needs a full SHA. ([docs.github.com](https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/enabling-features-for-your-repository/managing-github-actions-settings-for-a-repository?trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block&utm_source=openai))\n- **Keep pins current:** configure Dependabot version updates with the `github-actions` ecosystem in `.github/dependabot.yml`; it updates action references in workflows and reusable workflows. ([docs.github.com](https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/how-tos/secure-your-supply-chain/secure-your-dependencies/auto-update-actions?learn=dependency_version_updates&learnProduct=code-security&utm_source=openai))\n\nExample:\n\n```yaml\n- uses: actions/checkout@<40-character-commit-sha> # v4.x.x\n```\n\nKeeping the version comment on the same line helps Dependabot recognize and update the reference. ([docs.github.com](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/security/secure-use?utm_medium=referral&utm_source=openai))\n\n---\n\n**Sources:**\n1. Workflow dependency lockfiles - GitHub Docs\n   https://docs.github.com/en/actions/concepts/security/workflow-dependency-lockfiles\n\n2. Secure use reference - GitHub Docs\n   https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/security/secure-use?utm_medium=referral\n\n3. Managing GitHub Actions settings for a repository - GitHub Docs\n   https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/enabling-features-for-your-repository/managing-github-actions-settings-for-a-repository?trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block\n\n## Query: \"site:docs.github.com secure use reference pin actions full length commit SHA\"\n\nGitHub recommends pinning third-party GitHub Actions to a **full-length commit SHA** rather than a tag or branch. A SHA is immutable, while tags can be moved or deleted; verify that the SHA belongs to the intended action repository rather than a fork. ([docs.github.com](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/security/secure-use?utm_source=openai))\n\n```yaml\n- uses: actions/javascript-action@a824008085750b8e136effc585c3cd6082bd575f\n```\n\nGitHub also supports repository- and organization-level policies that **require actions to be pinned to full-length SHAs**. ([docs.github.com](https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/enabling-features-for-your-repository/managing-github-actions-settings-for-a-repository?trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block&utm_source=openai))\n\nFor stronger dependency protection, GitHub now recommends workflow dependency lockfiles where available: they lock direct and transitive action dependencies and verify repository identity at runtime. ([docs.github.com](https://docs.github.com/en/enterprise-cloud%40latest/actions/concepts/security/workflow-dependency-lockfiles?utm_source=openai))\n\n---\n\n**Sources:**\n1. Secure use reference - GitHub Docs\n   https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/security/secure-use\n\n2. Managing GitHub Actions settings for a repository - GitHub Docs\n   https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/enabling-features-for-your-repository/managing-github-actions-settings-for-a-repository?trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block\n\n3. Workflow dependency lockfiles - GitHub Enterprise Cloud Docs\n   https://docs.github.com/en/enterprise-cloud%40latest/actions/concepts/security/workflow-dependency-lockfiles\n---\nFull search results are stored as responseId \"mvehfxdwapvbly\". Use get_search_content({ responseId: \"mvehfxdwapvbly\", queryIndex: 0, offset: 0, limit: 30000 }) to retrieve the first bounded page; repeat with queryIndex 1 through 1."}],"details":{"queries":["site.docs.github.com security hardening GitHub Actions pin actions full length commit SHA Dependabot","site:docs.github.com secure use reference pin actions full length commit SHA"],"queryCount":2,"successfulQueries":2,"totalResults":6,"includeContent":false,"fetchId":null,"searchId":"mvehfxdwapvbly","queryProviders":[{"query":"site.docs.github.com security hardening GitHub Actions pin actions full length commit SHA Dependabot","providers":["openai"]},{"query":"site:docs.github.com secure use reference pin actions full length commit SHA","providers":["openai"]}],"truncated":false,"originalChars":4547,"returnedChars":4547,"omittedChars":0},"isError":false,"durationMs":10599,"timestamp":1792367685573}}
