{"type":"message","id":"fda8ae7a","parentId":"13e19efe","timestamp":"2026-10-18T23:55:02.680Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Yes—SHA-pinning GitHub Actions is normal security practice and supported by [GitHub’s guidance](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/security/secure-use).** It prevents a movable tag from silently changing the code your workflow runs. Dependabot can update SHA pins.\n\nThe distinction for 317 is:\n\n- **Pinning a SHA:** standard, sensible hardening.\n- **Pinning an unreleased upstream commit:** a more deliberate compatibility tradeoff.\n- **Adding custom scripts enforcing that exact SHA:** extra machinery, not necessary just to use pins.\n\nSo I’d clarify my earlier answer: **the pinning itself is conventional; the urgency and custom enforcement are the parts worth questioning.**","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad55c539d688191b34ea46039088c63\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","usage":{"input":1911,"output":146,"cacheRead":362368,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":364425,"cost":{"input":0.007644,"output":0.00219,"cacheRead":0.07247360000000001,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.08230760000000001}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1792367696793,"responseId":"resp_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad55c51bb4081919c52c81c04c2a5f1","rawStopReason":"completed","durationMs":5885,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}}
