onclusion":"success"},{"name":"benchmark-real-components","conclusion":"success"},{"name":"build (windows, amd64)","conclusion":"success"},{"name":"build (linux, arm64)","conclusion":"success"},{"name":"benchmark-corpus","conclusion":"success"},{"name":"test (windows-latest) / vet","conclusion":"success"},{"name":"test-cgo (ubuntu-latest)","conclusion":"success"},{"name":"test-cgo (macos-latest)","conclusion":"success"},{"name":"test (ubuntu-latest)","conclusion":"success"},{"name":"build (darwin, amd64)","conclusion":"success"},{"name":"build","conclusion":"success"},{"name":"lint","conclusion":"success"},{"name":"Entire Gates","conclusion":"failure"}]},"expectedRunnerIds":["trail-confidence","trail-drift","trail-risk","trail-security","trail-summary"],"startedRunnerIds":[],"terminalRunners":{},"mainReviewRunnerId":"trail-review","trailActivityObserved":true,"runnerPlanPending":false,"consecutiveGithubFailures":0,"consecutiveEntireFailures":0,"lastGithubSuccessAt":1792369503292,"lastGithubFailureAt":null,"lastGithubError":null,"lastEntireSuccessAt":1792369478682,"lastEntireFailureAt":1792368242721,"lastEntireError":null}},"id":"cfb2533e","parentId":"6548ed1d","timestamp":"2026-10-19T00:25:16.000Z"}
{"type":"message","id":"a1beb49f","parentId":"cfb2533e","timestamp":"2026-10-19T00:25:17.959Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_98141375dd864fb0960854f052284e89|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad56360dc4081918882cd8749312587","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# COR-2145 progress receipt\n\n## Decision / scope\n- Rejected the unsupported blanket \"trusted service response, no action\" disposition; the independent evidence audit did not establish that boundary.\n- Verified and selected the smallest justified fix: pin all 16 setup-go invocations to official immutable upstream commit `90ad2b35f69faf97585ad74d28fa006d2739b7af`, whose exact checked-in runtime bundles contain the repeated-DOCTYPE rejection and whose package-lock resolves fast-xml-parser 5.10.1. Current official v7 tag remains v7.0.0/vulnerable; no fixed v7 release verified. Keep Go versions and cache enabled; no all-action pinning or bundle rewrite.\n- Final commit `158038f1e9475575abe157433b2e7a16f2690ff5`: the final branch diff versus main changes only three workflow files, replacing all 16 setup-go refs with the immutable SHA and retaining provenance comments. No custom enforcement scripts/tests or new CI policy remain. Worktree clean after signed commit/push.\n\n## Verification\n- Earlier test-first evidence for the now-removed guard is historical only and is not claimed as a current test. Final simplification was deletion-only; the steward verified exact diff scope, preserved all 16 refs, provenance comments and other workflow bytes, and ran diff/format/ShellCheck/workflow-lint checks. No guard/fixture test remains in the final branch.\n- Existing Go suite, vet, cgo/default coverage, phase1 semantic tests, native/cross builds (darwin amd64/arm64, linux amd64/arm64, windows amd64), Node tests, browser tests, Python release/SDK/mutation/benchmark suites passed before simplification on unchanged app and workflow inputs; not repeated unnecessarily.\n- One host macOS Python 3.14.8 coverage unit test fails (`test_failed_suite_retains_failure_and_subprocess_coverage`: child.py coverage absent); its test/runner files are unchanged from origin/main. Full same 11-test suite (2 expected skips) passed in Ubuntu 24.04.5 x86_64, Python 3.14.8 from official actions/python-versions release asset SHA256 `fa74abc70a55c10f6631967784878704eef81bbde9b8ec27469534f6ba997cb3`, coverage 7.16.1, Git 2.43.0. Docker image `ubuntu@sha256:68ee22004a9109b44973313b02ff7b1de250f1de0f5ecb628d73f579aaff33ac`; container ran amd64 emulation on local ARM Docker host.\n- Unfiltered actionlint diagnostics are not reported as clean: exact origin/main baseline and current branch both emit 21 custom Depot runner-label warnings and 2 inline ShellCheck SC2035 warnings. Filtered check passed. Exact logs retained at `cor2145-actionlint-default-branch.log` and `cor2145-actionlint-current-branch.log` in this session's subagent artifacts.\n- Four-agent one-shot preflight completed. Two guard findings (.yaml coverage; durable negative test) were fixed in one worker batch; no second review round.\n\n## PR / review aggregate\n- Human-authored PR exists; its automatic Trail association is verified. PR and Trail descriptions now describe only the 16 immutable refs, distinguish the upstream `main` package 7.0.0 commit from the still-vulnerable v7 release tag, and no longer claim a pin guard or fixture tests are present. No manual Trail creation or Linear mutation.\n- Canonical Trail: https://entire.io/gh/entireio/entire-brain/trails/317, state open; local footer observations published at 2026-10-18T23:12:19.481837Z and 2026-10-18T23:32:50Z. Trail description updated for the approved simplification; reread after update confirmed open and new head `158038f1e9475575abe157433b2e7a16f2690ff5`.\n- Current head `158038f1e9475575abe157433b2e7a16f2690ff5`: GitHub `MERGEABLE`; 0 unresolved threads; Bugbot current terminal success; exact `trail-review` runner `evaluated/passed` at this SHA; 0 open findings. Parent's latest native review-monitor receipt confirms healthy GitHub/Entire sources; prior `source_unavailable` summary is superseded.\n- Monitors at `158038f1e9475575abe157433b2e7a16f2690ff5`: confidence 72, drift 15, risk 35, security 5, all evaluated; Slop not configured. Aggregate claims: 6 non_actionable_opinion and 3 already_fixed_or_stale, all 9 documented no-action dispositions with evidence recorded; actionable 0, insufficient-evidence 0. Private rationale retained steward-side only.\n- Latest direct current-head CI snapshot: parent-verified required inventory 18; 15 terminal success, 2 in progress, final Windows aggregate not yet started. Exact `Partial Gates` excluded. Entire Checks pending, Findings/up-to-date passed, Approvals failed for human review. Not merge-ready because CI is still running; exact next signal is the remaining current-head checks terminal and final Windows aggregate successful. Parent owns liveness/merge/post-merge monitoring; no approval polling.\n- Review steward completed one wave with no checkout changes. Its bounded tool failures included stale temp-path/guessed endpoint attempts; subsequent authenticated detail and direct checks succeeded. No code edits/commit/push by steward. One non-verification host `python3` wrapper invocation in its JSON-inspection command violated the custom exact-interpreter rule; no code changed. Preserve this process deviation in the parent receipt.\n\n## Resources / cleanup\n- Docker container `cor2145-python-coverage-ci-20261019` (ID `d09820e31fbac11c073af9e561218071e35735f9fd5cb28cb98709bc97f3007c`) and pulled Ubuntu image were removed; no volumes, privileged mode, credential/home/socket mounts, or persistent processes. Idempotent cleanup: `if docker container inspect cor2145-python-coverage-ci-20261019 >/dev/null 2>&1; then docker rm -f cor2145-python-coverage-ci-20261019; fi; if docker image inspect ubuntu:24.04 >/dev/null 2>&1; then docker image rm ubuntu:24.04; fi`.\n- Temporary Python dependency target, Playwright browser download, `webui/node_modules`, test-results, Go test outputs, and preflight diff artifact were removed. No persistent app/service/tunnel.\n- Intentional retained steward-side temporary evidence (no services/processes) in `/tmp/trail317-steward-detail.json`, `/tmp/trail317-steward-gates.json`, `/tmp/trail317-steward-refreshed.json`, `/tmp/trail317-steward-wave1-private-receipt.md`, `/tmp/trail317-upstream-commit.json`, `/tmp/trail317-upstream-setup.js`, and `/tmp/trail317-upstream-cache.js`; rationale remains steward-held and is not relayed. After the owner no longer needs these artifacts, exact idempotent cleanup is `rm -f -- /tmp/trail317-steward-detail.json /tmp/trail317-steward-gates.json /tmp/trail317-steward-refreshed.json /tmp/trail317-steward-wave1-private-receipt.md /tmp/trail317-upstream-commit.json /tmp/trail317-upstream-setup.js /tmp/trail317-upstream-cache.js`. No final workspace cleanup/removal before parent-authorized post-merge success gate.\n- Entire global mission listing during PR receipt routing removed numerous stale global mission pointer files (it reported missing backing records); underlying mission records/workspaces were not touched. No attempt was made to restore stale pointers or repeat global listing. A pull_request receipt was added to the current steward mission.\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":2878,"timestamp":1792369517959}}
