{"type":"message","id":"7e37a58f","parentId":"6a00a318","timestamp":"2026-10-19T01:51:03.760Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_2e4a5da75195417482e9459ef4999396|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad57784f39881919b862a229254a609","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: where-are-we-at\ndescription: Use when the user asks “where are we at,” “catch me up,” requests an orchestrator status update, or returns to an orchestrator pane after context may have scrolled away or changed.\ncompatibility: Requires a Herdr-managed orchestrator pane plus the Herdr CLI; GitHub and Entire refreshes require their authenticated CLIs when those resources exist.\n---\n\n# Where Are We At\n\nRestore current orchestrator context from live evidence; be concise and read-only.\n\n## Resolve owned work first\n\n1. Confirm `HERDR_ENV=1`; otherwise say that current-orchestrator ownership cannot be resolved and stop. Read `HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID` and `HERDR_PANE_ID`.\n2. Find the ledger under `~/.local/state/herdr/orchestrations/` whose `orchestrator_workspace_id` and `orchestrator_pane_id` exactly match. Its objective and stream rows are authoritative.\n3. A headerless legacy ledger may be used only when its stream IDs are present in current session context or `herdr pane read --current --source recent-unwrapped --lines 400`; label it `matched legacy ledger`. With no matching ledger, reconstruct ownership only from that context and transcript: retain this pane's explicit launch receipts and listed agents, workspaces, issues, PRs, and Trails. Label this `reconstructed from session`.\n4. If multiple candidates remain, list each candidate's objective and identifiers, then ask the user to select one. Never adopt every entry from `herdr agent list`, live workspaces, or another pane.\n\nNever mutate the ledger.\n\n## Refresh before reporting\n\nRefresh each non-`removed` stream:\n\n- Read Herdr state with `herdr agent get <agent>`; use `herdr agent read <agent> --source recent-unwrapped --lines 160` only to explain a recorded blocker or decision.\n- For an open PR, use `gh pr view <number> --json url,state,headRefOid,mergeable,statusCheckRollup`. Refresh it even if no Trail is linked yet.\n- For a recorded Trail, fetch authenticated Trail detail using the wire schema in `interrogating-slopgate` and refresh open findings with `entire trail finding list --freshness any` from its recorded checkout, even if no PR exists. The Trail-detail head field is `head_sha`; `entire trail show --json` is not a head-bound monitor snapshot. If both exist, require the Trail `head_sha` to equal the freshly fetched PR `headRefOid` before presenting Trail findings or monitor aggregates as current. Require each present terminal monitor receipt's evaluated SHA to equal the Trail `head_sha` before presenting its aggregate as current.\n\nReport a source failure as `unknown (<source>)`; never present remembered values as live. On a Trail/PR head mismatch, stale Trail detail, or a present terminal monitor evaluated-SHA mismatch, mark affected findings or monitor aggregates `unknown (Entire)` and identify the exact mismatch in `Watching — no action needed`; do not present stale values as current. Only `.monitors[]` keys are configured; absent keys are `not configured` and non-blocking. Do not read or repeat detailed findings, CI logs, monitor rationale, or per-claim evidence.\n\nDo not prompt or wake agents; answer dialogs; change Linear, PR, Trail, or ledger state; or alter workspaces.\n\n## Report exactly this shape\n\n### What we're doing\n\nState the objective in one or two sentences.\n\n### Where we're up to\n\nOne compact row per owned stream: phase, latest meaningful result, and next expected transition.\n\n### Open PRs and Trails\n\nFor human-facing reports (not artifact creation), verify a Trail match only from an actual link or association; repository or branch similarity is not evidence. When one or more verified matching Trails exist, show only their full clickable canonical Trail URL(s) and Trail state; do not identify or link the matched PR, including its URL, number, or identity. PR-derived evidence such as mergeability, check status, and unresolved-thread counts may remain in prose without identifying or linking the PR. If the Trail association exists but Trail state/detail is unavailable, show the Trail URL as unknown and do not fall back to the PR. A closed, merged, or unknown matching Trail remains primary; report its state or discrepancy rather than switching artifacts. If no matching Trail exists, show the clickable PR URL with `Trail: pending/not linked`. For multiple verified matching Trails, show all their canonical URLs and no PR. Never guess or manually create a Trail. Keep artifact creation, automatic Trail linking, review mechanics, personal gates, post-merge verification, and structured/internal PR evidence unchanged. Pi and Claude bottom status lines remain Trail-only. Omit closed or removed work unless it explains an active dependency or Trail/PR discrepancy.\n\n### Needs you now\n\nInclude only a genuine user decision or intervention. For each item state: the decision; why it is needed now with evidence; concrete options and trade-offs; a recommendation; and what remains blocked if deferred. If the recorded request lacks that context, say it needs clarification rather than inventing it.\n\n### Watching — no action needed\n\nList active agent work and external waits with owner, exact next signal, and last verified state.\n\nFinish with `Freshness: <timestamp>; ownership: <pane-bound ledger|matched legacy ledger|reconstructed from session>; refreshed: <sources>.`\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":65,"timestamp":1792374663760}}
