{"type":"message","id":"9a74eeb5","parentId":"775c1054","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:02:47.072Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_1517e0e286e34b03b336313eb70dbdd9|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad57a43c5b08191b01449e995381baa","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"complexity\": \"high\", \"harness\": \"claude\", \"model\": \"opus\", \"quota\": {\"claude\": {\"healthy\": true, \"sessionRemaining\": 56.00000000000001, \"stale\": false, \"weeklyRemaining\": 92.0, \"weeklyResetsAt\": \"2026-10-25T00:59:59.000Z\"}, \"codex\": {\"healthy\": true, \"stale\": false, \"weeklyRemaining\": 88.0, \"weeklyResetsAt\": \"2026-10-24T23:41:50.000Z\"}, \"generatedAt\": \"2026-10-19T02:01:26.717Z\"}, \"reason\": \"Weekly remaining / days until reset from generatedAt (one-hour floor): Claude: 92% / 5.95732 days = 15.4432; Codex: 88% / 5.90305 days = 14.9076. Selected Claude with the higher score.\", \"schema\": \"workspace-agent-route.v1\", \"status\": \"selected\"}\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":5,"timestamp":1792375367072}}
{"type":"message","id":"5ec9a552","parentId":"9a74eeb5","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:02:47.072Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_b8f72e7bce0d4fc2bbf1793ab87d4459|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad57a45993c8191bdc7c16544a30138","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/skill:owning-workspace-slice Own COR-2164 in this isolated entireio/entire-brain worktree through a conclusive verified disposition and, where appropriate, a tested compatible remediation PR reviewed to readiness. Alex explicitly requested workers to handle COR-2145 and COR-2164. This is implementation ownership, not another version/advisory inventory report. Apply owning-workspace-slice plus normal global/project instructions, brainstorming, Pi-native planning/delegated TDD, fresh review and verification. Parent alone mutates Linear lifecycle/dependencies and owns merge/post-merge/cleanup/removal.\n\n1. OUTCOME / WHY\nResolve the inherited benchmark Git dependency exposure without unsafe major overrides, needless churn or damage to benchmark evidence. First verify the new proposed dependency on COR-2154. A substantiated removal/dependency/no-code disposition may be better than patching, but it must be proved from current source and the actual pending change, not asserted from somebody else's summary. Return a concrete outcome/next dependency, not a setup-only handoff.\n\n2. ISSUE / AUTHORITATIVE REQUIREMENTS\nRead COR-2164 and all current comments: https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2164 . Core / P0 · GA the Local Brain / Post launch / Security / Alex. Original acceptance: exact current advisory/package status, actual benchmark/native-install Git operations and trusted/untrusted environment/config flow, compatible official remediation, inherited-vs-introduced distinction. No forced simple-git4 override or unrelated updates.\nNEW Suhaan comment2026-10-18T13:45:34Z id cbc63fb9-9078-4fea-b61c-fd516507a960 says scripts/bench not installed in CI/not shipped/local operator only, and COR-2154 will delete the entire dependency tree; recommends sequencing behind it and auditing after. Treat all these as claims to verify, not code facts or closure authorization. COR-2154 metadata currently says Backlog, relatedTo2164 (not formally blocked), own separate retrieval-ranker change requiring quality measurement (mean AND median on fixed queries) and install-footprint review. Its linked existing change is PR365; actual status/head/removal contents must be verified. Read current issue/branch/diff read-only, do NOT write/own that separate retrieval change or assume changing the product embedder automatically makes historical external embedding baselines obsolete. Do not delete benchmark tooling, archives or pins on that inference. Parent will set any justified formal Linear dependency after your evidence.\n\n3. DECISIONS / AUTHORITY / HARD CONSTRAINTS\nYou own exploration/spec/ephemeral plan, normal scoped dependency installs and actual repo test/build checks, implementation via configured Pi writer, normal commits/pushes, human-authored PR and automatic Trail association, then sole-writer review steward to readiness. Prefer maintained official compatible parent update/backport. If only a cross-major route exists, establish actual API/contract compatibility and focused tests; no blind forced4.x/parser override, unrelated dependency churn, preregistration/schema/checker weakening, production benchmark engine/pin/history/receipt repin or deletion. No force push, policy bypass/auto-approval, manual replacement Trail, unsafe host PoC/code-injection payloads, global tool/config/credential changes or upstream posting. No broader retrieval-ranker work or copying unmerged2154 changes. If removal is genuinely pending and makes a standalone patch wasteful, give parent exact verified dependency/removal acceptance/merge signal and retain workspace; do not quietly park or poll forever. If it does NOT remove this tree, say so and continue to a compatible scoped fix or the concrete compatibility decision needed. No PR merely for research prose if the accepted outcome is no-code; fresh independent evidence review is still required.\nPR soft ceiling400net/10files, hard800non-generated; split before exceeding. Python runtime incident restriction persists: /usr/bin/python3 /Users/alex/.local/state/herdr/orchestrations/dependency-followups-20261015/python314-incident/assert-runtime.py BEFORE verification, then genuine /opt/homebrew/bin/python3.14; no executable wrappers/shims/symlinks or global tool/config writes. Prior report's research-only no-install/no-execution restriction was scoped to that old task, not normal authorized implementation verification; no hostile payloads on this host.\n\n4. INTERFACES / DEPENDENCIES\nOnly write your new checkout. Separate2145 worker owns action/XML disposition; no dependency on that worker. Source is fresh origin/main, observed0f23cbc2cf12ec7d51229c3f1a82072e773989e3, not parent's old branch. The claimed COR-2154 dependency is UNVERIFIED pending your examination; don't invent a block or stack before proof. Do not alter another checkout or borrow unmerged fixes. Brain parent preflight unavailable (unknown command); normal own availability/capability checks and scoped disclosure/Graph structural discovery/impact remain required by AGENTS. Tool/harness infrastructure failure is a blocker, never fallback to another agent CLI/direct implementation.\n\n5. ACCEPTANCE / OWNERSHIP / LIVENESS\nConclusive current code/advisory/compatibility/removal findings, independent evidence review, and for any PR all actual CI-equivalent format/static/test/build gates, inspected complete diff and current-head personal review receipts. Ignore exact Partial Gates. Controller must delegate application implementation after planning using Pi workflow; no direct implementation shortcut. Once a review steward starts, it is the only writer. Human PR first, confirm linked Trail automatically; no manual fill-in. Send canonical Trail URL/state to parent immediately, publish verified local footer state, record PR receipt on owning mission. Parent-native Herdr watch handles liveness. Return aggregate review state and exact next external/decision signal; do not indefinitely poll. Do not clean/remove/exit/markDone until parent actual merge-commit success receipt and cleanup authorization. Keep resource/cleanup receipts. Controller idle may hide an active child: report actual evidence.\n\n6. VERIFIED PRIOR INPUTS / REPLACEABLE HYPOTHESES\nRead parent /Users/alex/.local/state/herdr/orchestrations/security-followups-20261017/assessment.md plus issue research comment0c5301ec-b969-4393-b4b6-65376f49ccf4. These are Oct17 snapshots, not current requirements: scripts/bench lock had node-llama-cpp3.22.1 -> simple-git3.36.0 -> scoped @simple-git/argv-parser1.1.1, inherited, official npm archive SHA512s matched lock. At that time latest node-llama-cpp3.22.2 stillrequiredsimple-git^3.36.0; latest3.xgit3.36.0(nofixed3.x); latestgit4.0.2withparser2.0.1. Active GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c CRITICAL parser<2.0.1 fixed2.0.1 (VISUAL + editor operation), GHSA-858h-whjf-mvg5 HIGHgit<=3.36.0fixed4.0.0(push-abbreviation guard), GHSA-g4wm-2vf7-vfgr HIGHsame range/fix(config include), GHSA-x6jw-m9v5-85vh CRITICALgit>=3.15.0,<4.0.1(trailer command config). Parent independently verified actual advisory metadata, VISUAL patch68874c239f0c7a87f4a68c3d2c4a0d7c75bb27f4, registry complete versions and archive integrity.\nImportant correction: Git can run during postinstall AND runtime getLlama automatic source-build fallback, not just an explicit source-download CLI. No observed HTTP embedding input path to Git env/options or unsafe operation was demonstrated; this is not a universal zero-exposure proof. Check present source, genuine all relevant callers and the newer human claims. Explicit gh -R entireio/entire-brain (entire:// origin); global advisory endpoint /advisories/GHSA-... avoids earlier guessed repo404s. No connection to old macOS Git fixture failure is established.\n\nStart now with current COR-2154/removal verification and issue feedback, settle the smallest justified path, and proceed through your full ownership workflow or return the exact real dependency/decision. No more inventory-only research reports.\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":5,"timestamp":1792375367072}}
{"type":"message","id":"2fcafb89","parentId":"5ec9a552","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:02:47.073Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_73e5afe16a3949e5a859e36af0784d95|fc_0b16ddefcb78f265016ad57a45993c81919c86d5d77d9f09da","toolName":"mcp","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"9d887425-bef6-43d8-ad9e-3009b070158d\",\"body\":\"Worker dispatch authorized by Alex. Starter packet and routed Pi Sol selection are prepared, including verification of Suhaan's new COR-2154-removal hypothesis before any patching. No formal COR-2154 block has been asserted; linked change is currently open/unmerged.\\n\\nDispatch is temporarily blocked by the parent's Herdr watch-guard infrastructure: combined first-worker creation/start output produced an ambiguous creation receipt. COR-2145 is safely running/watched in its isolated checkout; the guard has no reconciliation API and refuses further workspace creation even with the valid first workspace/watch recorded. No COR-2164 workspace or agent was created; no code was changed for this issue. Requires owner-authorized guard reset/reload before retrying the same launch protocol. No alternate harness or bypass attempted.\",\"attachments\":[],\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T21:58:43.886Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-18T21:58:43.771Z\",\"parentId\":null,\"resolvedAt\":null,\"quotedText\":null,\"author\":{\"id\":\"45a00cf6-3a37-45ab-a508-d9da7f9d514c\",\"name\":\"Alex Ong\"},\"onBehalfOf\":null},{\"id\":\"cbc63fb9-9078-4fea-b61c-fd516507a960\",\"body\":\"## Assessment: real criticals, zero exposure. Recommend sequencing behind COR-2154 rather than patching.\\n\\n**What it actually is.** \\\"Benchmark Git tooling\\\" resolves to **`simple-git`**, reached from the Stage 1b embed server. `npm audit --package-lock-only` on `scripts/bench`:\\n\\n| Package | Severity | Advisory |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `@simple-git/argv-parser` | **critical** | `VISUAL` editor env var omitted from unsafe-editor detection |\\n| `simple-git` | **critical** | unsafe-operation guard does not block trailer command configuration |\\n| `node-llama-cpp` | high | — |\\n\\nTotals: 2 critical, 1 high, 0 moderate/low.\\n\\n**The chain.** `node-llama-cpp` → `simple-git` → `@simple-git/argv-parser`. `node-llama-cpp` is the *only* reason any of this is present; `scripts/bench/package.json` declares it as the sole dependency, for `embed-server.mjs`.\\n\\n**Exposure: none that I can find.**\\n\\n- **Never in CI.** No workflow references `scripts/bench`, `embed-server`, or `node-llama-cpp`. Nothing installs this lockfile on a runner.\\n- **Never shipped.** It is Node tooling under `scripts/`; it is not in any release build. The product's embedder is a separate Go `staticEmbedder` in `internal/cli/embed.go`, unrelated to this tree.\\n- **Local-only, operator-run.** The embed server is Stage 1b benchmark tooling we start by hand. Both advisories need attacker-controlled git config or environment in the repository simple-git operates on — i.e. an attacker already on the machine running the benchmark.\\n\\nSo the severity is real upstream and the blast radius here is a developer laptop already under the operator's control.\\n\\n### Why patching is the wrong move\\n\\n**COR-2154 deletes this entire dependency tree.** It replaces the bundled embedder and RRF with in-process BM25 plus taxonomy filters — and `node-llama-cpp` exists solely to serve that embedder. When COR-2154 lands, `scripts/bench`'s only dependency goes, taking `simple-git` and `@simple-git/argv-parser` with it.\\n\\nBumping a transitive dep of a package we are about to remove buys nothing and costs a lockfile churn plus a re-verification of the benchmark harness.\\n\\n**Recommended disposition:** mark this blocked on **COR-2154** (which already has a PR) and re-run `npm audit` afterwards to confirm the tree is gone. If COR-2154 slips or is dropped, revisit — at that point the right fix is upgrading `node-llama-cpp` to a release carrying patched `simple-git`, not pinning the transitive.\\n\",\"attachments\":[],\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T13:45:34.203Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-18T13:45:34.108Z\",\"parentId\":null,\"resolvedAt\":null,\"quotedText\":null,\"author\":{\"id\":\"383d093a-5c76-4a6c-9c2b-660b61ca3f3d\",\"name\":\"Suhaan Thayyil\"},\"onBehalfOf\":null},{\"id\":\"0c5301ec-b969-4393-b4b6-65376f49ccf4\",\"body\":\"## Deeper assessment — 2026-10-17 (investigation only)\\n\\nCurrent immutable main `c8624c8826e4d2632510b46041a54694a0504650` still locks node-llama-cpp3.22.1 → simple-git3.36.0 → scoped @simple-git/argv-parser1.1.1. All three inspected npm archive SHA512s independently match the project lock. This remains inherited, not an introduced update regression; issue is not resolved.\\n\\n**Exposure:** Git can run during npm postinstall AND automatic server-startup source-build fallback. The initial suggestion that ordinary runtime necessarily uses prebuilts was too strong: published getLlama defaults build:auto; postinstall invokes the same default build selection. Embedding request text reaches inference after initialization, not observed Git flags/environment. Inspected cloning/history callers use fixed clone options and explicit messages; no editor-opening call with attacker-controlled VISUAL was established. Installer/operator/CI environment and repo configuration remain trust boundaries; this is not proof of universal non-reachability.\\n\\nCorrect global GitHub advisory endpoints confirm four active findings:\\n\\n* [GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c): CRITICAL parser<2.0.1, fixed2.0.1; untrusted VISUAL plus editor-opening operation and applicable editor/TERM settings. [Actual patch](https://github.com/steveukx/git-js/commit/68874c239f0c7a87f4a68c3d2c4a0d7c75bb27f4) adds VISUAL classification.\\n* [GHSA-858h-whjf-mvg5](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-858h-whjf-mvg5): HIGH simple-git<=3.36.0, fixed4.0.0; unsafe abbreviated push options.\\n* [GHSA-g4wm-2vf7-vfgr](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-g4wm-2vf7-vfgr): HIGH same range/fix; untrusted clone configuration includes/config-resolution environment.\\n* [GHSA-x6jw-m9v5-85vh](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-x6jw-m9v5-85vh): CRITICAL >=3.15.0,<4.0.1; untrusted trailer-command config plus interpret-trailers.\\n\\nNo current benchmark-input path satisfying these conditions was demonstrated. Not an exhaustive all-callers/CI-config audit or exploit proof.\\n\\n**Fix status:** full npm version metadata confirms newest stable simple-git3.x remains3.36.0. Current simple-git4.0.2 includes parser2.0.1. Latest node-llama-cpp3.22.2 STILL requires simple-git^3.36.0, excluding4.x. Therefore merely updating node-llama-cpp to its latest patch does NOT fix this; a compatible published3.x fix route was not found.\\n\\n**Recommendation:** maintained official parent update adopting the corrected Git stack, or maintainer-backed3.x security backport. No blind4.x/parser override. A prebuilt-only mitigation would need to cover BOTH installation and runtime fallback, supported-platform failure behavior, and benchmark provenance/pins; none was implemented or declared compatible.\\n\\nNo project source/pin changes, installs, builds, third-party execution or payloads. Research complete with explicit limits; remediation awaits decision/upstream support.\",\"attachments\":[],\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-17T04:53:28.020Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-17T04:53:27.568Z\",\"parentId\":null,\"resolvedAt\":null,\"quotedText\":null,\"author\":{\"id\":\"45a00cf6-3a37-45ab-a508-d9da7f9d514c\",\"name\":\"Alex Ong\"},\"onBehalfOf\":null}],\"hasNextPage\":false}"}],"details":{"mode":"call","mcpResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"9d887425-bef6-43d8-ad9e-3009b070158d\",\"body\":\"Worker dispatch authorized by Alex. Starter packet and routed Pi Sol selection are prepared, including verification of Suhaan's new COR-2154-removal hypothesis before any patching. No formal COR-2154 block has been asserted; linked change is currently open/unmerged.\\n\\nDispatch is temporarily blocked by the parent's Herdr watch-guard infrastructure: combined first-worker creation/start output produced an ambiguous creation receipt. COR-2145 is safely running/watched in its isolated checkout; the guard has no reconciliation API and refuses further workspace creation even with the valid first workspace/watch recorded. No COR-2164 workspace or agent was created; no code was changed for this issue. Requires owner-authorized guard reset/reload before retrying the same launch protocol. No alternate harness or bypass attempted.\",\"attachments\":[],\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T21:58:43.886Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-18T21:58:43.771Z\",\"parentId\":null,\"resolvedAt\":null,\"quotedText\":null,\"author\":{\"id\":\"45a00cf6-3a37-45ab-a508-d9da7f9d514c\",\"name\":\"Alex Ong\"},\"onBehalfOf\":null},{\"id\":\"cbc63fb9-9078-4fea-b61c-fd516507a960\",\"body\":\"## Assessment: real criticals, zero exposure. Recommend sequencing behind COR-2154 rather than patching.\\n\\n**What it actually is.** \\\"Benchmark Git tooling\\\" resolves to **`simple-git`**, reached from the Stage 1b embed server. `npm audit --package-lock-only` on `scripts/bench`:\\n\\n| Package | Severity | Advisory |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `@simple-git/argv-parser` | **critical** | `VISUAL` editor env var omitted from unsafe-editor detection |\\n| `simple-git` | **critical** | unsafe-operation guard does not block trailer command configuration |\\n| `node-llama-cpp` | high | — |\\n\\nTotals: 2 critical, 1 high, 0 moderate/low.\\n\\n**The chain.** `node-llama-cpp` → `simple-git` → `@simple-git/argv-parser`. `node-llama-cpp` is the *only* reason any of this is present; `scripts/bench/package.json` declares it as the sole dependency, for `embed-server.mjs`.\\n\\n**Exposure: none that I can find.**\\n\\n- **Never in CI.** No workflow references `scripts/bench`, `embed-server`, or `node-llama-cpp`. Nothing installs this lockfile on a runner.\\n- **Never shipped.** It is Node tooling under `scripts/`; it is not in any release build. The product's embedder is a separate Go `staticEmbedder` in `internal/cli/embed.go`, unrelated to this tree.\\n- **Local-only, operator-run.** The embed server is Stage 1b benchmark tooling we start by hand. Both advisories need attacker-controlled git config or environment in the repository simple-git operates on — i.e. an attacker already on the machine running the benchmark.\\n\\nSo the severity is real upstream and the blast radius here is a developer laptop already under the operator's control.\\n\\n### Why patching is the wrong move\\n\\n**COR-2154 deletes this entire dependency tree.** It replaces the bundled embedder and RRF with in-process BM25 plus taxonomy filters — and `node-llama-cpp` exists solely to serve that embedder. When COR-2154 lands, `scripts/bench`'s only dependency goes, taking `simple-git` and `@simple-git/argv-parser` with it.\\n\\nBumping a transitive dep of a package we are about to remove buys nothing and costs a lockfile churn plus a re-verification of the benchmark harness.\\n\\n**Recommended disposition:** mark this blocked on **COR-2154** (which already has a PR) and re-run `npm audit` afterwards to confirm the tree is gone. If COR-2154 slips or is dropped, revisit — at that point the right fix is upgrading `node-llama-cpp` to a release carrying patched `simple-git`, not pinning the transitive.\\n\",\"attachments\":[],\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T13:45:34.203Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-18T13:45:34.108Z\",\"parentId\":null,\"resolvedAt\":null,\"quotedText\":null,\"author\":{\"id\":\"383d093a-5c76-4a6c-9c2b-660b61ca3f3d\",\"name\":\"Suhaan Thayyil\"},\"onBehalfOf\":null},{\"id\":\"0c5301ec-b969-4393-b4b6-65376f49ccf4\",\"body\":\"## Deeper assessment — 2026-10-17 (investigation only)\\n\\nCurrent immutable main `c8624c8826e4d2632510b46041a54694a0504650` still locks node-llama-cpp3.22.1 → simple-git3.36.0 → scoped @simple-git/argv-parser1.1.1. All three inspected npm archive SHA512s independently match the project lock. This remains inherited, not an introduced update regression; issue is not resolved.\\n\\n**Exposure:** Git can run during npm postinstall AND automatic server-startup source-build fallback. The initial suggestion that ordinary runtime necessarily uses prebuilts was too strong: published getLlama defaults build:auto; postinstall invokes the same default build selection. Embedding request text reaches inference after initialization, not observed Git flags/environment. Inspected cloning/history callers use fixed clone options and explicit messages; no editor-opening call with attacker-controlled VISUAL was established. Installer/operator/CI environment and repo configuration remain trust boundaries; this is not proof of universal non-reachability.\\n\\nCorrect global GitHub advisory endpoints confirm four active findings:\\n\\n* [GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c): CRITICAL parser<2.0.1, fixed2.0.1; untrusted VISUAL plus editor-opening operation and applicable editor/TERM settings. [Actual patch](https://github.com/steveukx/git-js/commit/68874c239f0c7a87f4a68c3d2c4a0d7c75bb27f4) adds VISUAL classification.\\n* [GHSA-858h-whjf-mvg5](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-858h-whjf-mvg5): HIGH simple-git<=3.36.0, fixed4.0.0; unsafe abbreviated push options.\\n* [GHSA-g4wm-2vf7-vfgr](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-g4wm-2vf7-vfgr): HIGH same range/fix; untrusted clone configuration includes/config-resolution environment.\\n* [GHSA-x6jw-m9v5-85vh](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-x6jw-m9v5-85vh): CRITICAL >=3.15.0,<4.0.1; untrusted trailer-command config plus interpret-trailers.\\n\\nNo current benchmark-input path satisfying these conditions was demonstrated. Not an exhaustive all-callers/CI-config audit or exploit proof.\\n\\n**Fix status:** full npm version metadata confirms newest stable simple-git3.x remains3.36.0. Current simple-git4.0.2 includes parser2.0.1. Latest node-llama-cpp3.22.2 STILL requires simple-git^3.36.0, excluding4.x. Therefore merely updating node-llama-cpp to its latest patch does NOT fix this; a compatible published3.x fix route was not found.\\n\\n**Recommendation:** maintained official parent update adopting the corrected Git stack, or maintainer-backed3.x security backport. No blind4.x/parser override. A prebuilt-only mitigation would need to cover BOTH installation and runtime fallback, supported-platform failure behavior, and benchmark provenance/pins; none was implemented or declared compatible.\\n\\nNo project source/pin changes, installs, builds, third-party execution or payloads. Research complete with explicit limits; remediation awaits decision/upstream support.\",\"attachments\":[],\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-17T04:53:28.020Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-17T04:53:27.568Z\",\"parentId\":null,\"resolvedAt\":null,\"quotedText\":null,\"author\":{\"id\":\"45a00cf6-3a37-45ab-a508-d9da7f9d514c\",\"name\":\"Alex Ong\"},\"onBehalfOf\":null}],\"hasNextPage\":false}"}]},"server":"linear","tool":"list_comments"},"isError":false,"durationMs":1212,"timestamp":1792375367073}}
