d versions/advisories, actual benchmark/native-install Git operations, trusted versus untrusted config/environment/input, compatible official remedy and inherited-versus-introduced distinction. No forced simple-git4 override or unrelated dependency updates. Do not mutate Linear.\nSuhaan's comment cbc63fb9-9078-4fea-b61c-fd516507a960 (Oct18) says this tooling is local/operator-only, never installed in CI or shipped, and COR-2154 deletes its entire dependency tree; recommends sequencing behind2154. These are hypotheses to verify, not closure authority. Parent freshly read2164: Backlog, relatedTo2154, no formal blockedBy. Parent refreshed2154: Backlog; its existing linked change remains OPEN/unmerged at dfe713ecda030edf491e5597a9ae1227dea804d7 (PR365, feat/bm25-facts-ranker). The ranker change requires separate quality measurement including mean/median and install-footprint review. Inspect relevant current diff/source READ-ONLY; do not own/write that change, copy its unmerged implementation, or assume removing a product embedder also permits deleting historical external embedding baselines. Parent alone sets any evidence-supported dependency after your report.\n\n3. SETTLED CONSTRAINTS / AUTHORITY\nOwn discovery/design/ephemeral plan, normal scoped dependency installs and actual repo verification, implementation through the prescribed delegated writer workflow, normal non-force commit/push, human-authored PR and automatic Trail linking, then one sole-writer review steward to readiness. In this routed Claude workspace, invoke the applicable enabled Superpowers brainstorming/writing-plans/TDD/subagent-driven-development/fresh-review/verification workflows required by owning-workspace-slice. Controller must not implement application code after planning. Keep normal skill/plugin discovery enabled; a missing workflow is a blocker, not permission for direct edits or another agent CLI.\nPrefer a maintained official compatible parent update/backport. A cross-major route requir