d Graph structural/impact rules, disclose scoped fallbacks, never repair global\n  tools automatically.\n\n  5. ACCEPTANCE / LIVENESS\n  Actual code/advisory/compatibility or removal findings with fresh independent review. For any code PR: normal complete repo CI-equivalent format/static/test/build commands, full diff/size,\n  current-head CI/Bugbot/main review, zero unresolved threads/findings, MERGEABLE and complete present-monitor disposition receipt with zero actionable/insufficient claims. Ignore exactly Partial\n  Gates. Human PR first, verify automatic canonical Trail association; never create a filler Trail. Send canonical URL/state promptly, publish verified local footer state. Once a steward starts it is\n  sole writer; return aggregate receipts, not detailed rationale, to parent. No repeated preflight fanout on an existing PR and no approval polling. Parent native Herdr watch handles liveness; owner\n  idle may hide an active child. Report precise next signal/blocker. No final cleanup/release/removal/Done until parent actual-merge success receipt and explicit cleanup authorization; retain exact\n  owned resource cleanup commands and history.\n\n  6. VERIFIED PRIOR EVIDENCE / REPLACEABLE LEADS\n  Read /Users/alex/.local/state/herdr/orchestrations/security-followups-20261017/assessment.md and2164 research comment0c5301ec-b969-4393-b4b6-65376f49ccf4. These are Oct17 snapshots, NOT current\n  requirements. They established scripts/bench node-llama-cpp3.22.1 -> simple-git3.36.0 -> SCOPED @simple-git/argv-parser1.1.1, inherited; npm tarball SHA512s matched lock. Then-latest\n  node-llama-cpp3.22.2 still requiredsimple-git^3.36.0; no newer3.xgit patch, correctedgit4.0.2 withparser2.0.1. Refresh before choosing anything.\n  Four active advisory leads then: GHSA-v5rq-49vh-5v5c CRITICAL scopedparser<2.0.1/fix2.0.1(VISUAL+editor-opening operation); GHSA-858h-whjf-mvg5 HIGHgit<=3.36.0/fix4.0.0(push abbreviations);\n  GHSA-g4wm-2vf7-vfgr HIGHsame range/fix(config includes); GHSA-x6jw-m9v5-85vh CRITICALgit>=3.15.0,<4.0.1(trailer config). Actual VISUAL patch68874c239f0c7a87f4a68c3d2c4a0d7c75bb27f4. Global\n  authoritative GitHub API /advisories/GHSA-... works; earlier guessed repository security-advisory endpoints returned404, not auth failures.\n  Git can run in postinstall AND getLlama automatic source-build fallback, not just explicit CLI. No observed HTTP embedding-text-to-Git-env/options path was demonstrated; that is not universal safety\n  proof. Explicit gh -R entireio/entire-brain because entire:// origin breaks implicit host inference. No connection to the old macOS Git fixture CI failure is established.\n\n  Start now with present2164/2154 facts, choose the smallest evidence-supported outcome, and carry it through the ownership workflow. Do not repeat stale research, invent a dependency, or overengineer\n  the remedy.\n\n⏺ Skill(owning-workspace-slice)\n  ⎿  Successfully loaded skill\n\n  Called Linear 2 times, ran 6 shell commands\n\n⏺ PR #365's current head doesn't touch scripts/bench at all, so Suhaan's claim that it deletes that tree is false. Next I'll check upstream issue #669 and how node-llama-cpp actually calls simple-git.\n\n  Ran 7 shell commands\n\n⏺ Mapping whether the bench lockfile/manifest is pinned by the confirmatory benchmark — that decides whether any package.json change is even allowed.\n\n  Ran 5 shell commands\n\n⏺ Disposition forming: no code PR. Dispatching a fresh independent reviewer to adversarially check the evidence before I report.\n\n⏺ deep-reasoner(Independent review of COR-2164 disposition)\n  ⎿  Backgrounded agent (↓ to manage · ctrl+o to expand)\n\n⏺ Independent review is still running; waiting for its verdict before finalizing.\n\n  Status so far (step 3 of 4: evidence gathered → disposition drafted → independent review running → report to parent):\n\n  - COR-2154 removes the tree? No. The open PR (head dfe713ec) changes 94 files, none of them under scripts/bench. Its head tree still has the full bench dir and lockfile.\n  - Compatible official fix? None. node-llama-cpp 3.22.2 is the latest, and it still requires simple-git ^3.36.0. simple-git 3.x stops at 3.36.0, which is vulnerable. Only 4.0.2 fixes all four\n    advisories. The upstream issue (withcatai/node-llama-cpp#669) is open, and no maintainer has replied.\n  - Override route: blocked. The confirmatory benchmark pins the sha of scripts/bench/package.json, so editing it would break preregistered verification. simple-git 4 is also a behaviour-breaking major\n    (it filters environment variables and rejects abbreviated options).\n  - Side finding: the repo lockfile already fails its confirmatory pin. Dependabot changed it on Oct 12/16 (4a3eea… → 2b168b…). This is out of scope for this issue, but it will go to the parent.\n\n✻ Waiting for 1 background agent to finish\n\n› Message from @deep-reasoner (ctrl+o to expand)\n\n  Ran 1 shell command\n\n⏺ Agent \"Independent review of COR-2164 disposition\" finished · 3m 10s\n\n  Ran 1 shell command\n\n⏺ Skill(capturing-agent-knowledge)\n  ⎿  Successfully loaded skill\n\n  Ran 4 shell commands\n\n⏺ No safe compatible fix exists today, so there is no code PR and no Trail. COR-2154 does not remove this dependency tree.\n\n  What's left for you (parent):\n  1. Decide whether COR-2164 closes as a bounded no-action item with a re-trigger. Not a \"blockedBy COR-2154\": that change doesn't remove the tree (finding 1).\n  2. Decide whether to dismiss Dependabot alerts #7–#10, which are tied to scripts/bench, giving \"vulnerable code not used\" plus the re-trigger as the reason. I didn't dismiss them because that is a\n     change outside this checkout that I wasn't authorized to make.\n  3. Route finding 4 to whoever owns the confirmatory protocol.\n\n  Findings (checked against fresh origin/main 4d0b0688; a fresh independent reviewer confirmed or corrected each):\n  1. COR-2154 removal claim is false. Its open change (head dfe713ec) touches 94 files, none under scripts/. Its head tree still contains scripts/bench. It does delete internal/cli/embed_ollama.go, so\n     after it merges the bench server has no product consumer, but it is still in the repo.\n  2. No compatible official fix exists. The latest node-llama-cpp is 3.22.2 (Oct 17), and it still needs simple-git ^3.36.0. simple-git 3.x ends at 3.36.0, which is vulnerable. Only 4.0.2 fixes all four\n     advisories, and the argv-parser fix also needs that major version. The upstream issue (withcatai/node-llama-cpp#669) is open, with no maintainer reply and no bump on master. All four advisories\n     are active and unchanged since the Oct 17 snapshot.\n  3. An override is not a valid remedy.\n     - engine-verification-pins.json pins the sha of scripts/bench/package.json and of the lockfile.\n     - The pinned lock itself contains simple-git 3.36.0, so any remedy means deliberately re-pinning or retiring the confirmatory EmbeddingGemma arm. That is a product/protocol choice, not a dependency\n       bump.\n     - simple-git 4.0.0 also changes behaviour: it filters ambient env, rejects abbreviated options, and drops the default export.\n  4. Side finding: the repo lock (2b168b7a…) has not matched the pinned 4a3eea23… since the Oct 12/16 Dependabot bumps, so verify_engines.py already refuses current main. Commit c7da4201 worked around\n     it in tests rather than re-pinning. Dependabot still watches /scripts/bench, so each future bump widens this drift.\n  5. Threat model (bounded, not a claim of universal safety).\n     - The exposure is inherited: the June 12 pinned lock already had simple-git 3.36.0.\n     - Git runs only during node-llama-cpp's source-build fallback (postinstall, or getLlama() with build:\"auto\"). The calls are clone, removeRemote and applyPatch.\n     - Repo and tag come from operator env (NODE_LLAMA_CPP_REPO*) or CLI flags, not fixed values, so the trust boundary is the operator's own environment.\n     - There is no push, trailer config or editor operation. HTTP input only reaches embedding inference. No CI workflow installs this tree.\n  6. Re-trigger: a node-llama-cpp release that allows simple-git ^4, or a decision on the confirmatory re-pin.\n\n  Receipts:\n  - Checkout is clean at 4d0b0688. Nothing was committed or pushed, and no PR or Trail exists.\n  - Brain fact recorded: fact:fe3e7e6bfe301bf2e074cbea.\n  - New KB evidence note agent-knowledge-base/repositories/entire-brain/2026-10-19-cor-2164-bench-simple-git-advisories.md; its frontmatter and search checks passed.\n  - The only thing I created outside the vault is a downloaded tarball in the session scratchpad. Cleanup command: rm -rf\n    /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-alex--herdr-worktrees-entire-brain-alex-cor-2164-benchmark-git-security/122dc32f-b902-4809-b860-e4e1e4ed9f53/scratchpad/nlc\n  - Brain and Graph preflights passed (Brain v0.1.0-nightly.202610180624, Graph v0.4.1-nightly), so nothing fell back to other tools. I checked consumers of scripts/bench paths with text search, since\n    config strings are outside what Graph models. Linear was read but not changed.\n\n  Next: post the no-action disposition with the re-trigger on COR-2164, and decide on dismissing the four alerts.\n\n✻ Cogitated for 6m 46s · done 1:12 pm\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n❯ dismiss the four alerts with that reason\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  Opus 5.5 | [██░░░░░░░░░░░░░░] 150k/1.0M (15%)\n  alex-cor-2164-benchmark-git-security | (+0,-0) | alex/cor-2164-benchmark-git-security\n  ~/.h/w/e/alex-cor-2164-benchmark-git-security | 122dc32f-b902-4809-b860-e4e1e4ed9f53\n  ⏵⏵ auto mode on (shift+tab to cycle) · ← 